<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Jina Embeddings v2 | `jina-embeddings-v2-base-en`, `jina-embeddings-v2-base-zh` | Jina v2 is plain-text input. Jina v3/v4 are different and use the `task` parameter for retrieval tasks. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Style | Bindings | How asymmetric behavior is applied &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">17.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Prefix mode with a missing prefix variable&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b365e355f26b9e2eac9eff4198039b0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Some embedding models are instruction-free, sometimes described as using implicit intent. They are trained to handle query/document matching from the raw text itself and do not require query/document prefixes or provider task parameters. For these models, do not set `EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC=true`; leave it unset or set it to `false`, and do not configure `EMBEDDING_QUERY_PREFIX` or `EMBEDDING_DOCUMENT_PREFIX`. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For these models, do not set `EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC=true`; leave it unset or set it to `false`, and do not configure `EMBEDDING_QUERY_PREFIX` or `EMBEDDING_DOCUMENT_PREFIX`. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use this mode for embedding models that expect task instructions in the input text, such as models whose card documents prefixes like `search_query:`, `search_document:`, `query:`, or `passage:`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b365e355f26b9e2eac9eff4198039b0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC`">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| OpenAI Text Embedding 3 | `text-embedding-3-small`, `text-embedding-3-large` | The OpenAI embeddings API uses text input plus the model name; it does not expose a query/document task parameter. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
