<node id="&quot;ACCIDENTAL RETRIEVAL CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This avoids accidental retrieval changes when prefix variables are present in an environment but the user did not intentionally enable asymmetric embeddings.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RAW TEXT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"They are trained to handle query/document matching from the raw text itself.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAG DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DATA"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Clear the existing LightRAG data for the workspace and re-index the source files.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEXT TASK PREFIX BINDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The mode for embedding models that expect task instructions in the input text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b365e355f26b9e2eac9eff4198039b0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JINA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"EMBEDDING BACKEND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LightRAG passes query/document context to the provider-specific `task` for Jina.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server supports jina as an embedding backend.&lt;SEP&gt;"jina is a supported embedding backend.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OLLAMA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CLIENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Backend that exposes the LightRAG REST API surface.&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG prepends configured text prefixes for Ollama.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server supports ollama as an LLM backend.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server supports ollama as an embedding backend.&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the supported backends that expose the LightRAG REST API surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"ollama is a supported LLM backend.&lt;SEP&gt;"ollama is a supported embedding backend.&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG dynamically installs `ollama` as an LLM provider package.&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG dynamically installs `ollama` as an LLM provider package."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ollama client is supported and uses `{ROLE}_LLM_BINDING_HOST` for communication.&lt;SEP&gt;"Ollama client supports passing through `{ROLE}_LLM_BINDING_HOST`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd74b84904f076da611686fd7750bdea</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREFIX MODE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"MODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A mode used with `openai`, `azure_openai`, or `ollama` that requires both prefix variables to be configured."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b365e355f26b9e2eac9eff4198039b0c</data>
</node>
