</node>
<node id="&quot;UV.LOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Avoid editing `uv.lock` by hand as uv will overwrite manual edits.&lt;SEP&gt;"Commit `uv.lock` alongside `pyproject.toml` for consistency.&lt;SEP&gt;"Committing `uv.lock` ensures that collaborators and CI jobs share the same dependency graph.&lt;SEP&gt;"Editing `uv.lock` by hand is an action to be avoided, as uv will overwrite manual edits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regenerate the lock file after changing dependency constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;"The text advises to keep `uv.lock` in sync with the project and commit it whenever it changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text indicates that `uv.lock` should be committed whenever it changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text reminds to keep `uv.lock` in sync with the project and commit it whenever it changes, as it only changes when a command is run that tells it to."&lt;SEP&gt;"`uv.lock` and `requirements.txt` can coexist, but it is recommended to rely on `uv.lock` alone.&lt;SEP&gt;"`uv.lock` is a file that captures the exact version of every dependency, including transitive ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"`uv.lock` is a file that is read only during dependency resolution and is about 1 MB in size.&lt;SEP&gt;"`uv.lock` is a lock file used in the uv project to manage dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;"uv.lock is a file that is used for caching UV package downloads.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ea9b2e06bd3e26acee17a3b67d9a834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d43eaedfdb0bd6c70bdaa2381e96ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-100681c982044751140d02d193a76196</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAKE ENV-BASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An existing `VLLM_EMBED_DEVICE` / `VLLM_RERANK_DEVICE` value is preserved when running `make env-base`."&lt;SEP&gt;"Running `make env-base` preserves existing environment variables to avoid overwriting them with GPU auto-detection results.&lt;SEP&gt;"When rerunning `make env-base`, existing configurations are preserved.&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'make env-base' command is used to set up the base environment for remote models and local servers.&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'make env-base' is used for setting up the environment base."&lt;SEP&gt;"`make env-base` is the normal starting point because it creates the initial `.env`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8fbdf17e3767d2cc6b62e0485bfedf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12c55028ed60ac15f2cc10cf11febe66</data>
</node>
