<node id="&quot;MAKE ENV-SECURITY-CHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Running `make env-security-check` is an option to audit the `.env` file for potential security risks.&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'make env-security-check' command is used to perform a security check on the environment before exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'make env-security-check' is used to check for security before the environment is exposed.&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'make env-security-check' is used to check security before exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The command make env-security-check is used to audit the current .env for missing authentication, unsafe whitelist settings, weak JWT secrets, and other setup-level security risks without rewriting any files.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `make env-security-check` command is used to audit the `.env` file for security risks, protecting sensitive information.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ea9b2e06bd3e26acee17a3b67d9a834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</node>
