<node id="&quot;MAX_ASYNC_LLM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"VARIABLE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Base maximum LLM concurrency. A role inherits it when `{ROLE}_MAX_ASYNC_LLM` is not set. `MAX_ASYNC` is still accepted as a deprecated alias."&lt;SEP&gt;"Controls concurrent LLM calls, including extraction, merging, query keyword generation, and final answer generation (deprecated alias: `MAX_ASYNC`)."&lt;SEP&gt;"MAX_ASYNC_LLM is a configuration in LLM Configuration section."&lt;SEP&gt;"MAX_ASYNC_LLM is set to a fallback value when unset."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parameter that controls concurrent LLM calls, including extraction, merging, query keyword generation, and final answer generation. It is deprecated and has an alias `MAX_ASYNC`.&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAX_ASYNC_LLM variable sets the maximum async operations (deprecated alias: MAX_ASYNC).&lt;SEP&gt;"The `MAX_ASYNC_LLM` environment variable sets the maximum concurrent requests to the LLM (MAX_ASYNC is still accepted as a deprecated alias)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `MAX_ASYNC_LLM` environment variable sets the maximum number of concurrent LLM requests, which can be adjusted for performance.&lt;SEP&gt;"MAX_ASYNC_LLM is set to '4' for LLM configuration settings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'MAX_ASYNC_LLM' environment variable defines the maximum number of concurrent requests to the LLM.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082eb07a755d44999510e8f240806102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea9b2e06bd3e26acee17a3b67d9a834</data>
</node>
