<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Configurable index types for Milvus vector storage are set through environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are set to configure the local reranker. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are used to configure the storage implementation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are used to tune system parameters and control system behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG can be configured using environment variables in the .env file.&lt;SEP&gt;"Parameters are passed in via `.env` (or environment variables) and read once at `LightRAG` construction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions environment variables as a way to configure the chunker parameters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server loads environment variables from `.env` into the system environment variables at startup, prioritizing system environment variables over .env settings.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server recommends using environment variables for configuration, providing flexibility and the ability to change settings without server restarts.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server uses environment variables for configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;"The endpoint and key values can be used to set environment variables in the `.env` file.&lt;SEP&gt;"It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server.&lt;SEP&gt;"Storage implementation is specified through environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server configuration relies on environment variables for its setup.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is configured using environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `.env` file contains environment variables for each instance.&lt;SEP&gt;"The environment variables are loaded from the `.env` file."&lt;SEP&gt;"You can use these values to set the environment variables in the `.env` file.&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are optional when using vector_db_storage_cls_kwargs, serving as fallback values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are used as fallback values for any parameters not provided in kwargs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables are used for configuration resolution after parameters passed via vector_db_storage_cls_kwargs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment variables can be mixed with kwargs for configuration purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Verify the corresponding environment variables for the external service call.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `.env` file contains environment variables that are necessary to run the GraphRAG pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea9b2e06bd3e26acee17a3b67d9a834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e2827f0656f23647a5ad5b252099d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9de68fb6438d36191c59a2bd51dc2410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0019d86a98d6eeaac4d5a59a03aa2580</data>
</node>
