  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">4.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each time `apipeline_process_enqueue_documents` starts up, it pulls all documents in `PARSING` / `ANALYZING` / `PROCESSING` / `PENDING` / `FAILED` to continue processing. The resume path **branches by &quot;whether content has been extracted&quot;**, ensuring that any document, regardless of its previous progress, has an idempotent result when resumed under the current `process_options`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Increase `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` to 100 when processing extremely large batches of documents: `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=100`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Entity and relation extraction is not performed if the `!` option is used.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Three layers of semantic guarantee:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The resume rule only applies to documents whose `doc_id` already exists in `doc_status`. New files joining the queue require the file dedup logic in &quot;Concurrency and Reentry Constraints&quot;, to avoid new files squeezing out the records of files whose content has already been successfully extracted.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Increase `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` to 200 when processing massive batches of documents across multiple cloud regions: `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=200`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks are still written to the vector store regardless of the `!` option.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**`addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` full baseline** (modifiable at runtime via SDK, affecting subsequent enqueues):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Many knowledge fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction. Add them below using the same format.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Parse queues are **created dynamically from the registry's `ParserSpec.queue_group` (one registry snapshot per batch): the built-in native/mineru/docling each own a group, legacy shares the native pool (local, no network), and a third-party engine may declare its own group with a custom worker count (see `docs/ThirdPartyParser-zh.md`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunking strategies F/R/V/P determine how text is divided into chunks.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**`full_docs[doc_id][&quot;chunk_options&quot;]` slim snapshot** (projected by selector; example below is for `process_options=&quot;R&quot;`):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Add them below using the same format.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Parse queues for the mineru and docling engines are specified to be `parse_queues[&quot;mineru&quot;]` and `parse_queues[&quot;docling&quot;]` respectively, each with a certain number of workers: N2 and N3, and these queues are part of a system of parse queues that includes processing, analyzing, and inserting into the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The document processing background task is running, including the classification stage and processing stage.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;selector → sub-dictionary mapping: F → `fixed_token`, R → `recursive_character`, V → `semantic_vector`, P → `paragraph_semantic`; without a selector, F is the default. Each sub-dictionary corresponds one-to-one with the keyword-only parameters of the corresponding chunker function; when adding new parameters, no dispatcher change is needed, just add a kwarg to the chunker function.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;parameters of the `mineru` / `docling` engines will also invalidate the cache, causing the engine to re-parse the file content on the next upload of the same file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The &lt;3rd-party group&gt; parse queue is specified to be `parse_queues[&lt;3rd-party group&gt;]` and it has a custom pool, which is created per ParserSpec.queue_group, indicating a specific configuration for third-party engines.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/scan` endpoint uses the background task to reject overlapping scans; it does not block upload/insert operations itself.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `file_path` | Basename of the filename (without directory), **preserves the original name provided by the user (including the square-bracket hint)**, e.g., `abc.[native-iet].docx` is written as-is. When no valid source is provided, it is saved as `unknown_source`. The filename hint is not stripped, so the management UI can &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`native` is LightRAG's built-in structured content extractor that runs **fully locally**: it does not depend on external services such as MinerU / Docling, the extraction stage never calls a VLM, and it works out of the box with no deployment. Its runtime dependencies are only `python-docx` + `defusedxml` (required); the markdown path additionally relies on the **optional** `cairosvg` for SVG rasterization (when missing, the SVG is skipped with a warning and the rest of the content is unaffected).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The process of resolving the stored document parser engine and the role of environment variables in tuning system parameters are highlighted. Environment variables control system behavior, with their values affecting the system's performance and functionality. These values are read at the construction of `LightRAG` and can be adjusted through `.env` or environment variables. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `scanning_exclusive` flag is an exclusive subset of `scanning` and is true only during the classification phase of the scan.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;U path — LightRAG mandates `canonical_basename` uniqueness within the same workspace (HTTP 409 on upload / enqueue), and combined with the pipeline's serialization per document, `*.docling_raw/` has no concurrent write conflicts and needs no extra locks.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Supported extensions: `docx` / `md` / `textpack`. How to enable:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The role of `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` as a worker pool size and semaphore cap is emphasized. It is the maximum number of concurrent documents that can be processed at the entity/relation extraction + ingest stage. This value serves as a limit for the concurrency level of the process stage.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `run_scanning_process` reads `doc_status` to classify documents during the classification phase and cannot interleave with concurrent writers.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`_manifest.json` invalidation conditions (any triggers a cache miss): Source file size or sha256 does not match manifest; `DOCLING_ENDPOINT` does not match the `endpoint_signature` recorded in manifest; `DOCLING_ENGINE_VERSION` is set and does not match the `engine_version` recorded in manifest; `options_signature` does not match — any OCR / equation / pipeline field change triggers it, covering: Tunable env: `DOCLING_DO_OCR` / `DOCLING_FORCE_OCR` / `DOCLING_OCR_ENGINE` / `DOCLING_OCR_PRESET` / `DOCLING_OCR_LANG` / `DOCLING_DO_FORMULA_ENRICHMENT`; Hard-coded constants: `pipeline` / `target_type` / `to_formats` / `image_export_mode` (written into the signature to prevent old bundles from being mistakenly reused if these values change in the future); Main JSON missing, size, or sha256 does not match; Any image in `artifacts/` missing or size mismatch; `LIGHTRAG_FORCE_REPARSE_DOCLING=true`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`native` parses OOXML directly and recognizes the following structures, writing them to the corresponding sidecars (whether a sidecar is produced depends on the document's actual content; see [§4.2](#42-__parsed__-directory-structure)):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The significance of queue sizes and backpressure is noted. The small default `QUEUE_SIZE_INSERT=4` is chosen to prevent memory bloat during the slow and memory-intensive process stage. This size provides backpressure to the analyze stage and prevents overloading the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After classification, the `scanning_exclusive` flag is cleared immediately, and concurrent uploads are allowed once the scan enters the processing phase.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The &quot;either side empty → skip&quot; semantics of `engine_version` / `endpoint_signature` is the same as MinerU §4.3: when the field was empty at manifest-write time (first parse without `DOCLING_ENGINE_VERSION` configured) or when the current environment variable is not set, the check is skipped for that item; adding the version number later does not automatically invalidate the historical cache; `LIGHTRAG_FORCE_REPARSE_DOCLING=true` is needed to trigger.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Image export details:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`file_source`, and duplicates are checked by the basename of `file_source`; lacking a valid `file_source` returns 400 directly.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `pending_enqueues` count represents the number of upload/insert calls that have passed `_reserve_enqueue_slot` but have not completed their background task.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/documents/scan` directory scanning uses the same set of indexes, but in order to facilitate automatic retry of unfinished files, it has separate archive and re-process rules for duplicate filenames.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The affected blocks' `positions` degrade to `[{&quot;type&quot;: &quot;paraid&quot;, &quot;range&quot;: null}]`. This is only a notice and **does not affect parsing success**; if you need precise paragraph provenance, follow the hint and &quot;Save As .docx&quot; in Word 2013+ to regenerate the ids.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When the SDK path calls `insert` / `ainsert` / `apipeline_enqueue_documents` without `file_paths`, that is allowed; related behavior is detailed in §8.4. Such documents without a source have `file_path` saved as `unknown_source`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The background task releases the slot in `finally` after completing its execution.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For ordinary upload, text APIs, and core enqueue APIs, as long as a file with the same name already exists in `doc_status` — whether that record is currently `PENDING`, `PARSING`, `ANALYZING`, `PROCESSING`, `FAILED`, or `PROCESSED` — the same-name file is considered a duplicate.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `md`: splits by heading (ATX `#`), recognizes native pipe tables (with header), HTML `&lt;table&gt;` (with `&lt;thead&gt;`, preserving colspan/rowspan), block-level equations (a paragraph starting with `$$` and ending with `$$`; inline `$...`)">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Empty strings, `no-file-path`, and `unknown_source` are all considered unknown sources; they do not block new source-less text from being enqueued, nor do they deduplicate each other as same-named files.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `request_pending` signal prompts the running processing loop to scan another round.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For `/documents/scan` directory scan: If multiple files in the same scan share the same canonicalized name, the file with a supported engine hint is processed first; if no variant has a hint, the first file after sorting is processed, and the rest are archived to `__parsed__` and skipped.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `textpack`: is a native-exclusive extension and is routed to native automatically without a hint/rule.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The storage backend provides basename direct lookup via `get_doc_by_file_basename`, internally comparing against the `canonical_basename` field (the input parameter is first canonicalized through `canonicalize_parser_hinted_basename`). `JsonDocStatusStorage` already implements an in-memory traversal; other backends currently fall back to the default implementation (scanning all states and comparing `canonical_basename`), to be augmented with native indexes in subsequent PRs.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The processing loop checks `request_pending` after each batch and re-pulls the snapshot.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If the same-name record is already `PROCESSED`, the file just scanned is treated as already processed; the system emits a warning, moves the input file to the sibling `__parsed__` directory, and skips enqueueing.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MANY knowdge fragements with entities were missed in the last extraction. Add them below using the same format:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Documents with different filenames but identical extracted content are also considered duplicates. The hash here is the content hash of the final text or LightRAG Document obtained by the configured extraction engine; it is not the hash of the original file bytes.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Entry point behavior for `/documents/upload`, `/documents/text`, and `/documents/texts` when `scanning_exclusive=True` or `destructive_busy=True` results in an HTTP 409 error, and the file is not written or enqueued.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If the same-name record is not `PROCESSED`, the scanned file is not skipped simply because of the same name, but also does not re-extract / overwrite the existing record. The specific path depends on the form of the existing record (consistent with the classification rules listed below in the &quot;Why is scan still the exclusive writer&quot; section):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;mineru-api image set to mineru:latest &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `full_docs` and `doc_status` write or fill in the `content_hash` field according to the content format:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If not, the file is saved and a background task is scheduled, with the slot reserved by `pending_enqueues++` and a strict name precheck performed.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Same name non-PROCESSED with `full_docs` present → **resume path**: doc_status is preserved as-is, the source file remains in `INPUT/`, and the processing loop picks it up by status query (no re-extract, no overwrite of existing status).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;container_name for mineru-api is set to mineru-api &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `parse_format=raw`: the MD5 of the text after `sanitize_text_for_encoding`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/documents/scan` endpoint emits a warning and returns `scanning_skipped_pipeline_busy` if `busy=True`, `scanning=True`, or `pending_enqueues&gt;0` and immediately returns without scheduling a background task.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Same name `FAILED` with `full_docs` missing → recognized as an extraction-error stub written by `apipeline_enqueue_error_documents`: scan deletes the stub and **enqueues the current file(&quot;hyper-relation&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;restart policy for mineru-api is always &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `parse_format=lightrag`: the MD5 of the `*.blocks.jsonl` file parsed out of `lightrag_document_path`. Relative paths are resolved against `INPUT_DIR`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If all conditions are idle, the `/documents/scan` endpoint sets `scanning=True` and schedules the background task, which clears the flag in `finally` upon completion.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For ordinary upload and core enqueue APIs, a file with the same name — even if its content has changed — must have its old document record deleted before re-upload or re-enqueue; the two automatic recoveries above only apply to the directory-scan path.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;profiles for mineru-api include api &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `parse_format=pending_parse`: no hash is written yet; it is filled in by subsequent steps after parsing actually completes (to avoid mistakenly judging by empty content).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/documents/clear` and `/documents/delete_document` endpoints return `status=&quot;busy&quot;` synchronously and do not schedule a background task if `busy=True`, `scanning=True`, or `pending_enqueues&gt;0`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text APIs must provide a valid `file_source`, and duplicates are checked by the basename of `file_source`; lacking a valid `file_source` returns 400 directly.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ports exposed for mineru-api are 8000:8000 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The `legacy` path deduplicates content hashes after locally extracting text and during enqueue; on hit, this record is written as `FAILED duplicate`, and no new `full_docs`, chunks, or graph data are generated.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If all conditions are idle, the endpoints set `busy=True` and `destructive_busy=True` before the `delete_document` returns `deletion_started`, and the background task's `finally` clears both flags.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Empty strings, `no-file-path`, and `unknown_source` are all considered invalid `file_source` values, and the text APIs will return a 400 error if any of these are provided.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;environment variables set for mineru-api include MINERU_MODEL_SOURCE: local &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The `native` / `mineru` / `docling` paths first enqueue with `pending_parse`; after parsing completes and `content_hash` is filled in, if another document already has the same hash, this record is stopped before entering analysis, chunking, entity extraction, and graph writing.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `apipeline_enqueue_documents` internal (last-line guard) throws a `RuntimeError` if `scanning_exclusive=True` and `from_scan=False`, or `destructive_busy=True`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG document processing pipeline supports MinerU as a document parser and offers two MinerU access modes: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;environment variables set for mineru-api include MINERU_TOOLS_CONFIG_JSON: /root/mineru-lightrag.json &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Duplicate records are marked as `filename` or `content_hash` in `metadata.duplicate_kind` for diagnosis. Content-hash duplicates also record `metadata.is_duplicate=true`, `metadata.original_doc_id`, and `metadata.original_track_id`; duplicates discovered only after parsing also have the temporarily-written `full_docs` deleted.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Otherwise, it enqueues normally and nudges `request_pending=True` after writing `doc_status` if `busy=True`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then add the following configuration to LightRAG's `.env` file: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;volumes mounted for mineru-api include ./mineru-lightrag.json:/root/mineru-lightrag.json &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Related warnings minimize repetitive noise: when scanning discovers a same-name file already `PROCESSED`, a log and pipeline status are written; duplicates at the enqueue stage use the LightRAG layer's `Duplicate document detected (...)` log; content duplicates only discovered after parsing use `Duplicate content skipped after parsing` and write a pipeline status. Scan archiving does not emit the extra `[File Extraction]Duplicate skipped`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `from_scan=True` flag is a bypass for the scan's own background-task enqueue to allow enqueueing files that have already been scanned.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT=https://mineru.net   # Default value, usually no need to change &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;entrypoint for mineru-api is mineru-api &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The storage backend provides hash direct lookup via `get_doc_by_content_hash`; the naming convention is the same as `get_doc_by_file_basename`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In the old version, `busy=True` always rejected any new enqueue, reasoning that modifying `doc_status` would interleave with the pipeline worker thread.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;* `local` mode: uses a locally deployed MinerU service. See the deployment instructions below. After the local MinerU service is started, add the following configuration to LightRAG's `.env` file: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;command executed for mineru-api includes --host 0.0.0.0 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;&gt; Within an enqueue batch (the same `apipeline_enqueue_documents` call), basename and content_hash dedup are also performed; on hit, subsequent entries are written as `FAILED` directly and marked with `existing_status=batch_duplicate`. Basename dedup only applies to valid filenames; `unknown_source`, `no-file-path`, and empty sources only participate in content-hash dedup.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;However, in practice, write order guarantees consistency, batch-level snapshots prevent interleaving, and `request_pending` is designed to handle new work arrivals.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After the local MinerU service is started, add the following configuration to LightRAG's `.env` file: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;command executed for mineru-api includes --port 8000 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Cross-call concurrent dedup** is also guaranteed by the workspace-level serialization lock (see [§6.7 enqueue serialization lock (preventing concurrent dedup leakage)](#67-enqueue-serialization-lock-preventing-concurrent-dedup-leakage)): two concurrent enqueues of identical content with different filenames will not both leak past the `content_hash` check.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;With this mechanism, users can continue to upload new documents during long batch processing, and the background task will automatically be picked up by the running loop after writing `doc_status`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For the remaining detailed MinerU configuration, refer to the MinerU section of the environment variable example file [env.example](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/blob/main/env.example) at the repository root. The `official` and `local` modes each have different environment variable configurations; read the instructions in the example file carefully. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;command executed for mineru-api includes --allow-public-http-client &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Copy `Dockerfile` and `compose.yaml` from the official GitHub repository [opendatalab/MinerU](https://github.com/opendatalab/MinerU) to your local machine. Both files can be found in the repository's `docker` directory. For special GPUs from Chinese vendors, you need to choose the corresponding `Dockerfile`. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Scan is still the exclusive writer because it enqueues new files and reads `doc_status` to make classification decisions, which cannot interleave with other writers.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MANY knowledge fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction. Add them below using the same format.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;command executed for mineru-api includes --gpu-memory-utilization 0.45 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Starting from version v1.5.0 (currently on the dev branch), LightRAG's file processing pipeline has received a major upgrade.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After classification, scan reads `doc_status` to decide what to do with each file, including archiving, resuming, or deleting based on the status and presence of `full_docs`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After preparing the two files above, build the Docker image with the following command: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;command executed for mineru-api includes --enable-vlm-preload true &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Supports multiple file content extraction engines: legacy, native, mineru, docling.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;These read–decide–write combinations cannot interleave with other writers, so scan must remain the exclusive writer, and the scan endpoint will reject operations when necessary.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;docker build --tag mineru:latest . &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ulimits set for mineru-api include memlock: -1 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Supports multiple text chunking methods: Fix, Recursive, Vector, Paragraph.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Many knowledge fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction process.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed4f68e46f6dea178b121e735b681e3b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once the image is built, start the API service with the following command (the `--profile api` parameter indicates starting only MinerU's API service; the service listens on port 8000 by default): &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ulimits set for mineru-api include stack: 67108864 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Supports disabling entity-relation extraction for individual files.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;detection knobs `CHUNK_P_REFERENCES_TAIL_N` (default 2) / `CHUNK_P_REFERENCES_HEADINGS` (pipe-separated, default `References\|Bibliography\|参考文献`) are env-only and read live at run time. Global default can be set via env var `CHUNK_P_DROP_REFERENCES.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;docker compose -f compose.yaml --profile api up -d &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;IPC is set to host &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG Server introduces an intermediate file-processing format: `LightRAG Document`. This format supports multimodal data such as tables and images, and also includes the document's section/paragraph metadata, which is convenient for content traceability later.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Parameters may also be attached to the **engine token** to override an external engine's per-file behaviour. They are encoded into the persisted `parse_engine` field and feed both the engine request and its raw-bundle cache signature (so changing a parameter forces a re-parse rather than reusing a stale bundle).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For image build details, GPU driver setup, model weight locations, etc., refer to the official README: &lt;https://github.com/opendatalab/MinerU&gt;. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;healthcheck for mineru-api includes curl -f http://localhost:8000/health || exit 1 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This document is organized from the perspective of **LightRAG Server** deployment and use: the quick-start configuration that can be applied directly is given first, followed by configuration syntax for content extraction and chunking, storage / directory layout, deduplication, concurrency, and resume rules.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;```text\npaper.[mineru(page_range=1-3,language=en,local_parse_method=ocr)].pdf   # filename hint\nscan.[docling(force_ocr=true)].pdf\nLIGHTRAG_PARSER=pdf:mineru(language=en);*:legacy-R                       # rule\n```&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Advanced configuration: enabling vLLM preload and title-level correction (optional)** &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;deploy resources set for mineru-api include devices with driver: nvidia &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Keep the legacy file-processing behavior: All files are processed using the legacy document parsing and chunking strategy. Either leave `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` unconfigured, or set it to the following value: `&lt;br&gt;` ```bash&lt;br&gt;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER=*:legacy-F`&lt;br&gt;````&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Currently supported engine parameters (canonical / alias):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;On top of the basic deployment, it is recommended to additionally enable two MinerU **server-side** features for your local MinerU. Both modify MinerU container-side configuration (the in-container `mineru.json` and the official `compose.yaml`), and do not involve any LightRAG env variable; title-level correction additionally requires an available LLM API. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;deploy resources set for mineru-api include device_ids: [&quot;0&quot;] &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Recommended starting file-processing behavior: No reliance on external document parsing services or on `VLM` vision models. Use the new built-in `Native` engine to parse `docx` documents with table (t) and equation (e) modality analysis enabled, paired with the `P` chunking strategy; other documents use the legacy content extractor paired with the more effective `R` chunking strategy. `&lt;br&gt;` ```bash&lt;br&gt;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER=*:native-teP,*:legacy-R`&lt;br&gt;````&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **`page_range` may contain multiple page segments — write one `page_range=...` item per segment.** Inside `(...)` a comma only separates parameters, so a multi-segment list should be written as `page_range=1-3,page_range=5,page_range=7-9`, not as the env-var single-string form `MINERU_PAGE_RANGES=&quot;1-3,5,7-9&quot;`. A **multi-segment** `page_range` requires `MINERU_API_MODE=official`; `local` mode accepts only a single page/range (for example, `page_range=1-3`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **vLLM startup preload**: loads the VLM model into GPU memory at container startup, avoiding the model-loading latency on the first parse request. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;deploy resources set for mineru-api include capabilities: [gpu] &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Enable multimodal processing capability: Enabling multimodal processing requires the `MinerU` file parsing service and a `VLM` vision recognition model. Use `Native` to parse `docx` files; use `MinerU` to parse `pdf`, `office`, and various image files. All of the above files have image (i), table (t), and equation (e) modality analysis enabled and are paired with the `P` chunking strategy. Other documents fall back to the legacy content extractor paired with the `R` chunking strategy. `&lt;br&gt;` ```bash&lt;br&gt;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER=*:native-iteP,*:mineru-iteP,*:legacy-R`&lt;br&gt;```` `&lt;br&gt;` `VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE=true` `&lt;br&gt;` `VLM_LLM_MODEL=kimi-k2.6` `&lt;br&gt;` `MINERU_API_MODE=local` `&lt;br&gt;` `MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **`local_parse_method` is local-only.** It only affects the local MinerU request, so it is **rejected** under `MINERU_API_MODE=official` (the official API neither sends it nor folds it into the cache key — accepting it would silently do nothing).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Title-level correction (`title_aided`)**: MinerU uses an external LLM to correct the title hierarchy of the parsed output, improving the quality of the structured artifacts. This is especially helpful for the [P (paragraph semantic) chunking strategy](#25-file-processing-options), which depends on the title structure; the `P` chunking strategy splits by titles first, so the more accurate the title hierarchy, the better the chunking semantics. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Restarting the API service to take effect &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For VLM configuration, see [Role-based LLM/VLM Configuration Guide](RoleSpecificLLMConfiguration.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Only `mineru` and `docling` accept engine parameters; attaching one to `legacy`/`native` is a friendly error. Validation runs at startup (`LIGHTRAG_PARSER`) and at upload.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Step 1: Export and modify `mineru-lightrag.json` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Using the Docling File Parsing Engine &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The complete configuration model is as follows: `&lt;br&gt;` ```text&lt;br&gt;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER=ext:engine-options,ext:engine,*:legacy-R&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`filename.[ENGINE].ext&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`filename.[ENGINE-OPTIONS].ext&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`filename.[-OPTIONS].ext&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;````&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Merge priority: engine parameters resolve for the **final engine** — a rule's engine parameters are dropped when a filename hint selects a different (usable) engine.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Copy `/root/mineru.json` from the official image to `mineru-lightrag.json` in the host's current directory (using the fixed container name `temp_mineru`, without running the container): &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Minimal configuration for Docling File Parsing Engine &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Common combination examples: `&lt;br&gt;` ```bash&lt;br&gt;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER=pdf:mineru-R,docx:native-ietP,*:legacy-R&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`MINERU_API_MODE=local&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`DOCLING_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:5001`&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`my-proposal.[native-iet].docx   # Use the native engine, enable drawing/table/equation analysis&lt;br&gt;`&lt;br&gt;`my-memo.[native-R!].docx        # Use the native engine, recursive semantic chunking, disable knowledge graph construction`&lt;br&gt;````&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `parse_engine` is stored in hint syntax (e.g. `mineru(page_range=1-3)`) and shown in `doc_status` metadata so you can see the parse parameters a document used.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;docker create --name temp_mineru mineru:latest &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Environment variables for Docling File Parsing Engine &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For backward compatibility, when the configuration is not modified, the upgraded file content extraction behavior remains the original `legacy` behavior. To enable the new content processing engines, configure as described in this section.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Engine | Description | Supported file formats (extensions) |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;docker cp temp_mineru:/root/mineru.json ./mineru-lightrag.json &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Polling-budget environment variables for Docling File Parsing Engine &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To enable the new content processing engines, configure as described in this section.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`mineru` and `docling` are external content extraction engines; before enabling related rules, the services must be running first, and the corresponding endpoint/token must be configured in LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;docker rm temp_mineru &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Bundle-cache environment variables for Docling File Parsing Engine &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MANY knowdge fragements with entities were missed in the last extraction.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG caches the parsing results of the `mineru` and `docling` engines locally. Re-uploading the same file usually does not trigger the engine to re-parse the document. To delete the parse cache, you must click the &quot;also delete file&quot; option in the delete-file dialog of the document management interface. Modifying the endpoint addresses and effective extraction parameters of the `mineru` / `docling` engines will also invalidate the cache, causing the engine to re-parse the file content on the next upload of the same file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then modify `llm-aided-config.title_aided` in `mineru-lightrag.json`: fill in `api_key` and change `enable` to `true` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Prerequisites for `DOCLING_DO_FORMULA_ENRICHMENT` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text document discusses various aspects of the LightRAG parser and its chunking strategies, including the responsibilities of process_options and chunk_options, as well as the environment variables involved in configuring the chunker parameter settings.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`native` is LightRAG's built-in structured content extractor that runs **fully locally**: it does not depend on external services such as MinerU / Docling, the extraction stage never calls a VLM, and it works out of the box with no deployment&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`api_key` / `base_url` / `model` should be replaced with an LLM service available to you (the example uses Alibaba Cloud DashScope's OpenAI-compatible endpoint). &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Docling Local Deployment &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The responsibilities of process_options and chunk_options are orthogonal, with process_options selecting the chunking strategy and chunk_options deciding the parameters to use for that strategy.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Many knowledge fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction, indicating a potential issue with the extraction process or data interpretation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You need to register an account at the [MinerU official website](https://mineru.net/) and create an API-KEY first. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Enable LaTeX equation recognition &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;All environment variables are read into `addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` during the `LightRAG.__init__` stage, and the service must be restarted for changes to take effect.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The legacy `apipeline_enqueue_documents` behavior of `reprocess_existing_non_processed=True` would directly delete non-PROCESSED old records and rebuild them during scan, which conflicts with the rules in §5 / §6; it has been entirely removed.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MINERU_API_TOKEN=&lt;your_token&gt; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Important note for GPU support &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Environment variables are read into `addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` once when `LightRAG` is instantiated, and the service must be restarted for changes to take effect.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Replacement paths: scan handles same-named files per the classification rules in §6.4 (archive / resume / delete stub then re-enqueue), uniformly picked up by the resume rules in §7 inside the processing loop.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">24.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT=http://&lt;your_mineru_local_server_ip&gt;:8000 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The image for mineru-api is specified as mineru:latest &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Documents already enqueued hold the frozen snapshot of `full_docs.chunk_options` and are unaffected by changes to environment variables.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Automatic resume: scan handles same-named files per the classification rules in §6.4 (archive / resume / delete stub then re-enqueue), uniformly picked up by the resume rules in §7 inside the processing loop.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">24.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For the remaining detailed MinerU configuration, refer to the MinerU section of the environment variable example file [env.example](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/blob/main/env.example) at the repository root. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The container mineru-api has a restart policy of always &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The chunker invocation takes the corresponding sub-dictionary from `full_docs.chunk_options` and dispatches to F/R/V/P by the `process_options.chunking` selector.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Forced refresh: first call `/documents/{doc_id}` to delete the old document, then upload the same-named new file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">24.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
