  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text does not provide any explicit entities or relationships related to 'V strategy-specific `chunk_token_size` (hard cap, automatically re-split through R when exceeded)' as these are part of the default settings for the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `process_options.chunking` selector dispatches the chunker invocation to the appropriate chunking strategy (F/R/V/P) based on the selected strategy.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The legacy `apipeline_enqueue_documents` behavior of `reprocess_existing_non_processed=True` would directly delete non-PROCESSED old records and rebuild them during scan, which conflicts with the rules in §5 / §6; it has been entirely removed. This means that the system will no longer delete non-PROCESSED records by default when enqueueing new documents.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After upload passes the reservation but before saving the file, a two-pass check is required:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The entrypoint for mineru-api is mineru-api &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text does not provide any explicit entities or relationships related to 'V inherits the top-level resolved value when unset' as these are part of the default settings for the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `CHUNK_SIZE` environment variable is the legacy top-level chunk_token_size fallback for the chunker parameter settings.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Automatic resume: scan handles same-named files per the classification rules in §6.4 (archive / resume / delete stub then re-enqueue), uniformly picked up by the resume rules in §7 inside the processing loop. This ensures that the system can resume processing without losing any data or reprocessing the same documents multiple times.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **INPUT directory scan**: canonicalize the basename to be saved via `canonicalize_parser_hinted_basename`, traverse the INPUT directory for any existing same-canonical variant (with hint / without hint); 409 on hit.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The command executed for mineru-api includes --host 0.0.0.0 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text does not provide any explicit entities or relationships related to 'server-only deployments usually don't hit this tier' as these are part of the default settings for the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `CHUNK_OVERLAP_SIZE` environment variable is the legacy overlap fallback for the chunker parameter settings when no specific overlap settings are provided for the chosen chunking strategy.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Forced refresh: first call `/documents/{doc_id}` to delete the old document, then upload the same-named new file. This method ensures that the system always uses the most recent version of the document.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. **doc_status check**: call `get_existing_doc_by_file_basename` with the canonicalized basename; 409 on hit.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The command executed for mineru-api includes --port 8000 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text mentions 'R separator cascade', which is a method used to split text into chunks based on semantic boundaries, ordered from the strongest to the weakest.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `CHUNK_F_SIZE` environment variable is the strategy-specific `chunk_token_size` for the F (forward) chunking strategy if it is not explicitly set.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The removal of the `reprocess_existing_non_processed=True` behavior and the introduction of these new methods are intended to provide a more robust and predictable system that adheres to the rules outlined in §5 / §6 without the risk of unintended data loss or reprocessing.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Both pass → save the file → schedule the bg task → bg task calls `apipeline_enqueue_documents` to write the store + calls `apipeline_process_enqueue_documents` to trigger processing.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
