  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text specifies that server-only deployments typically do not need to interact with the explicit chunker settings, as these are usually handled at the client or server level depending on the deployment setup.&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It computes embeddings of adjacent sentences, then finds semantic breakpoints based on the specified threshold strategy (e.g., percentile, standard_deviation, or interquartile) for splitting.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
