</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When the body under the same heading is too long and falls back to R, overlap can be preserved according to `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`; bridging text between adjacent large tables can also be repeated into the surrounding table chunks within that budget.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Endpoint for the current mode (`MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT` / `MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT`) and the `endpoint_signature` recorded in manifest are both non-empty but inconsistent;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. B reads `doc_status` to check `content_hash`: still miss (A hasn't upserted yet).">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;my-memo.[native-R!].docx        # Use the native engine, recursive semantic chunking, disable knowledge graph construction&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
