  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This chunking method can only be applied to `lightrag` content stored in the sidecar directory. If `lightrag` content does not exist, it degrades to chunking with `R`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `content_list.json` size or sha256 does not match manifest;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. A upserts `full_docs` + `doc_status`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;my-proposal.[-!].docx           # Use the default engine, only disable knowledge graph construction&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This chunking method produces far fewer overlapping chunks than the `R` or `F` strategies.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Size of any recorded non-critical file (images, `middle.json`, etc.) does not match manifest;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;4. B upserts `full_docs` + `doc_status`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;my-proposal.[mineru].docx       # Use the MinerU engine, all processing options default&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The global multimodal switch `addon_params[&quot;enable_multimodal_pipeline&quot;]` is deprecated; the related behavior is now uniformly controlled by the file-level `i/t/e` options. See [Appendix A](#appendix-a-notes-on-upgrading-from-legacy).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;About the &quot;either side empty → skip&quot; semantics of `engine_version` / `endpoint_signature`: when the field was empty at manifest-write time (e.g., `MINERU_ENGINE_VERSION` was not configured at first parse), or when the current environment variable is not set, the check is skipped for that item. If the version env was not set at first parse, setting it later does not automatically invalidate the historical cache — this scenario requires manually setting `LIGHTRAG_FORCE_REPARSE_MINERU=true` to trigger re-parsing.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Result: both `PENDING` rows with the same `content_hash` enter the downstream pipeline, and the row that should have been identified as `duplicate_kind=content_hash` was **not** identified.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ext:engine;ext:engine;*:legacy&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Different characters of processing options take effect at different stages of the pipeline:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `docling` engine extracts the zip artifact returned by docling-serve (DoclingDocument JSON, Markdown, and referenced images) into the `__parsed__/&lt;canonical filename&gt;.docling_raw/` directory during parsing, and writes `_manifest.json` as the integrity validation file. On a subsequent parse, the IR builder reads the `.json` file in that directory and feeds it to `DoclingIRBuilder`, no longer calling docling-serve.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;With the serialization lock, the second enqueue's dedup read is guaranteed to see the row already upserted by the first, taking the normal &quot;no new unique document&quot; early-return path and writing this run as a `duplicate_kind=content_hash` FAILED row.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ext:engine-options&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Option | Stage | Description |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Directory layout:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The lock only covers:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LIGHTRAG_PARSER=docx:native-iet&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| i/t/e | Analyzing (multimodal analysis) | Determines whether VLM summarization analysis is invoked on the images / tables / equations in the sidecar.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Avoid duplicate uploads/conversions. When parsing the same file again, the source file's hash + size is first validated against `_manifest.json`; on hit, the upload / poll / download against docling-serve is skipped, and the local `.json` is fed directly through DoclingIRBuilder → SidecarWriter.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The lock does **not** cover the `request_pending` nudge (outside the lock; only briefly takes `pipeline_status_lock`), and does **not** block the `get_docs_by_statuses` read of the processing loop (which goes through `doc_status`'s own concurrent reads — a KV-level atomic with the enqueue writes, not contending for the same lock). Lock order: `enqueue_serialize → pipeline_status_lock`; no deadlock path.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LIGHTRAG_PARSER=pdf:legacy-R(chunk_ts=800,chunk_ol=80);*:legacy-R&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**The extraction stage is unaffected**: the content extraction engine outputs `drawings.json` / `tables.json` / `equations.json` sidecar files based on what the document actually contains.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Preserve diagnostic information. When docling-serve parses incorrectly or downstream sidecar fields are abnormal, you can go straight to `*.docling_raw/` to compare the original DoclingDocument JSON, Markdown, and `artifacts/` images.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The pipeline is divided into 3 stages, each with an independently tunable worker pool:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;paper.[mineru-R].pdf                            # filename hint&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;As a result, simply tweaking the `i`/`t`/`e` options to trigger &quot;re-analysis&quot; can complete VLM later without re-parsing the original file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MANY knowlege fragements with entities were missed in the last extraction.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;N1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">85.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Add them below using the same format:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| ! | Extraction (entity-relation extraction) | Skips entity/relation extraction and graph writing; chunks are still written to the vector store to retain naive / mix retrieval capabilities.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;slides.[docling].pptx&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;N2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">85.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When archived, the original filename (including `[hint]`) is preserved, e.g., `report.[native-iet].docx` is archived as `__parsed__/report.[native-iet].docx`, making it easy to trace the user's original name and processing options.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;memo.[native-P].docx&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| F/R/V/P | Chunking (text chunking) | Determines which chunking strategy to use; does not affect the output of the parsing stage.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;is incrementally filled in; when changing `F/R/V/P`, chunks and graph are rebuilt; when changing `!`, KG construction is stopped or restored. Engine changes are considered a &quot;major change&quot;, uniformly handled by delete + re-upload, not implicitly happening on the resume path.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;N3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">85.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;notes.[-R(chunk_ts=800,chunk_ol=80)].md                            # filename hint&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;&gt; Modality availability is signaled solely by &quot;whether the sidecar file exists&quot;; the content extraction engine does not need to declare its capabilities in meta.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This chapter targets developers who **directly import the `LightRAG` class** for integration, covering runtime APIs, constructor parameters, and removed legacy interfaces that Server deployments don't use. Server users usually don't need to read this chapter.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;N4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">85.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;notes.[-R(chunk_ts=800,chunk_ol=80)].md                            # rule&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If a given document contains no images/tables/equations, the corresponding sidecar is not written; even if the user has enabled `i/t/e`, the corresponding modality is silently skipped, but `analyze_multimodal` logs an INFO-level line for that document (`[analyze_multimodal] sidecar e:equations empty: doc—id ...`), making it easy to diagnose &quot;why didn't the VLM run&quot;.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;```python\nfrom lightrag import LightRAG\nrag = LightRAG(working_dir=&quot;./rag_storage&quot;, ...)\nawait rag.initialize_storages()\nawait rag.ainsert(&quot;text&quot;, file_paths=&quot;doc.pdf&quot;)```&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;abling LaTeX equation recognition)">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Configuration settings for MINERU and DOCLING are specified.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This is not an error.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following behaviors of this invocation style differ from the Server path: you can change `addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` without restarting the process, you can pass per-file `chunk_options` into `apipeline_enqueue_documents`, and you can dynamically override the F strategy's pre-split parameters in an `ainsert` call.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following uses a Docker-based docling-serve deployment as an example, giving the complete steps from image download to model mounting.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The analysis result directory: structured parsing results are written into a subdirectory named with the **canonicalized filename** (with `[hint]` removed) plus the `.parsed` suffix, avoiding name conflicts with the archived original file and ensuring that the same logical document continues to point to the same directory when the filename hint or processing options change.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The MINERU_API_MODE is set to local.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` is strictly validated at startup: unknown content extraction engines, malformed extension syntax, explicitly using an unsupported extension, external engines missing endpoint, and illegal characters in processing options all cause startup to fail.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`LightRAG(chunk_token_size=…, chunk_overlap_token_size=…)` is **tier 3** in §3.3's priority chain: &quot;legacy constructor field&quot;. Strategy-agnostic and coarse-grained default, fills only slots still empty:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After deployment completes, write `DOCLING_DO_FORMULA_ENRICHMENT=true` into LightRAG's `.env` to enable LaTeX equation recognition.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For example, the analysis results of `report.docx`, `report.[native].docx`, and `report.[native-iet].docx` are all written into `__parsed__/report.docx.parsed/`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT is set to http://localhost:8000.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- When a wildcard rule matches a certain extension, the engine must pass two usability checks (see `parser_routing._engine_is_usable`): (a) the engine's capability table supports that extension; (b) if it is an external engine (`mineru` / `docling`), the corresponding endpoint/token environment variable is configured.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Lower priority than `addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` explicit values (§8.3) and strategy-specific env (§3.2).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Important**: the steps below are based on an environment where the GPU supports CUDA 13. If your GPU is older and does not support CUDA 13, replace the image name `docling-serve-cu130:main` in the command and compose file with the tag corresponding to your CUDA version. For the list of available images, see [docling-serve Packages](https://github.com/orgs/docling-project/packages?repo_name=docling-serve).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Analysis result files: the LightRAG Document blocks file and sidecars are named with the canonicalized filename stem, e.g., `__parsed__/report.docx.parsed/report.blocks.jsonl`; the same directory may also contain `report.tables.json`, `report.drawings.json`, `report.equations.json`, and the `report.blocks.assets/` image asset directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The DOCLING_ENDPOINT is set to http://localhost:5001.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Filename hints have higher priority than `LIGHTRAG_PARSER`. If the engine specified in a hint does not support that extension, the system falls back to the default rules to continue selecting an available engine.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Higher priority than the legacy env `CHUNK_SIZE` / `CHUNK_OVERLAP_SIZE`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**1. Pull the image**">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;File processing configurations are provided for specific files.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- If the filename hint provides a non-empty options string, the hint takes precedence; otherwise the default options of the matching item in `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` are used; if neither is provided, all defaults are used.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The instance fields `self.chunk_token_size` / `self.chunk_overlap_token_size` are always back-filled to `int` after `__post_init__`, so legacy paths still reading these two fields (e.g., the `chunk_opts.get(&quot;chunk_token_size&quot;) or self.chunk_token_size` fallback in `pipeline.py`) continue to work.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**2. Download models**">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Whether a sidecar is generated is determined by the document content**: the parser only writes the corresponding file when the document actually contains tables / images / equations.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;File processing configurations are provided for my-memo.[native-R!].docx.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- If no rule is available, the file content extraction falls back to `legacy`; if `legacy` also does not support the file extension, an error entry is added to the system and the uploaded file remains in the `INPUT` directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` is an `ObservableAddonParams` field; it can be **modified at runtime**:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Create the docling working directory&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This is the only signal of modality availability — the engine does not need to declare capabilities in meta. The `i`/`t`/`e` options only determine whether the next stage invokes the VLM for summarization analysis on already-existing sidecars.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;File processing configurations are provided for my-proposal.[-!].docx.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- At most one of F/R/V/P may appear; repeating the same option has effect only once but does not raise an error.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After modification, **subsequent enqueues** get the new defaults; already-enqueued documents keep the snapshot from their enqueue moment (see the three layers of semantic guarantee in §3.3). This is tier 1 of §3.3's priority chain: &quot;`addon_params[&quot;chunker&quot;]` explicit value&quot;, winning everything.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Create the model mount directory&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- When parsing fails, the original file is not moved, making it easy to fix the configuration and re-process.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Parse queues are created dynamically from the registry's `ParserSpec.queue_group` (one registry snapshot per batch): the built-in native/mineru/docling each own a group, legacy shares the native pool (local, no network), and a third-party engine may declare its own group with a custom worker count (see `docs/ThirdPartyParser-zh.md`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Case-sensitive: the chunking options F/R/V/P must be uppercase; other options i/t/e must be lowercase.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;and &quot;Save As .docx&quot; in Word 2013+ to regenerate the ids.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Copy the existing models inside the container into the models directory&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- When `/documents/scan` encounters a file with the same name that is already `PROCESSED`, the input file is treated as already processed and moved to `__parsed__`, not enqueued as a new document.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At enqueue time, `resolve_stored_document_parser_engine` puts each document into the corresponding parse queue based on its `parser_engine` (from `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` defaults or the filename hint); the parse queues are completely non-blocking with respect to each other — mineru saturation does not slow down docling or native. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- If illegal characters appear inside the square brackets, the entire hint is invalidated, the engine follows the default rules, and the options fall back to `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` defaults or all defaults; a warning is also logged.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Package structure requirements** (the body is located by extension, not a fixed `text.markdown` name, so you can pack it with any zip tool): &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Download the equation recognition model&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After parsing, they enter `q_analyze` (multimodal analysis) uniformly, and then enter `q_process` (entity/relation extraction + ingest).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- When `/documents/scan` finds multiple files that share the same canonicalized name in the same scan, it prefers the file with a supported engine hint to respect the user's engine selection; if no variant has a hint, it processes the first file in sorted order. Other variants emit warnings and are moved to `__parsed__`, avoiding files in the same batch overwriting each other.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `P` is only effective for structured `LightRAG Document` results extracted by `native`;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- File-reference images embedded by relative path are resolved relative to the bundle root and **may live in any subdirectory** (not only `assets/`); directory traversal is forbidden (`..`, absolute paths, or references escaping the bundle root are skipped with a warning), and the resolved bytes must pass an image magic-byte check or they are skipped. Relative-path images in a standalone `.md` (not a textpack) are not resolved (skipped with a warning). &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**3. Create `docker-compose.yaml`**">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- When duplicate content hashes are found during scanning or parsing, the input file is likewise moved to `__parsed__`; this `doc_status` entry is kept as `FAILED duplicate` for tracking.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Environment variable | Default | Effect | Tuning advice |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Computes embeddings of adjacent sentences, which helps in understanding the context and relationships between sentences.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- SVG images (base64 / textpack file / downloaded) are rasterized to PNG via cairosvg before being written to the sidecar; if cairosvg is unavailable or rendering fails, the image is skipped (with a warning). &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Create `docker-compose.yaml` in the `docling` directory from the previous step, with the following contents:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- File moves only act on the current input file and do not overwrite or move existing document source files. If a file with the same name already exists at the destination, the system automatically appends `_001`, `_002`, etc., e.g., `report.pdf` is archived as `report_001.pdf`, `report_002.pdf`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Several key points:**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Semantic breakpoints are determined based on the specified threshold strategy.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- External URL images (`![](http://...)`) are **downloaded and embedded by default** (`NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_DOWNLOAD_ENABLED` defaults to `true`); a drawing is always emitted (the fetched asset on success, or an external-link fallback on failure). Downloading allows only globally-routable public IPs (both DNS-resolved IPs and every redirect target are checked, and the socket dials the validated IP directly to defeat DNS rebinding; any ambient `HTTP(S)_PROXY` is ignored); private / loopback / link-local / reserved / CGNAT (`100.64.0.0/10`) ranges are all rejected. To allow specific internal ranges, configure a CIDR allowlist via `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_ALLOWED_NON_PUBLIC_CIDRS`. Set the flag to `false` to instead drop external images entirely (no drawing emitted, so a document whose only images are external links produces no `drawings.json`). &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then execute `docker compose up -d` in that directory to start the service.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `mineru` engine writes the complete artifacts returned by the MinerU service (`content_list.json` + optional `full.md` / `middle.json` / `layout.pdf` / `images/`, etc.) into the `__parsed__/&lt;canonical filename&gt;.mineru_raw/` directory during parsing, and writes `_manifest.json` as the integrity validation file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. Parsing stage is isolated per engine**, so when mixing native/mineru/docling, you don't have to worry about a slow engine dragging another down.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Any semantic chunk exceeding `chunk_token_size` is automatically split by R.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `LIGHTRAG_FORCE_REPARSE_NATIVE` (default `false`): discard the `.native_raw/` cache and re-download external images over the network. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After the container is ready, set the following in LightRAG's `.env`:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Design goals:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. mineru / docling default to 2**: both have high resource usage, so the default keeps parallelism modest. Lower to 1 when resources are tight (OOM / VRAM contention / failure retry); with multi-GPU or a dedicated parser server, you can raise them manually.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This ensures that the `SemanticChunker` does not produce overlapping chunks.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_DOWNLOAD_ENABLED` (default `true`): the master switch for external-image downloading; set to `false` to drop all external images. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This enables LightRAG to recognize equations in documents via the local docling-serve and output them in LaTeX form.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text does not provide any explicit entities or relationships related to 'R separator cascade', 'ordered from strongest to weakest semantic boundary', 'English `.?!`', or 'Chinese / mixed Chinese-English documents split at semantic boundaries' as these are part of the default settings for the system.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` doubles as worker pool size and semaphore cap**: the pipeline creates a `Semaphore(max_parallel_insert)`, and each process worker also takes the semaphore before extraction and ingest. So even if you manually raise the worker count, the actual concurrency cap is still bounded by this value — just tune it directly.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Paragraph chunking is the native method for processing.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The remaining download / size / SSRF variables (`NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT` / `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_DOWNLOAD_REQUIRED` / `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_MAX_BYTES` / `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_MAX_SVG_PIXELS` / `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_ALLOWED_NON_PUBLIC_CIDRS`) — their meanings and defaults are listed in [env.example](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/blob/main/env.example) at the repository root. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Processing options control the behavior of a single file with respect to multimodal analysis, knowledge graph construction, and text chunking.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Avoid duplicate uploads. When parsing the same file again, the source file's content hash + size is first validated against `_manifest.json`; on hit, the MinerU service call is skipped and the local `content_list.json` is fed directly through adapter → SidecarWriter.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;4. Queue size and backpressure**: the small default `QUEUE_SIZE_INSERT=4` is intentional — the process stage is slow and memory-hungry; when the queue fills, analyze blocks, and backpressure reaches the parse stage, preventing thousands of parsing results from piling up in memory at once.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It strictly avoids mixing content from different headings.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Downloaded external images are cached in `&lt;file&gt;.native_raw/` (beside `.parsed/`, analogous to `.mineru_raw`/`.docling_raw`), reused directly when re-parsing the same unchanged file instead of going back over the network; the cache is invalidated when the source content or the size / SVG-pixel / CIDR options above change. When the document is deleted (with &quot;also delete file&quot; checked in the delete dialog), this cache directory is removed together with `.parsed/`. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MANY knowledge fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d682b153512aa160e070210c1816855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Preserve diagnostic information. When MinerU parses incorrectly or downstream sidecar fields are abnormal, you can go straight to `*.mineru_raw(&quot;hyper-relation&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;5. How changes take effect**: all parameters are passed in via `.env` (or environment variables), read once at `LightRAG` construction; restart the service after changing them.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Overlap can be preserved if the body under the same heading is too long.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `official` mode: uses MinerU's cloud API v4 service. You need to register an account at the [MinerU official website](https://mineru.net/) and create an API-KEY first. Then add the following configuration to LightRAG's `.env` file: &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;the queue fills, analyze blocks, and backpressure reaches the parse stage, preventing thousands of parsing results from piling up in memory at once.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text discusses various parameters and configurations related to chunking in a system, such as `CHUNK_V_SIZE`, `CHUNK_V_BREAKPOINT_THRESHOLD_TYPE`, and `CHUNK_P_SIZE` among others.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Typical tuning scenarios:**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">13.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Bridging text between tables can be included in the chunking process.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MINERU_API_MODE=official &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">21.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**How changes take effect**: all parameters are passed in via `.env` (or environment variables), read once at `LightRAG` construction; restart the service after changing them.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text explains how the chunking slots are resolved by a specificity-ordered chain, with explicit values taking precedence over strategy-specific env values, and so on.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Large batch of PDFs + local MinerU on a single GPU: `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU=2`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This method is specific to `lightrag` content in the sidecar directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MINERU_API &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Large batch of PDFs + local MinerU on a single GPU: `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU=2`, `MAX_PARALLEL_ANALYZE=5`, `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=3` (defaults are fine; lower MINERU to 1 if VRAM is tight).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text gives an example of how the resolution chain works, using `CHUNK_R_OVERLAP_SIZE=42` and `LightRAG(chunk_overlap_token_size=2)`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=3` when running on a cloud service with limited quotas: `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=3`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If `lightrag` content is not present, the method degrades to using `R`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Many knowlege fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9de68fb6438d36191c59a2bd51dc2410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Large batch of PDFs + MinerU cloud service: `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU=3~5` (depending on cloud quota), others at defaults.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text explains the special case for P's `chunk_token_size`, which does not walk the full four-tier chain and directly resolves via `CHUNK_P_SIZE` env &gt; `DEFAULT_CHUNK_P_SIZE` (2000).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Increase `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` to 10 when processing very large batches of documents: `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT=10`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `P` method produces fewer overlapping chunks than `R` or `F`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9d304dd05997f1c95abd0c1b7c76746</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;field is filled in.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">3.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Pure docx / txt (only native): `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE=10`; `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` derived from `MAX_ASYNC_LLM/3`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text emphasizes that `CHUNK_F_SIZE` / `CHUNK_R_SIZE` / `CHUNK_V_SIZE` work differently from `CHUNK_P_SIZE` because when unset, they fall back to the top-level `chunk_token_size` (F is the default global window, R prefers a smaller target to better split sentences, while V typically wants to be enlarged to reduce over-splitting).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
