<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAG SERVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SERVICE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Instructions for starting the LightRAG Server are provided.&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG Server loads environment variables from the `.env` file into the system environment variables on startup, and system environment variables take precedence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nginx is used as a reverse proxy in front of LightRAG Server to handle large file uploads."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is designed to provide a Web UI and API support. It facilitates document indexing, knowledge graph exploration, and a simple RAG query interface. It also provides an Ollama-compatible interface for AI chat bots to access LightRAG easily."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is recommended to be configured with environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is started with the command `docker compose up`, which can run in the background with the `-d` parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server requires specific settings to be configured before starting.&lt;SEP&gt;"The document is organized from the perspective of LightRAG Server deployment and use."&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG Server is a server that requires Nginx to configure `client_max_body_size` for the `/documents/upload` endpoint to handle large file uploads."&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG Server loads environment variables from the `.env` file."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server can be accessed without authentication by default, but can be secured with an API Key or account credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is a software application that requires configuration using environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is designed to provide a Web UI and API support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server is recommended to be configured using environment variables."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server operates in 'Gunicorn + Uvicorn' preload mode.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server supports two operational modes: Uvicorn and Gunicorn + Uvicorn.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server provides the REST API for integrating LightRAG into projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28550335f56f105359c1f2c45cf572d1</data>
</node>
