<node id="&quot;MINERU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARSER"</data>
  <data key="d4">MINERU is a comprehensive document parser that forms an integral part of the LightRAG document processing pipeline. It is designed to handle a wide array of file formats, including PDFs, Microsoft Office documents, various image formats, and more. MINERU operates as an external content extraction engine, which necessitates the service to be running and the appropriate endpoint/token to be configured within the LightRAG system. This engine is utilized locally on a single GPU for processing large batches of PDFs and is capable of handling configurations for parameters such as `page_range`, `language`, and `local_parse_method`.

MINERU shares similarities in semantics with the LightRAG, particularly in the handling of `engine_version` and `endpoint_signature` checks, adhering to the 'either side empty → skip' rule. It supports only the `mineru` and `docling` engines for accepting engine parameters. Additionally, MINERU is equipped with the ability to invalidate cache and re-parse file content upon subsequent uploads of the same file, ensuring that the most up-to-date information is processed.

The parser's functionality is further extended by its support for structured output, which can produce a `.blocks.jsonl` sidecar. This structured output is achieved through the P strategy, which is particularly valid for MINERU's heading-driven structural splitting. MINERU detects headings by examining an item's `text_level` or `label`, identifying them as `title` or `section_header`, and maintains the parent chain using a heading_stack.

The system ensures that the original file is preserved first for parsing, and it enqueues files for processing using paths such as `native`, `mineru`, and `docling`. It is configured to parse `pdf`, `office`, and various image files for multimodal processing, with `my-proposal` set to use MINERU with default processing options. The `mineru` parser is specifically used for extracting content from PDFs, and it supports a broad range of file formats for comprehensive document processing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-502fd83a7f153d429f3536ae34c05bb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
