<node id="&quot;HEADING LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy prevents long-block re-splitting by considering table-row boundaries and heading levels, maintaining the structure of the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy utilizes heading levels and `parent_headings` to maintain hierarchy information, which is often underused by other methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"`native` recognizes Heading levels 1–9 (inferred from `pPr/outlineLvl` or the style inheritance chain), feeding the `P` chunking strategy's heading-based splitting. The recognized headings are written to the `blocks.jsonl` sidecar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
