<node id="&quot;READ–DECIDE–WRITE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Read-decide-write combinations cannot interleave with other writers.&lt;SEP&gt;"Read-decide-write process must not interleave with other writers to prevent stale view-based classification decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EQUATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ELEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`native` recognizes OMML → LaTeX, distinguishing block-level vs inline. The recognized equations are written to the `equations.json` sidecar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANALYSIS RESULT DIRECTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DIRECTORY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Structured parsing results are written into the analysis result directory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;F (FORWARD) CHUNKING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The F (forward) chunking strategy is one of the methods used to divide text into chunks, typically processing the text in the order it appears.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;_MANIFEST.JSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `_manifest.json` file is written as the integrity validation file during parsing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The conditions for invalidating `_manifest.json` and triggering a cache miss are listed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file's hash and size are validated against `_manifest.json` to avoid duplicate uploads and conversions."&lt;SEP&gt;"`_manifest.json` is used to record invalidation conditions that trigger a cache miss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FILE_PATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `file_path` parameter in the `insert_text` function refers to a path to a file, which is necessary for the system to access text data.&lt;SEP&gt;"file_path is a field that contains the basename of the filename without directory.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6c748ee608ace11e7d348ea0448f352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-EXTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The purpose of this process is to re-extract the file, allowing for "fix the source file, scan again" to take effect.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLASSIFICATION DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Classification decisions cannot be based on a stale view.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PNG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `png` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANONICALIZED FILENAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE NAME"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The canonicalized filename is used for the analysis result directory name."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_F_OVERLAP_SIZE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `CHUNK_F_OVERLAP_SIZE` environment variable provides a specific overlap setting for the F (forward) chunking strategy when no other overlap setting is defined.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOURCE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Source file is fixed and scanned again.&lt;SEP&gt;"Source file size or sha256 does not match the manifest, triggering a cache miss."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file remains in `INPUT/` for non-PROCESSED records with `full_docs` present.&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file size or sha256 must match the manifest to avoid a cache miss."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file stays at its original location.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-742706ba2caa2b3584f3a7dd55c34a82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASENAME OF THE FILENAME (WITHOUT DIRECTORY)">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DESCRIPTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"file_path contains the basename of the filename without directory.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-821452c2e57f78506ae365dc36678fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDINARY UPLOAD AND CORE ENQUEUE APIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"API"</data>
  <data key="d4">"For ordinary upload and core enqueue APIs, the process requires deletion of the old document record before re-upload or re-enqueue.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCAN ENDPOINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Scan endpoint rejects when certain conditions are present.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JPEG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `jpeg` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSED SUFFIX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE NAME"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `.parsed` suffix is added to the canonicalized filename."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRONGEST TO WEAKEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ORDER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The order of splitting is from the strongest to the weakest semantic boundaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEMO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The file memo is set to use the native-P engine as specified in the filename hint.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FILE_SOURCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A valid `file_source` is necessary for the text APIs to perform duplicate checks.&lt;SEP&gt;"Duplicates are checked by the basename of `file_source`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_R_SIZE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `CHUNK_R_SIZE` environment variable is used to define the `chunk_token_size` for the R (recursive) chunking strategy if this size is not otherwise specified.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHA256&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Source file size or sha256 is used to match with the manifest and trigger a cache miss if it does not match."&lt;SEP&gt;"The source file's sha256 must match the manifest to avoid a cache miss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Reservation is passed before saving the file.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `gif` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPORT.DOCX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE NAME"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The analysis results are written into `__parsed__/report.docx.parsed/` for `report.docx`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGLISH PUNCTUATION MARKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"English punctuation marks like `.?!` are used for splitting text in the default settings.&lt;SEP&gt;"The system does not include literal matching of English punctuation marks in the default settings.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIVE-P&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CHUNKING STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunking strategy native-P is used for the document my-proposal.docx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The file memo is set to use the native-P engine as specified in the filename hint.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASENAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The basename of `file_source` is used for checking duplicates.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;R (RECURSIVE) CHUNKING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The R (recursive) chunking strategy involves recursively dividing the text into smaller segments, which can be more complex and potentially more granular than other strategies.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINERU_ENGINE_VERSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"VARIABLE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `MINERU_ENGINE_VERSION` environment variable must be consistent with the `engine_version` recorded in the manifest to avoid a cache miss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TWO-PASS CHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A two-pass check is required before saving the file.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BMP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `bmp` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPORT.[NATIVE].DOCX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE NAME"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The analysis results are written into `__parsed__/report.docx.parsed/` for `report.[native].docx`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The use of English punctuation marks is part of the default settings for the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Notes on the `include_chunk_content` parameter and its behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"The file notes is set to use the -R engine with chunking parameters chunk_ts=800 and chunk_ol=80 as specified in the filename hint.&lt;SEP&gt;"The rule specifies the file notes to use the -R engine with chunking parameters chunk_ts=800 and chunk_ol=80.&lt;SEP&gt;"The notes provide additional information about the include_chunk_content parameter and its behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"The table includes notes on the file format.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;400&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"HTTP STATUS CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Lacking a valid `file_source` returns 400 directly.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_R_OVERLAP_SIZE ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `CHUNK_R_OVERLAP_SIZE` environment variable is used to provide a specific overlap setting for the R (recursive) chunking strategy when no other overlap setting is defined.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGINE_VERSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The 'either side empty → skip' rule for `engine_version` is the same as in MinerU §4.3."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `engine_version` is used to validate `DOCLING_ENGINE_VERSION` and trigger a cache miss if they do not match."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `engine_version` recorded in the manifest must be consistent with the `MINERU_ENGINE_VERSION` environment variable to avoid a cache miss."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `split_option` object may contain `engine_version` metadata from the parsing engine.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INPUT DIRECTORY SCAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Input directory scan is performed to canonicalize the basename and check for existing variants, resulting in a 409 error if a match is found.&lt;SEP&gt;"Input directory scan is performed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `tiff` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAG DOCUMENT BLOCKS FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The LightRAG Document blocks file is named with the canonicalized filename stem."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LITERAL MATCHING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"English punctuation marks are excluded from literal matching to prevent mis-splitting.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;-R&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ENGINE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The file notes is set to use the -R engine with chunking parameters chunk_ts=800 and chunk_ol=80 as specified in the filename hint.&lt;SEP&gt;"The rule specifies the file notes to use the -R engine with chunking parameters chunk_ts=800 and chunk_ol=80.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SDK PATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The SDK path allows calls to `insert` / `ainsert` / `apipeline_enqueue_documents` without `file_paths`.&lt;SEP&gt;"The SDK path calls `insert` / `ainsert` / `apipeline_enqueue_documents` without `file_paths`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_R_SEPARATORS ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `CHUNK_R_SEPARATORS` environment variable is a JSON array string that lists separators for the R (recursive) chunking strategy, indicating where text should be split.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;API_MODE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `api_mode` recorded in the manifest must be consistent with the `MINERU_API_MODE` to avoid a cache miss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOC_STATUS CHECK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Doc status check is performed to ensure no duplicate entries exist, resulting in a 409 error if a match is found.&lt;SEP&gt;"Doc status check is performed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEBP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `webp` format for image export details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIDECARS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `native` engine writes recognized structures to the corresponding sidecars. It supports `docx` and `md` extensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sidecars are named with the canonicalized filename stem."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHINESE AND MIXED CHINESE-ENGLISH DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT_TYPE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The system splits Chinese and mixed Chinese-English documents at semantic boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MY-PROPOSAL.[NATIVE-IET].DOCX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"File processing configuration is provided for my-proposal.[native-iet].docx.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3219553e6504cf126a5429743398bc71</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSERT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The SDK path calls `insert`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c5bff8f2fe6a621cc9a6ced39ccfaf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JSON ARRAY STRING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A JSON array string is a formatted string that represents an array of values in JSON format, which is commonly used to store and exchange data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT is a configuration parameter that specifies the endpoint for the MinerU API. "&lt;SEP&gt;"MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT is set to 'https://mineru.net', indicating the official endpoint for MinerU parser.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT` must be consistent with the `endpoint_signature` recorded in the manifest to avoid a cache miss."&lt;SEP&gt;"The configuration sets MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT to `https://mineru.net`."&lt;SEP&gt;"The configuration uses the default endpoint `https://mineru.net` for the MinerU official service.&lt;SEP&gt;"The environment variable 'MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT' is used to set the official endpoint for MinerU.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e2827f0656f23647a5ad5b252099d6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAVE THE FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The file is saved after checks pass.&lt;SEP&gt;"The file is saved after passing the two-pass check, scheduling a background task to enqueue and process the file.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Embedded images are exported to a `&lt;base&gt;.blocks.assets/` directory beside `blocks.jsonl`, supporting `emf` format for image export details. EMF/WMF (and the previews of OLE objects such as Visio) can currently only be "extracted to disk" and cannot enter multimodal analysis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANONICALIZED FILENAME STEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
