<node id="&quot;POSITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Content typically contains the original paragraph positions "&lt;SEP&gt;"The `positions` field is an array of `position` objects that identify the layout position of the text block.&lt;SEP&gt;"The affected blocks' `positions` degrade to `[{"type": "paraid", "range": null}]` when some paragraphs lack paraId. native docx collects the `w14:paraId` written by Word 2013+ as a paragraph-level provenance anchor. This is only a notice and does not affect parsing success. If precise paragraph provenance is needed, regenerate ids by saving the file in Word 2013+ to regenerate ids."&lt;SEP&gt;"The positions array is used to identify the original location of content in the file.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
