<node id="&quot;DOCKER COMPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOOL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Docker Compose is recommended for installation with plugins.&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker Compose is the most convenient way to deploy and run the LightRAG Server."&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker Compose is used for deploying the LightRAG Server.&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker Compose is used for deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker Compose is used to deploy and run the LightRAG Server, which is the most convenient way to do so.&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker compose is a command used to manage multi-container Docker applications. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Restart the API service using docker compose with -f compose.yaml --profile api up -d.&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'docker compose' command is used to manage Docker containers for a remote LLM, local embedding, and rerank setup.&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'docker compose' is used to manage multi-container Docker applications.&lt;SEP&gt;"Docker Compose is used to launch multiple LightRAG instances by specifying unique `WORKSPACE` and `PORT` environment variables for each container in the `docker-compose.yml` file, ensuring independent configurations for each instance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cedc79909a2121d28e3444802703cf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
