</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios. It outlines key principles and installation scenarios for end users, contributors, and for testing package builds. It also describes how to create distribution packages and the automated release process through GitHub Actions. The guide provides a quick reference for different scenarios and instructions for Bun installation. The file structure of the project is outlined, and troubleshooting steps are provided for common issues with the installation and building process. The document ends with a summary indicating the completion of the guide.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Yes. The build scripts (`dev`, `build`, `preview`, `lint`) are runtime-agnostic and work with both Bun and Node.js/npm:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92a537a957f50ee447215475d9dc5bba</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use `pip install -e &quot;.[api]&quot;` for development&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92a537a957f50ee447215475d9dc5bba</data>
</node>
