<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios. It outlines key principles and installation scenarios for end users, contributors, and for testing package builds. It also describes how to create distribution packages and the automated release process through GitHub Actions. The guide provides a quick reference for different scenarios and instructions for Bun installation. The file structure of the project is outlined, and troubleshooting steps are provided for common issues with the installation and building process. The document ends with a summary indicating the completion of the guide. The guide emphasizes the importance of the frontend build process and its role in the project's functionality and distribution. It also highlights the use of Git and PyPI for version control and distribution, respectively. Additionally, it mentions the role of contributors in the development process and the need for a clean and efficient build process to ensure the project's quality and maintainability.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FILE STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The File Structure of the LightRAG project describes the organization of files and directories within the project. This is important for contributors and users to understand how the project is structured and where to find specific files.&lt;SEP&gt;"The File Structure section outlines the directory and file organization within the LightRAG project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIP INSTALL -E &quot;.[API]&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Contributors can install the package in editable mode without building the frontend, which is optional and can be done later."&lt;SEP&gt;"Use this command for development to install the package in editable mode without building the frontend.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NPM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOOL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A package manager that can be used instead of Bun.&lt;SEP&gt;"A package manager that is fully supported.&lt;SEP&gt;"npm is a tool that can be used instead of Bun.&lt;SEP&gt;"npm is fully supported.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92a537a957f50ee447215475d9dc5bba</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL INSTALLATION (TESTING PACKAGE BUILD)">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"USER TYPE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Normal Installation for testing package build. Frontend must be built before installation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal Installation is for testing the package build process, requiring the frontend to be built before installation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GITHUB ACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"GitHub Actions are automated workflows that can be triggered on various events, such as code commits or pull requests. They are used in the LightRAG project to automate the release process, including building the frontend and publishing the package to PyPI.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FROM PYPI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"USER TYPE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"End Users can install from PyPI. The command is `pip install lightrag-hku[api]`. Frontend is included and no building is required after installation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PYPI USERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"GROUP"</data>
  <data key="d4">"No action needed, frontend included for PyPI users.&lt;SEP&gt;"Users of PyPI who do not need to take any action as the frontend is included.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92a537a957f50ee447215475d9dc5bba</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GIT REPOSITORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Frontend build results are NOT included in Git Repository (kept clean)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Git Repository is the primary location for the LightRAG project's source code. It is used for version control and collaboration among developers. The repository is designed to keep the codebase clean by not including frontend build results, which are separate from the source code.&lt;SEP&gt;"The Git Repository is where the project is stored and managed. The frontend build results are not included in this repository, ensuring a clean codebase."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIP INSTALL -E &quot;.[API]&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The command to install the package in editable mode for development.&lt;SEP&gt;"pip install -e ".[api]" is a command for development to install a package.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92a537a957f50ee447215475d9dc5bba</data>
</node>
