<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The setup wizard helps you configure LightRAG in three parts: `env-base` sets up the LLM, embedding model, and optional reranker; `env-storage` adds or changes storage backends such as PostgreSQL, Neo4j, Redis, Milvus, Qdrant, MongoDB, or Memgraph; `env-server` sets server host and port, WebUI labels, authentication, API keys, and SSL.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RERANKER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS OPTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Optional reranker configuration is available for reranking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Optional reranker is set up in `env-base`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENV-BACKUP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`make env-backup` is a command to create a backup of the LightRAG setup."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
