  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"SSL is set up in `env-server`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAKE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The command 'make' is used to compile or build in the context of this document.&lt;SEP&gt;"The wizard is accessed through `make` commands."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONGO_URI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARAMETER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The MONGO_URI parameter is used for hosting-side connections with MongoDB.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e8030e636243c7d9ef84975499293ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAKE ENV-STORAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The 'make env-storage' command is used to add storage capabilities to the environment after the base setup.&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'make env-storage' is used to add storage after the base setup."&lt;SEP&gt;"The command 'make env-storage' is used to add storage to the environment setup.&lt;SEP&gt;"`make env-storage` requires an existing `.env`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCKER DEPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Details beyond the interactive wizard are provided for Docker deployment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONGOVECTORDBSTORAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STORAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"MongoVectorDBStorage adds a workspace prefix to the collection name for data isolation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MongoVectorDBStorage requires Atlas Search / Vector Search support to operate correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;"MongoVectorDBStorage is used for vector storage in MongoDB.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e8030e636243c7d9ef84975499293ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STORAGE BACKENDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE PACKAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LightRAG dynamically installs packages for storage backends, such as `redis`, `neo4j`, `pymilvus`, `pymongo`, `asyncpg`, `qdrant-client`."&lt;SEP&gt;"Storage backends like PostgreSQL, Neo4j, Redis, Milvus, Qdrant, MongoDB, or Memgraph are set up in `env-storage`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERACTIVE SETUP WIZARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The interactive setup wizard can generate a configured `.env` file.&lt;SEP&gt;"The interactive setup wizard guides you through the configuration of LightRAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"Use the interactive setup wizard instead of editing `env.example` by hand.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONGODB+SRV:// ATLAS CLUSTER URI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DATABASE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An Atlas cluster URI is a specific type of external endpoint for MONGO_URI.&lt;SEP&gt;"An Atlas cluster URI is an example of an external endpoint.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e8030e636243c7d9ef84975499293ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPOSITORY ROOT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
