<node id="&quot;LLM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LLM (Language Learning Model) is set up in `env-base`."&lt;SEP&gt;"LightRAG supports binding to various LLM backends.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM used by Open WebUI is responsible for generating session titles and keywords.&lt;SEP&gt;"The bottleneck of document indexing speed mainly lies with the LLM, which can be accelerated by increasing the concurrency level of the LLM."&lt;SEP&gt;"The performance bottleneck of document indexing is often the LLM, which can be improved by increasing concurrency levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open WebUI uses an LLM (Large Language Model) for session title and session keyword generation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;"Open WebUI uses an LLM to perform session title and session keyword generation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM (Large Language Model) can answer questions based on the chat history using the `/bypass` prefix.&lt;SEP&gt;"The equation objects are analyzed by an LLM.&lt;SEP&gt;"The table objects are analyzed by an LLM.&lt;SEP&gt;"The text is fed to the LLM for entity/relation extraction. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Lower-cost models are recommended for extraction, while stronger models are suggested for final answers. Vision-language models are recommended for multimodal analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"LLM is used for entity extraction, relationship extraction, entity summarization, relationship summarization, claim extraction, and community report generation in Standard GraphRAG."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082eb07a755d44999510e8f240806102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</node>
