<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Many knowlege fragments with entities were missed in the last extraction. Add them below using the same format.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To change the default value of the enable_rerank parameter to false, set the following environment variable: RERANK_BY_DEFAULT=False&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After starting the lightrag-server, you can add an Ollama-type connection in the Open WebUI admin panel. And then a model named `lightrag:latest` will appear in Open WebUI's model management interface.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;By default, the /query and /query/stream endpoints return references with only reference_id and file_path. For evaluation, debugging, or citation purposes, you can request the actual retrieved chunk content to be included in references&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Users can then send queries to LightRAG through the chat interface. You should install LightRAG as a service for this use case.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The content field is an array of strings, where each string represents a chunk from the same file. A single file may correspond to multiple chunks, so the content is returned as a list to preserve chunk boundaries&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Open WebUI uses an LLM to do the session title and session keyword generation task. So the Ollama chat completion API detects and forwards OpenWebUI session-related requests directly to the underlying LLM.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">23.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Example API Request:{&quot;query&quot;:&quot;What is LightRAG?&quot;,&quot;mode&quot;:&quot;mix&quot;,&quot;include_references&quot;:true,&quot;include_chunk_content&quot;:true}&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Screenshot from Open WebUI:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Example Response (with chunk content):{&quot;response&quot;:&quot;LightRAG is a graph-based RAG system...&quot;,&quot;references&quot;:[{&quot;reference_id&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;file_path&quot;:&quot;/documents/intro.md&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[&quot;LightRAG is a retrieval-augmented generation system that combines knowledge graphs with vector similarity search...&quot;,&quot;The system uses a dual-indexing approach with both vector embeddings and graph structures for enhanced retrieval...&quot;]},{&quot;reference_id&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;file_path&quot;:&quot;/documents/features.md&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[&quot;The system provides multiple query modes including local, global, hybrid, and mix modes...&quot;]}]&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The default query mode is `hybrid` if you send a message (query) from the Ollama interface of LightRAG. You can select query mode by sending a message with a query prefix.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Notes:&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This parameter only works when include_references=true.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Setting include_chunk_content=true without including references has no effect.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Breaking Change: Prior versions returned content as a single concatenated string. Now it returns an array of strings to preserve individual chunk boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;A query prefix in the query string can determine which LightRAG query mode is used to generate the response for the query. The supported prefixes include:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The examples below are reference snippets for tuning existing deployments. For a first run, follow Progressive Setup Recipes instead of copying the entire env.example file by hand.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For example, the chat message `/mix What's LightRAG?` will trigger a mix mode query for LightRAG. A chat message without a query prefix will trigger a hybrid mode query by default.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For a first run, follow Progressive Setup Recipes instead of copying the entire env.example file by hand.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/bypass` is not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell the API Server to pass the query directly to the underlying LLM, including the chat history. So the user can use the LLM to answer questions based on the chat history.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# HOST=0.0.0.0&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If you are using Open WebUI as a front end, you can just switch the model to a normal LLM instead of using the `/bypass` prefix.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;PORT=9621&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">19.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/context` is also not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell LightRAG to return only the context information prepared for the LLM. You can check the context if it's what you want, or process the context by yourself.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;WORKERS=2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When using LightRAG for content queries, avoid combining the search process with unrelated output processing, as this significantly impacts query effectiveness. User prompt is specifically designed to address this issue — it does not participate in the RAG retrieval phase, but rather guides the LLM on how to process the retrieved results after the query is completed.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# LIGHTRAG_API_PREFIX=/site01&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We can append square brackets to the query prefix to provide the LLM with the user prompt:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ENTITY_EXTRACTION_USE_JSON=true&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">19.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For example, the chat message `[Use mermaid format for diagrams] Please draw a character relationship diagram for Scrooge` will trigger a mix mode query for LightRAG with the user prompt included.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE=entity_type_prompt.yml&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;By default, the LightRAG Server can be accessed without any authentication. We can configure the server with an API Key or account credentials to secure it.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
