  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MAX_ASYNC_LLM=4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;TOKEN_EXPIRE_HOURS=4">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_BINDING=openai&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">33.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Passwords without a prefix are treated as plaintext. To store a bcrypt password, prefix the generated hash with `{bcrypt}`. The easiest way to generate a value that can be pasted directly into `AUTH_ACCOUNTS` is:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;lightrag-hash-password --username admin">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_BINDING_HOST=https://api.openai.com/v1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">33.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The command prompts for the password and prints an `admin:{bcrypt}...` entry ready to paste into `.env'.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_BINDING_API_KEY=your-api-key&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Currently, only the configuration of an administrator account and password is supported. A comprehensive account system is yet to be developed and implemented.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;KEYWORD_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If Account credentials are not configured, the Web UI will access the system as a Guest. Therefore, even if only an API Key is configured, all APIs can still be accessed through the Guest account, which remains insecure. Hence, to safeguard the API, it is necessary to configure both authentication methods simultaneously.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;QUERY_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Azure OpenAI API can be created using the following commands in Azure CLI (you need to install Azure CLI first from [https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli)):">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;RERANK_TIMEOUT=&lt;empty&gt;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
