</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After modifying the `.env` file, a new terminal session must be opened for the changes to take effect, as the server loads environment variables at startup.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Below are the command line options for the LightRAG API Server:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# RERANK_TIMEOUT=30&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server. There is an example environment variable file named `env.example` in the root directory of the project. Please copy this file to the startup directory and rename it to `.env`. After that, you can modify the parameters related to the LLM and Embedding models in the `.env` file. It is important to note that the LightRAG Server will load the environment variables from `.env`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;System environment variables take precedence over the `.env` file settings when the server starts, ensuring that system-wide configurations can override local ones.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For example, setting the `--host` and `--port` options will define the server's host and port:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_MODEL=bge-m3:latest&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Web UI facilitates document indexing, knowledge graph exploration, and a simple RAG query interface. Document indexing is the process of organizing and storing documents in a way that makes them easily searchable. Knowledge graph exploration allows users to navigate and interact with the structured knowledge stored in the server. The RAG query interface provides a simple and intuitive way to retrieve information from the indexed documents. These functionalities are essential for the server to serve its purpose effectively, enabling users to quickly find the information they need. The Web UI is designed to be user-friendly, with a clean and intuitive interface that makes it easy for users to navigate and perform tasks. The simplicity of the RAG query interface is particularly noteworthy, as it allows even non-technical users to perform complex searches without difficulty. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;During startup, the server loads the environment variables from the `.env` file into the system environment variables, affecting the server's configuration.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For detailed information on supported storage options, please refer to the storage section in the README.md file located in the root directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_DIM=1024&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG Server also provides an Ollama-compatible interface, aiming to emulate LightRAG as an Ollama chat model. This compatibility is achieved by implementing a set of APIs and protocols that allow the server to communicate with Ollama chat models. This enables the server to be used in scenarios where Ollama chat models are required, such as in customer service or educational applications. The Ollama-compatible interface is a significant step forward in making the LightRAG Server more accessible and versatile, as it opens up new possibilities for integration with other systems and services. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Running `make env-security-check` can audit the current `.env` file for security risks, ensuring that sensitive information is not exposed.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG now supports configurable index types for Milvus vector storage (AUTOINDEX, HNSW, HNSW_SQ, IVF_FLAT, etc.) through environment variables.&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_BINDING=ollama&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;API can be created using the following commands in Azure CLI (you need to install Azure CLI first from [https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli))">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;HNSW_SQ requires Milvus 2.6.8+ and provides significant memory savings.&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_BINDING_HOST=http://localhost:11434&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This allows AI chat bots, such as Open WebUI, to access LightRAG easily. The ease of access for AI chat bots is a testament to the server's design, which prioritizes user experience and ease of integration. This is particularly important in today's digital landscape, where the ability to quickly and easily integrate AI capabilities into existing systems is highly valued. The simplicity of the interface and the ease of use for AI chat bots are key factors in the server's appeal to developers and businesses looking to enhance their systems with AI capabilities. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Change the resource group name, location, and OpenAI resource name as needed">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;See the &quot;Using Milvus for Vector Storage&quot; section in the main README.md for complete configuration options.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# Optional asymmetric embedding for prefix-based models:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">18.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Review the [v1.5.0rc2 release notes](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/releases/tag/v1.5.0rc2) before upgrading a production instance. The release notes provide detailed information about the new features, changes, and potential issues that may arise during the upgrade process. It is essential for users to review these notes to ensure a smooth transition and to avoid any unexpected issues. The release notes are a valuable resource for users who want to stay informed about the latest updates and improvements to the LightRAG Server. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME=LightRAG">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">22.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At most one of `F`, `R`, `V`, and `P` should be selected for a file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC=true&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LOCATION=swedencentral">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text provides instructions on how to start the service and verify its health. This is done by running a command to start the Docker containers and another to check the service's status. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunker parameters are configured with `CHUNK_SIZE`, `CHUNK_OVERLAP_SIZE`, and strategy-specific variables such as `CHUNK_R_SEPARATORS`, `CHUNK_V_BREAKPOINT_THRESHOLD_TYPE`, `CHUNK_P_SIZE`, and `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">15.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To keep the old file-processing behavior while upgrading the server, set: `&lt;code&gt;LIGHTRAG_PARSER=*:legacy-F&lt;/code&gt;`. This setting ensures that the server continues to use the legacy file-processing behavior, which may be necessary for compatibility with existing systems or workflows. It is a simple and effective way to maintain the status quo while still taking advantage of the new features and improvements in the latest version of the server. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The purpose of setting max_tokens parameter is to truncate LLM output before timeouts occur, thereby preventing document extraction failures.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-280dedf626baee86fc0d61cdd836e6ac</data>
