  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. Start the appropriate backend service or confirm the hosted provider credentials 2. Start the RAG server 3. Upload some documents using the document management endpoints 4. Query the system using the query endpoints 5. Trigger document scan if new files are put into the inputs directory&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Keep v1.4-compatible behavior:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If you need to configure different LLMs/VLMs for entity extraction, keyword extraction, final answers, or multimodal analysis, see the [Role-Specific LLM/VLM Configuration Guide](./RoleSpecificLLMConfiguration.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">20.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The API Server can be configured in two ways (highest priority first):">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/health` endpoint reports operational state and selected configuration, including role LLM configuration, LLM/embedding/rerank queue status, workspace/storage workspace mapping, VLM enablement, rerank enablement, and pipeline busy/scanning/destructive status. It always returns HTTP 200 so it stays usable as a liveness probe, but the configuration and operational diagnostics are returned **only to authenticated callers** (valid JWT or `X-API-Key`). Unauthenticated callers receive only liveness signals (`status`, `auth_mode`, `core_version`, `api_version`, `pipeline_busy`/`pipeline_active`, and the WebUI title/availability fields — all of which are also exposed by the unauthenticated `/auth-status` endpoint or are plain booleans). Provide credentials to retrieve the full payload, e.g. `curl -H &quot;X-API-Key: &lt;key&gt;&quot; http://localhost:9621/health`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Recommended starting point without external parser services:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here are some examples of common settings for LLM and Embedding models:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Most of the configurations come with default settings; check out the details in the sample file: `.env.example`. Storage configuration should also be set through environment variables or the `.env` file.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG implements asynchronous document indexing to enable frontend monitoring and querying of document processing progress. Upon uploading files or inserting text through designated endpoints, a unique Track ID is returned to facilitate real-time progress monitoring.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# MINERU_API_MODE=official&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When targeting Google Gemini, set `LLM_BINDING=gemini`, choose a model such as `LLM_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest`, and provide your Gemini key via `LLM_BINDING_API_KEY` (or `GEMINI_API_KEY`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">19.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use environment variables `LLM_BINDING` or CLI argument `--llm-binding` to select the LLM backend type. Use environment variables `EMBEDDING_BINDING` or CLI argument `--embedding-binding` to select the Embedding backend type.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**API Endpoints Supporting Track ID Generation:**">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# MINERU_API_TOKEN=your_mineru_api_token&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Ollama LLM + Ollama Embedding:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Bedrock ignores `LLM_BINDING_API_KEY` and `EMBEDDING_BINDING_API_KEY`. Use SigV4 credentials through the AWS credential chain, or set the process-level `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` environment variable before startup for Bedrock API key / bearer-token auth:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">19.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Document Processing Status Query Endpoint:**">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">1.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# MINERU_OFFICIAL_ENDPOINT=https://mineru.net&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3-large is a document that includes several configuration options for a service called LightRAG. The configuration is detailed in various steps that pertain to different aspects of the service, including embedding dimensions, data storage, reranking, and deployment settings. This text seems to be a reference document for setting up and operating LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">10.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Important Note: The embedding model and asymmetric embedding configuration must be determined before document indexing, and the same settings must be used during the query phase. For certain storage solutions (e.g., PostgreSQL), the vector dimension must be defined upon initial table creation. When changing the embedding model, embedding dimension, `EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC`, query/document prefixes, or provider task behavior, clear the existing LightRAG workspace/vector data and re-index the source files.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_BINDING=bedrock">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This endpoint provides comprehensive status information including:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# MINERU_MODEL_VERSION=vlm&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The WebUI can be accessed after the service is started. Users can upload documents and run queries through the WebUI. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For the full validation rules and examples, see [Asymmetric Embedding Configuration](./AsymmetricEmbedding.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
