<node id="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STORAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Configuration commands are listed for OpenSearch, including the export of environment variables.&lt;SEP&gt;"Data isolation is achieved through index name prefixes for OpenSearch."&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch is a supported search and analytics engine by LightRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch is a supported storage solution by LightRAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"For OpenSearch, data isolation is achieved through index name prefixes."&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch is a supported storage solution by LightRAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"Graph traversal for OpenSearch is explained with details on the use of the `graphlookup` command and fallback mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;"Installation instructions are given for OpenSearch using Docker without plugins.&lt;SEP&gt;"Installation instructions with Docker Compose (recommended, with plugins) are given.&lt;SEP&gt;"Instructions for starting OpenSearch with Docker Compose are provided.&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch is a storage solution that provides unified support for LightRAG storage types (KV, Vector, Graph, DocStatus) and offers various search capabilities and scalability.&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch is required with version 3.x or higher and the k-NN plugin enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;"OpenSearch provides a unified storage solution for all four LightRAG storage types (KV, Vector, Graph, DocStatus). It offers native k-NN vector search, full-text search, and horizontal scalability without cloud-only restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;"Running a full OpenAI + OpenSearch demo is detailed, requiring an `OPENAI_API_KEY`.&lt;SEP&gt;"Running the OpenSearch storage demo is described with the necessary environment variables.&lt;SEP&gt;"Unit testing instructions using Python's pytest and mocks are provided.&lt;SEP&gt;"Verification steps to ensure the OpenSearch cluster is running are given.&lt;SEP&gt;"Visualization of the knowledge graph via LightRAG WebUI is explained with a configuration example.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPEN WEBUI ADMIN PANEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"INTERFACE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The Ollama-type connection is added in the Open WebUI admin panel, where the model `lightrag:latest` will appear in the model management interface."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ollama-type connection is added in the Open WebUI admin panel. It leads to the appearance of a model named `lightrag:latest` in the model management interface."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
