<node id="&quot;CONTENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Content typically contains the body text under that heading "&lt;SEP&gt;"Each element contains the chunk text "&lt;SEP&gt;"Internally the implementation uses content as temporary fields "&lt;SEP&gt;"Prior versions returned `content` as a single concatenated string, but now it returns an array of strings to preserve chunk boundaries. To get a single string, join the array elements with a separator like `"\n\n"`.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `content` field is an array of strings, representing chunks from the same file, with each chunk preserved as a separate string in the list to maintain boundaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"content is a field that returns an array of strings representing chunks from the same file."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `content` field contains the actual table data in a structured format.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `content` field contains the text content, with special handling for equations and images as placeholder tags, and headings rendered with markdown syntax.&lt;SEP&gt;"The content is part of the blockid computation. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6df28f5232d5c31b9f64164c61a08e65</data>
</node>
