</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONFIGURATION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Nginx needs to be configured with `client_max_body_size` for the `/documents/upload` endpoint."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `client_max_body_size` configuration setting is used to specify the maximum request body size that the server will accept."&lt;SEP&gt;"The configuration `client_max_body_size` is set to 100M for large file uploads in the `/documents/upload` endpoint."&lt;SEP&gt;"The configuration `client_max_body_size` is set to 8M for LLM queries with long context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS is commented out, indicating it is not set for optional VLM configuration settings."&lt;SEP&gt;"SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS is set to 2000, indicating the maximum number of trailing tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;"SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS is set to 2000, which is the maximum number of trailing tokens to consider for the VLM process.&lt;SEP&gt;"SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS is set to 2000.&lt;SEP&gt;"The parameter SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS is set to 2000.&lt;SEP&gt;"This is an environment variable that limits the number of trailing tokens in surrounding content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARAMETER "</data>
  <data key="d4">"client_max_body_size is a parameter that sets the maximum request body size allowed for incoming requests to the Nginx proxy. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE is a configuration in Settings for document indexing section."&lt;SEP&gt;"ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE should be used with a YAML profile stored under PROMPT_DIR/entity_type.&lt;SEP&gt;"ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE is commented out, indicating it is not set for document indexing settings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Use ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE instead of ENTITY_TYPES.&lt;SEP&gt;"entity_type_prompt_file is a file that contains entity type guidance and can be used to configure the entity extraction process. It is loaded from the directory specified by PROMPT_DIR or the default location if PROMPT_DIR is not set.&lt;SEP&gt;"entity_type_prompt_file is a file that loads an entity extraction prompt profile. The profile can define `entity_types_guidance`, `entity_extraction_examples`, and `entity_extraction_json_examples`. It is loaded from `${PROMPT_DIR:-./prompts}/entity_type`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c74b3a56df033faf9eedb477d804a55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOUR_API_KEY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LLM_BINDING_API_KEY is set to your_api_key in the example."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-280dedf626baee86fc0d61cdd836e6ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;413 REQUEST ENTITY TOO LARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ERROR"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Nginx will reject files larger than 1MB (the default limit) with a `413 Request Entity Too Large` error before the request reaches LightRAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `413 Request Entity Too Large` error is returned when the file exceeds the limit.&lt;SEP&gt;"Without the configuration, Nginx will return a `413 Request Entity Too Large` error for files larger than 1MB."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPENSEARCH STORAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STORAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"If you use OpenSearch storage and the cluster is older than OpenSearch 3.3.0, upgrade OpenSearch before enabling the v1.5 storage path and validate existing indices.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LightRAG Server uses OpenSearch storage and requires OpenSearch 3.3.0 or later for new deployments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
