<node id="&quot;ASYMMETRIC EMBEDDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Asymmetric embedding configuration is described in the section below.&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding for prefix-based models is optional."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding is an explicit opt-in feature.&lt;SEP&gt;"The Asymmetric Embedding Configuration section explains how to enable and configure asymmetric embeddings.&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding is a feature that must be explicitly enabled and requires certain backend support.&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding is an explicit opt-in feature that requires the selected embedding backend to support provider task parameters or task prefixes.&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding is an explicit opt-in feature.&lt;SEP&gt;"Asymmetric embedding is discussed in the section titled 'Asymmetric Embedding Configuration'."</data>
