  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Max tokens value can be calculated by this formula: `LLM_TIMEOUT * llm_output_tokens/second` (i.e. `240s * 50 tokens/s = 12000`, max_tokens should smaller than 12000)"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-280dedf626baee86fc0d61cdd836e6ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASYMMETRIC EMBEDDING CONFIGURATION DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The Asymmetric Embedding Configuration document contains validation rules and examples for asymmetric embedding.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;--PORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"COMMAND-LINE PARAMETER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Command-line parameter for server listening port."&lt;SEP&gt;"Command-line parameter for specifying the server's port number.&lt;SEP&gt;"command-line parameter that specifies the server listening port (default: 9621)</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The v1.5.0rc2 release adds the new file-processing pipeline, parser routing, multimodal analysis, role-specific LLM/VLM configuration, JSON entity extraction, and several provider/storage changes.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;During startup, configurations in the `.env` file can be overridden by command-line parameters.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Review the [v1.5.0rc2 release notes](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/releases/tag/v1.5.0rc2) before upgrading a production instance.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This is because each time LightRAG Server starts, it loads the environment variables from the `.env` file into the system environment variables, and system environment variables have higher precedence.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To keep the old file-processing behavior while upgrading the server, set:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Reranking can be enabled or disabled on a per-query basis for optional settings.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LIGHTRAG_PARSER=*:legacy-F">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/query` and `/query/stream` API endpoints include an `enable_rerank` parameter, which is set to `true` by default, controlling whether reranking is active for the current query for optional settings.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;ENTITY_TYPES is no longer supported. Use ENTITY_TYPE_PROMPT_FILE instead, with a YAML profile stored under PROMPT_DIR/entity_type (PROMPT_DIR defaults to ./prompts). A sample template is available at prompts/samples/entity_type_prompt.sample.yml.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If you use OpenSearch storage and the cluster is older than OpenSearch 3.3.0, upgrade OpenSearch before enabling the v1.5 storage path and validate existing indices. For new deployments, use OpenSearch 3.3.0 or later.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# see also env.ollama-binding-options.example for fine tuning ollama&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Changing the embedding model, embedding dimension, asymmetric embedding behavior, or query/document prefixes changes vector semantics. Clear the affected LightRAG workspace/vector data and re-index source files.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Changing parser routing (LIGHTRAG_PARSER) or filename hints affects newly uploaded files. To switch an existing document to another parser engine, delete that document and upload it again.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Changing chunker settings (CHUNK_*), affects documents enqueued after the server restarts. Reprocess older documents if you want their stored chunk_options snapshot to match the new settings.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Enabling multimodal options (i/t/e) requires parsed sidecars plus VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE=true. Existing documents can be reprocessed to run VLM analysis on available sidecars; switching extraction engines still requires delete + re-upload.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
