  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG supports these embedding backends:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use this path when you want the WebUI and API running first, with no external database, parser service, or local model service.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use `DOCLING_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:5001` when routing files to `docling`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;* jina">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`LIGHTRAG_PARSER` defines default extraction rules by file extension. Rules are matched left to right and can be separated by commas or semicolons:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;* voyageai">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;WEBUI_TITLE='My First LightRAG KB'&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;```bash LIGHTRAG_PARSER=pdf:mineru-R,docx:native-ietP,*:legacy-R```&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;WEBUI_DESCRIPTION='Simple and Fast Graph Based RAG System'&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Supported engines:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Different instances need to access the same database instance, but data isolation must be achieved using workspaces to prevent data conflict and destruction.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;OLLAMA_EMULATING_MODEL_TAG=latest&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| Engine | Use case |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The command-line 'workspace' argument and the 'WORKSPACE' environment variable in the '.env' file can be used to specify the workspace name for the current instance, with the command-line argument having higher priority.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;SUMMARY_LANGUAGE=English&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here is how workspaces are implemented for different types of storage: local file-based databases, databases storing data in collections, Qdrant vector database, relational databases, graph databases, and OpenSearch.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `legacy` | Original extraction behavior. Good for compatibility and simple text-like files. |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To maintain compatibility with legacy data, the default workspace for PostgreSQL is 'default' and for Neo4j is 'base' when no workspace is configured.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `native` | Built-in structured parser, currently focused on `.docx` and LightRAG Document sidecars. |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all external storages, the system provides dedicated workspace environment variables to override the common 'WORKSPACE' environment variable configuration.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `mineru` | External MinerU parser for PDFs, Office files, and images. Requires `MINERU_API_MODE` plus `MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT` or `MINERU_API_TOKEN`. |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG Server can operate in the 'Gunicorn + Uvicorn' preload mode to prevent document indexing tasks from blocking RAG queries.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `docling` | External docling-serve parser for PDFs, Office files, Markdown/HTML, and images. Requires `DOCLING_ENDPOINT`. |&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;CPU-heavy document extraction tools should be deployed as external services to prevent blocking the API process.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG Server is designed to provide a Web UI and API support.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Below are several environment variables related to concurrent processing in LightRAG Server, including 'WORKERS', 'MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT', and 'MAX_ASYNC_LLM'.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_BINDING_API_KEY=your_api_key&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">21.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Web UI facilitates document indexing, knowledge graph exploration, and a simple RAG query interface.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;On macOS, Gunicorn multi-worker mode requires the Objective-C fork-safety override before the Python process starts.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LLM_MODEL=gpt-5-mini&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">21.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG Server also provides an Ollama-compatible interface, aiming to emulate LightRAG as an Ollama chat model.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG service file should be created from the sample file and the ExecStart command must be either 'lightrag-gunicorn' or 'lightrag-server' without wrapper scripts.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;KEYWORD_LLM_MODEL=gpt-5-nano&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This allows AI chat bots, such as Open WebUI, to access LightRAG easily.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To install the LightRAG service on Ubuntu, the service file must be copied to /etc/systemd/system, daemon-reloaded, and the service started and enabled.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;QUERY_LLM_MODEL=gpt-5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">21.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2222a5f74e1118344a0513e7d693837a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For example, the chat message `/mix What's LightRAG?` will trigger a mix mode query for LightRAG. A chat message without a query prefix will trigger a hybrid mode query by default.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We provide Ollama-compatible interfaces for LightRAG to allow AI chat frontends supporting Ollama to access LightRAG easily.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;az cognitiveservices account deployment create --resource-group $RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME  --model-format OpenAI --name $RESOURCE_NAME --deployment-name text-embedding-3-large --model-name text-embedding-3-large --model-version &quot;1&quot;  --sku-capacity 80 --sku-name &quot;Standard&quot;:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_BINDING=openai&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/bypass` is not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell the API Server to pass the query directly to the underlying LLM, including the chat history. So the user can use the LLM to answer questions based on the chat history. If you are using Open WebUI as a front end, you can just switch the model to a normal LLM instead of using the `/bypass` prefix.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You can test the API endpoints using the provided curl commands or through the Swagger UI interface.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Open WebUI can be used to connect to LightRAG and perform session title and session keyword generation tasks using an LLM.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;az cognitiveservices account show --name $RESOURCE_NAME --resource-group $RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME --query &quot;properties.endpoint&quot;:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_BINDING_HOST=https://api.openai.com/v1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/context` is also not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell LightRAG to return only the context information prepared for the LLM. You can check the context if it's what you want, or process the context by yourself.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Make sure to:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For Qdrant vector database, data isolation is achieved through payload-based partitioning (Qdrant's recommended multitenancy approach).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;az cognitiveservices account keys list --name $RESOURCE_NAME -g $RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_BINDING_API_KEY=your_api_key&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When using LightRAG for content queries, avoid combining the search process with unrelated output processing, as this significantly impacts query effectiveness. User prompt is specifically designed to address this issue — it does not participate in the RAG retrieval phase, but rather guides the LLM on how to process the retrieved results after the query is completed. We can append square brackets to the query prefix to provide the LLM with the user prompt:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/health` endpoint reports operational state and selected configuration, including role LLM configuration, LLM/embedding/rerank queue status, workspace/storage workspace mapping, VLM enablement, rerank enablement, and pipeline busy/scanning/destructive status.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For relational databases, data isolation is achieved by adding a 'workspace' field to the tables for logical data separation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The output of the last command will give you the endpoint and the key for the OpenAI API. You can use these values to set the environment variables in the `.env` file:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-large&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We can append square brackets to the query prefix to provide the LLM with the user prompt:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It always returns HTTP 200 so it stays usable as a liveness probe, but the configuration and operational diagnostics are returned **only to authenticated callers** (valid JWT or `X-API-Key`). Unauthenticated callers receive only liveness signals (`status`, `auth_mode`, `core_version`, `api_version`, `pipeline_busy`/`pipeline_active`, and the WebUI title/availability fields — all of which are also exposed by the unauthenticated `/auth-status` endpoint or are plain booleans). Provide credentials to retrieve the full payload, e.g. `curl -H &quot;X-API-Key: &lt;key&gt;&quot; http://localhost:9621/health`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After modifying the `.env` file, you need to reopen the terminal for the new settings to take effect.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;EMBEDDING_DIM=3072&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;By default, the LightRAG Server can be accessed without any authentication. We can configure the server with an API Key or account credentials to secure it.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG implements asynchronous document indexing to enable frontend monitoring and querying of document processing progress.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use environment variables `LLM_BINDING` or CLI argument `--llm-binding` to select the LLM backend type. Use environment variables `EMBEDDING_BINDING` or CLI argument `--embedding-binding` to select the Embedding backend type:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</node>
