  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You can select query mode by sending a message with a query prefix. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`MAX_ASYNC_RERANK` falls back to `MAX_ASYNC_LLM` when unset (`MAX_ASYNC` is still accepted as a deprecated alias).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If the LLM supports high concurrency, document indexing can be accelerated by increasing the concurrency level of the LLM.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;These variables have higher precedence over system environment variables when the server starts.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/bypass` is not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell the API Server to pass the query directly to the underlying LLM, including the chat history. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`RERANK_TIMEOUT` has an independent default because reranker requests are usually shorter than LLM generation requests.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG Server uses environment variables to configure the number of worker processes, the number of parallel files to process, and the maximum number of concurrent requests to the LLM.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You cannot change storage implementation selection after adding documents to LightRAG. Data migration from one storage implementation to another is not supported yet. For further information, please read the sample .env.example file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Command-line parameters can modify the configurations in the `.env` file during startup.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`/context` is also not a LightRAG query mode; it will tell LightRAG to return only the context information prepared for the LLM. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For comprehensive reranker configuration examples, including Cohere-compatible chunking options and Jina/Aliyun endpoints, refer to the `env.example` file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'WORKERS' environment variable sets the number of worker processes.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Milvus Index Configuration: LightRAG now supports configurable index types for Milvus vector storage (AUTOINDEX, HNSW, HNSW_SQ, IVF_FLAT, etc.) through environment variables. HNSW_SQ requires Milvus 2.6.8+ and provides significant memory savings. See the 'Using Milvus for Vector Storage' section in the main README.md for complete configuration options.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44dde1b8fa9d74e9edbda4a6a1d22019</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Common command-line parameters for LightRAG include `--host`, `--port`, `--timeout`, etc.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When using LightRAG for content queries, avoid combining the search process with unrelated output processing, as this significantly impacts query effectiveness. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Reranking can be enabled or disabled on a per-query basis.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT' environment variable defines the number of parallel files to process in one batch.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `LIGHTRAG_API_PREFIX` can be set to handle multiple instances behind a reverse proxy.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;User prompt is specifically designed to address this issue — it does not participate in the RAG retrieval phase, but rather guides the LLM on how to process the retrieved results after the query is completed. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07113c82d8f800d43e240dceb9a4230</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `/query` and `/query/stream` API endpoints include an `enable_rerank` parameter, which is set to `true` by default, controlling whether reranking is active for the current query.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'MAX_ASYNC_LLM' environment variable defines the maximum number of concurrent requests to the LLM.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **Global Limit (8MB)**: Sufficient for LLM queries with long conversation history and context (128K tokens ≈ 512KB + JSON overhead).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The WebUI is mounted at `/webui` within the server and can serve any prefix.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server. There is an example environment variable file named `env.example` in the root directory of the project.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To change the default value of the `enable_rerank` parameter to `false`, set the following environment variable:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;On macOS, the Objective-C fork-safety override is required for Gunicorn multi-worker mode to function properly.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. **Upload Endpoint (100MB)**: Must match or exceed `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE` in your `.env` file. The default `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE` is 100MB.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Docker Compose is recommended for deploying the LightRAG Server.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Please copy this file to the startup directory and rename it to `.env`. After that, you can modify the parameters related to the LLM and Embedding models in the `.env` file.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;By default, the `/query` and `/query/stream` endpoints return references with only `reference_id` and `file_path`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Objective-C fork-safety override must be set before the Python process starts in Gunicorn multi-worker mode.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. **Streaming Endpoints**: Disable gzip compression (`gzip off`) for streaming endpoints to ensure real-time response delivery. LightRAG automatically sets `X-Accel-Buffering: no` header to disable response buffering.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;A project directory is required, and the `docker-compose.yml` file is copied into it.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is important to note that the LightRAG Server will load the environment variables from `.env` into the system environment variables each time it starts. **LightRAG Server will prioritize the settings in the system environment variables to .env file**.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For evaluation, debugging, or citation purposes, you can request the actual retrieved chunk content to be included in references.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'lightrag.service' file must be created from the sample file and must not include wrapper scripts for the ExecStart command.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;4. **Timeout Settings**: Large file uploads and LLM generation require longer timeouts; adjust `proxy_read_timeout` and `proxy_send_timeout` accordingly.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `.env` file should be customized and placed next to `docker-compose.yml`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Important**: The `content` field is an **array of strings**, where each string represents a chunk from the same file. A single file may correspond to multiple chunks, so the content is returned as a list to preserve chunk boundaries.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The given text '3-large' is not a proper context, it appears to be a code snippet or a command line output rather than a coherent sentence. This text is not suitable for the extraction of knowledge segments, entities, or relationships. No meaningful entities or relationships can be extracted from this input.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Official LightRAG Docker images are fully compatible with offline or air-gapped environments. If you want to build up your own offline environment, please refer to [Offline Deployment Guide](./OfflineDeployment.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The server is started with `docker compose up`, and can be run in the background with `-d`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Example API Request:**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following 'EMBEDDING_DIM', 'EMBEDDING_TOKEN_LIMIT', and 'EMBEDDING_SEND_DIM' values indicate configuration settings for a document embedding service. These settings do not represent a context that can be segmented, nor do they provide information about entities or relationships. As such, no entities or relationships can be extracted from this input.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;There are two ways to start multiple LightRAG instances. The first way is to configure a completely independent working environment for each instance. This requires creating a separate working directory for each instance and placing a dedicated `.env` configuration file in that directory. The server listening ports in the configuration files of different instances cannot be the same. Then, you can start the service by running `lightrag-server` in the working directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Historical versions of LightRAG Docker images can be found in the repository.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here are some examples of common settings for LLM and Embedding models:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Example Response (with chunk content):**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The configuration details for data storage systems like 'LIGHTRAG_KV_STORAGE', 'LIGHTRAG_DOC_STATUS_STORAGE', and 'LIGHTRAG_GRAPH_STORAGE' are technical settings that do not form a knowledge segment or context suitable for entity or relationship extraction. This information does not represent a sentence with meaning, nor does it provide a basis for identifying entities or relationships.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The second way is for all instances to share the same set of `.env` configuration files, and then use command-line arguments to specify different server listening ports and workspaces for each instance. You can start multiple LightRAG instances in the same working directory with different command-line arguments. For example:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `env.example` file serves as the complete configuration reference.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Notes**:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'RERANK_BINDING', 'RERANK_MODEL', and related configuration values provided here are technical settings for reranking in a document search service. These settings do not represent a context, knowledge segment, or entities that can be extracted for relationship identification.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The purpose of a workspace is to achieve data isolation between different instances. Therefore, the `workspace` parameter must be different for different instances; otherwise, it will lead to data confusion and corruption.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `make env-*` setup wizard uses the `env.example` file.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Important Note**: The embedding model and asymmetric embedding configuration must be determined before document indexing, and the same settings must be used during the query phase. For certain storage solutions (e.g., PostgreSQL), the vector dimension must be defined upon initial table creation. When changing the embedding model, embedding dimension, `EMBEDDING_ASYMMETRIC`, query/document prefixes, or provider task behavior, clear the existing LightRAG workspace/vector data and re-index the source files.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- This parameter only works when `include_references=true`. Setting `include_chunk_content=true` without including references has no effect.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The configuration details for enabling multimodal parsing with MinerU's official API, such as 'LIGHTRAG_PARSER', 'VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE', and 'MINERU_API_TOKEN', are technical settings that do not form a knowledge segment or context suitable for entity or relationship extraction. This information is not meaningful in the context of entity and relationship extraction.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When launching multiple LightRAG instances via Docker Compose, simply specify unique `WORKSPACE` and `PORT` environment variables for each container within your `docker-compose.yml`. Even if all instances share a common `.env` file, the container-specific environment variables defined in Compose will take precedence, ensuring independent configurations for each instance.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;A minimal Docker run with hosted LLM and embedding models is recommended for beginners(&quot;hyper-relation&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Prior versions returned `content` as a single concatenated string. Now it returns an array of strings to preserve individual chunk boundaries. If you need a single string, join the array elements with your preferred separator (e.g., `&quot;\n\n&quot;.join(content)`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58732a4b6a97c3eeba3cb6d1206d401e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The 'make env-base', 'make env-storage', and 'make env-server' commands provided are instructions for configuring the environment for a service and do not represent a context, knowledge segment, or entities suitable for entity or relationship extraction.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">0.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Configuring an independent working directory and a dedicated `.env` configuration file for each instance can generally ensure that locally persisted files in the in-memory database are saved in their respective working directories, achieving data isolation. By default, LightRAG uses all in-memory databases, and this method of data isolation is sufficient. However, if you are using an external database, and different instances access the same database instance, you need to use workspaces to achieve data isolation; otherwise, the data of different instances will conflict and be destroyed.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a514646a651da9026d7f8eb73aa2f08</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The configurations in `.env` files are loaded into the system environment variables on server start.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</node>
