  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This ensures that only relevant information is presented to the VLM/LLM for analysis.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `footnotes` field is a list of footnotes associated with the equation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `&lt;cite type=&quot;table&quot; refid=&quot;tb-…&quot;&gt;Table 1&lt;/cite&gt;` → `&lt;cite type=&quot;table&quot;&gt;Table 1&lt;/cite&gt;`; `&lt;cite type=&quot;equation&quot; refid=&quot;eq-…&quot;&gt;Equation 2&lt;/cite&gt;` → `&lt;cite type=&quot;equation&quot;&gt;Equation 2&lt;/cite&gt;`. Only the `refid` attribute is removed; the `&lt;cite type=&quot;…&quot;&gt;…&lt;/cite&gt;` wrapper is preserved — letting the VLM/LLM recognize &quot;this is a reference to another table/equation&quot; rather than ordinary text, while hiding the parser-internal id that the LLM cannot see.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`positions` | Array of `position` objects: identifies the layout position of the text block; when the text block comes from multiple positions in the layout, multiple `position` objects appear. See [§8](#8-positions) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `blockid` / `heading` / `parent_headings` / `surrounding` / `llm_analyze_result` fields of equations.json have the same meaning as in drawings.json. Different or newly added fields are described below:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Table objects are extracted from the file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cleanup process happens before token-budget truncation to ensure a clean and structured input for the LLM.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The goal is to avoid extracting entities that are invisible in the article and injecting too much noise into the extraction results. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `llm_cache_list` field in equations.json contains the list of analysis results used for caching purposes.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Exception: surrounding of the `tables.json` type first goes through `remove_table_tags` before stripping, removing all `&lt;cite type=&quot;table&quot;&gt;` blocks entirely (when analyzing the target table, we don't want to be distracted by dangling references to other tables);&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `id` field is used to form `eq-&lt;doc_hash&gt;-&lt;NNNN&gt;` (`doc_hash` is the 32-character md5 portion of `doc_id` with the `doc-` prefix removed) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Table objects are sent to an LLM for analysis; analysis results are written back.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
