  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Cleanup happens **before** token-budget truncation: the token count is computed on &quot;what the LLM actually sees&quot;, and truncation does not land inside an uncleaned `id=&quot;…&quot;` attribute, avoiding broken tag structure;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The chunking strategies `F` / `R` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `format` field is fixed to `&quot;latex`&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The file stores equation objects.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;does not read this field; cross-document deduplication is handled separately by `doc_status.content_hash`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The chunking strategies `F` / `R` / `V` that ignore document section structure operate on the concatenated `content` fields. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When LightRAG uses multimodal-capable content parsing engines such as native/mineru/docling to extract file content, it splits &quot;body text + multimodal objects + parsing metadata&quot; into a `*.parsed/` directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When the target object itself sits at the start / end of the block, the corresponding side is `&quot;&quot;` instead of `&quot;n/a&quot;` (when assembling the prompt, the empty string is later displayed as `n/a`);&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The MI012 module is used to support the oxygen-supply and anti-gravity control function of the oxygen-supply and anti-gravity regulator... &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `content` field is the raw LaTeX (possibly containing Unicode operators, outer `\[ \]`); does not include the leading/trailing `$` delimiters; read directly by the modal analysis stage &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Equation objects are extracted from the file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`table_file` / `equation_file` / `drawing_file` | `bool` | Whether the corresponding sidecar files exist (when true, the corresponding file must exist) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Therefore, concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks must form the complete document content — no content missing, no content overlapping. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each JSON / JSONL file in that directory is collectively called a **sidecar** file.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`enrich_sidecars_with_surrounding` is idempotent: each `analyze_multimodal` entry point recomputes and overwrites `surrounding`, so after changing `SURROUNDING_LEADING_MAX_TOKENS` / `SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS` there is no need to manually clean the sidecar — just re-run multimodal analysis and `surrounding` will be rewritten under the new budget.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Every recognized heading starts its own block: if a heading is immediately followed by body text, that body is merged into the same block (content = markdown-rendered heading line + body); if a heading has no following body (e.g., it is immediately followed by a heading at the next level), it still becomes a standalone block whose content is just the markdown-rendered heading line. This ensures that concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks still reconstructs the complete original text without overlap. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `self_ref` field is optional; object reference from the original parsing engine output (e.g., Docling JSON Pointer `#/texts/15`, or MinerU `content_list.json#/45`), used to look up the original artifact when tracing back &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Equation objects are sent to an LLM for analysis; analysis results are written back.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`asset_dir` | `bool` | Whether the `blocks.assets` asset directory exists &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Sidecars are the only reliable source of truth for the subsequent pipeline (multimodal analysis → multimodal chunk construction → entity extraction → cache cleanup on document deletion).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;8. positions&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `llm_analyze_result` field is the canonicalized LaTeX equation output by the LLM (outer `$ / \[ \] / equation` environment, Unicode converted to LaTeX, no leading/trailing `$` delimiters); this is the string actually used by the downstream multimodal chunk &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The directory stores original image assets.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`split_option` | `object` | Optional. Free-form metadata the parsing engine records about itself (e.g. `engine_version`, engine-specific extras). Omitted entirely when the engine recorded nothing (the common native/markdown case). Chunking is NOT performed at the parse stage — it is the downstream chunker's responsibility — so this field never carries chunking parameters. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks produced by chunking strategies record the blockid for tracing the chunk back to its location in the sidecar. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">56.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The sidecar format is LightRAG's built-in universal file interchange format; new multimodal content extraction engines must follow this format.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`position` objects have multiple types, and the `type` field determines its type:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The goal is to avoid injecting too much noise into the extraction results.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">12.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Original image files are extracted from the document.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`blocks` | `int` | Number of content lines (excluding meta) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To let the P chunking strategy split body text without breaking multimodal objects, three XML-style placeholder tags are used inside `content` &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The purpose of publicly documenting the **LightRAG Sidecar** format is to make it convenient for community developers to write their own content parsing engines.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</node>
