</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Applicable to docx-format files; locates content by `paragraph id` (paraid). The `range` field specifies the start and end `paragraph id`s; `charspan` is an optional field specifying that the content starts at character m and ends at character n of the paragraph. When `charspan` is not provided, the `blockid` covers the entire content of the start and end paragraphs. Example:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `llm_cache_list` field contains the list of analysis results used for caching purposes.&quot;">
