<node id="&quot;BLOCKID COMPUTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `blockid` is computed using the formula `md5(doc_id + ":" + block_index + ":" + heading + ":" + content)`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Content typically contains parent_headings "&lt;SEP&gt;"Same-level merging requires `parent_headings` to be exactly equal for true siblings.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy uses `parent_headings` to preserve the hierarchical structure of the document, ensuring that the relationships between headings and subheadings are maintained during chunking."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy uses heading outline level and `parent_headings` + table-row boundaries + anchors + hierarchy-aware merging for chunking."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy utilizes heading levels and `parent_headings` to maintain hierarchy information, which is often underused by other methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `parent_headings` field contains a string array listing the top-down list of ancestor headings, excluding the current heading.&lt;SEP&gt;"The `parent_headings` field is a string array of ancestor headings. "&lt;SEP&gt;"The `parent_headings` field lists the top-down list of ancestor headings.&lt;SEP&gt;"This checks for consistency in `parent_headings` of adjacent clauses to block cross-topic merging."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6df28f5232d5c31b9f64164c61a08e65</data>
</node>
