</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Earlier versions of LightRAG baked the site prefix into the JavaScript bundle at build time (via `VITE_API_PREFIX` / `VITE_WEBUI_PREFIX`). Every site that used a different prefix needed its own WebUI build, and reusing a single Docker image across sites required a rebuild step at deploy time. Since the runtime-config-injection refactor:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text clarifies that Vite's dev server serves the SPA at its own root (`/`) regardless of the prefix configured.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8695c3b8cfc1cc28382a176ac4d0e7ba</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text advises to confirm the backend is running with the matching `LIGHTRAG_API_PREFIX`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eefa10d662229bd1054dbd21eaf6d102</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| - **Strip** — proxy removes the prefix, backend sees `/webui/` and `/documents/foo`. The nginx example below uses this style.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text provides an example of the `.env.local` file for the second scenario, which simulates a site prefix.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8695c3b8cfc1cc28382a176ac4d0e7ba</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The result: a single `lightrag/api/webui/` directory (or Docker image) is reusable across any number of sites with no per-site build artifact.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text emphasizes that `VITE_DEV_API_PREFIX` only affects the composition of API URLs after the page is loaded and the paths the dev proxy intercepts.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
