  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eefa10d662229bd1054dbd21eaf6d102</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| - **Verbatim** — proxy forwards the request unchanged, backend sees `/site01/webui/` and `/site01/documents/foo`. The Vite dev flow ([Scenario 2](#scenario-2--simulate-a-site-prefix)) and any non-rewriting proxy use this style.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The browser only talks to `localhost:5173` for SPA assets, no WebSocket-upgrade config needed on any upstream.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f50a1a569536dcf7b4109c246e92d1a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;How runtime prefix injection works&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text explains that the setting `base: './'` in `vite.config.ts` allows for a single production build to be reusable across any number of reverse-proxy mount points.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8695c3b8cfc1cc28382a176ac4d0e7ba</data>
