</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| A small ASGI middleware in `create_app` prepends `root_path` to `scope[&quot;path&quot;]` whenever the path does not already include it, so plain Routes and Mount sub-apps (the WebUI's `StaticFiles`) both resolve identically in either mode. You do not need to standardize on one forwarding style.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Two options, picked by where the prefix-aware upstream lives. The Vite-side configuration is identical; only this one variable changes.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f50a1a569536dcf7b4109c246e92d1a</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each request for `index.html` goes through `SmartStaticFiles` in `lightrag/api/lightrag_server.py`, which reads the static `index.html` produced by `bun run build` and looks for the placeholder comment `&lt;!-- __LIGHTRAG_RUNTIME_CONFIG__ --&gt;`.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">9.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text clarifies that tying the dev URL to a prefix would force the build to bake the prefix back in, which is not necessary.">
