  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Check whether the table's token count actually exceeds `table_max`. A table below the threshold stays whole and does not trigger first/middle/last slicing.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It decomposes this goal into concrete rules for three scenarios (tables, long blocks, fine-grained sections), expanded one by one in §3.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">14.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy utilizes heading levels and `parent_headings` to maintain hierarchy information, which is often underused by other methods.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
