  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_P_SIZE PARAMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARAMETER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The CHUNK_P_SIZE parameter is set to 2000 for the P strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CURRENT BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The current block is deeper than the previous block.&lt;SEP&gt;"The current block is shallower than the next block.&lt;SEP&gt;"The process applies to the current block when it is below `target_ideal`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANCHORSPLIT &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"AnchorSplit drives re-splitting of long text chunks.&lt;SEP&gt;"The effect is achieved by the AnchorSplit stage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE PARAMETER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARAMETER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE parameter is set to 100 for the P strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERGED REAL TOKEN COUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOKEN"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The merged real token count does not exceed `target_max`.&lt;SEP&gt;"The merged real token count must be less than or equal to `target_max`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;P AUTO-DEGRADES TO R&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The process of `P` auto-degrading to `R` when `full_docs[doc_id].parse_format` is `raw`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BODY-LESS HEADING GLUING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A parent heading is never separated from its child content.&lt;SEP&gt;"Parent headings are glued to their child content to ensure they are not separated.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FILE OVERRIDES FOR NATIVE-P MINERU-P SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"File overrides can be used to specify settings for `native-P` and `mineru-P` for specific files."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ABSORBED NEIGHBOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"BLOCK"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The absorbed neighbour does not need to be below `target_ideal` for merging.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNRECOGNIZED FORMAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This refers to a table format that is not recognized and can only go through character splitting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEADINGGLUE &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"HeadingGlue glues body-less heading blocks forward into their child.&lt;SEP&gt;"The effect is achieved by the HeadingGlue stage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIVE-P SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CHUNKING STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunking strategy native-P is specified for certain files."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BACKWARD MERGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A backward merge requires the previous block to be less than `target_ideal`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARACTER SPLITTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The process of splitting a table into characters when it is of unrecognized format."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEVELMERGE &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LevelMerge performs hierarchy-aware two-phase merging.&lt;SEP&gt;"The effect is achieved by the LevelMerge stage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINERU-P SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CHUNKING STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunking strategy mineru-P is specified for certain files."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTIONAL RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Directional rules define how blocks can merge based on their table-slice role.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLEROWSPLIT'S ROLE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The mechanism that TableRowSplit uses to determine the role of the table cannot be applied to unrecognized formats."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERLAP RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Overlap rules ensure sufficient recall context without mis-attribution of section/table boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGINE WITH SUFFIX:ENGINE-OPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An engine with the specified `suffix:engine-options` that can combine with other engines for sidecar production."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE-SLICE ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rules apply to blocks with different table-slice roles.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THRESHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The threshold is the token count that determines if a table should be split into first, middle, or last slices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCX / PDF / PPTX / … &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The pipeline starts with DOCX, PDF, PPTX, etc.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIDECAR-PRODUCING ENGINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An engine capable of producing sidecars, which are additional data files for document parsing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPLIT-TABLE SLICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"All split-table slices are frozen from merging.&lt;SEP&gt;"Split-table slices are frozen in the cross-level stage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STAYS WHOLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A table below the threshold remains as a whole unit and is not split into slices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIVE(DOCX) / MINERU / DOCLING PARSER &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The native(docx) / mineru / docling parser emits basic blocks by heading, no token splitting.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATIVE PARSER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARSER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The native parser is used for docx files with the P chunking strategy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NONE (AN ORDINARY BLOCK / AN UNSPLIT WHOLE TABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`none` blocks can absorb the next block forward and can be absorbed by the previous block.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE ACROSS CONTENT LINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A bridge that spans across different content lines does not contribute to the bidirectional overlap in TableBridge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLOCKS.JSONL &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The input is `.blocks.jsonl`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINERU PARSER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARSER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The mineru parser is used for pdf files with the P chunking strategy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST (A BLOCK AT THE START OF A TABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`first` blocks cannot absorb the next block forward and cannot be absorbed by the previous block.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATCHED TAIL ABSORPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Batched tail absorption is a process that can separate a heading from its child content in LevelMerge."&lt;SEP&gt;"The presence of a middle table slice blocks the batched tail absorption process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIDECAR (.TABLES.JSON / .EQUATIONS.JSON / .DRAWINGS.JSON / .BLOCKS.ASSETS/) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The sidecar files include .tables.json, .equations.json, .drawings.json, and .blocks.assets.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCLING PARSER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PARSER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The docling parser is used for other supported formats with the P chunking strategy.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDDLE (A BLOCK IN THE MIDDLE OF A TABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`middle` blocks cannot absorb the next block forward and cannot be absorbed by the previous block.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Small blocks are unsaturated after Phase A.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTLABELING &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"PartLabeling provides line-level provenance numbering.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAST (A BLOCK AT THE END OF A TABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`last` blocks cannot absorb the next block forward and cannot be absorbed by the previous block.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-LEVEL MERGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Cross-level merging is attempted for unsaturated small blocks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL CHUNK LIST &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The final output is a list of chunks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDINARY (`NONE`) BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"BLOCK"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An ordinary `none` block has reached `target_ideal` and is followed by a run of same-level small blocks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHALLOW-ABSORBS-DEEP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Cross-level merging allows shallow-absorbs-deep.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECALL TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunks are made understandable on their own at recall time.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE SLICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Each table slice has an internal field `table_chunk_role`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL TOKEN COUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOKEN"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The total token count of the run of small blocks is below `small_tail_threshold`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEXT BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The current block may absorb the next block forward.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCRETE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The goal is decomposed into concrete rules for different scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Role is a column in the table with a meaning and gluing strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULL_DOCS[DOC_ID].PROCESS_OPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This checks if `full_docs[doc_id].process_options` includes `P`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVIOUS BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The previous shallower block may absorb the current block.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERLAP INVARIANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Overlap invariants define where text duplication is allowed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEANING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Meaning is a column in the table with a meaning and gluing strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERGING IN REVERSE DIRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Merging in the reverse direction is forbidden.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION BOUNDARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Section boundaries never overlap to avoid mis-attribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLUING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Gluing strategy is a column in the table with a meaning and gluing strategy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULL_DOCS[DOC_ID].PARSE_FORMAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This checks if `full_docs[doc_id].parse_format` is equal to `lightrag`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CROSS-LEVEL STAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Split-table slices do not participate in cross-level absorption.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROW-LEVEL SLICING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Row-level slicing is non-overlapping.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `first` role is the first slice of the original table."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NONE BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Only `none` blocks participate in cross-level absorption.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEADINGBLOCKS &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"STAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The effect is achieved by the HeadingBlocks stage.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL TABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `first` role is associated with the first slice of the original table."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"If `full_docs[doc_id].parse_format` is `raw`, the legacy path was taken and `P` auto-degrades to `R`."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term `raw` indicates the legacy path was taken and `P` auto-degrades to `R`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POST-MERGE REAL-TOKEN RE-MEASUREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Post-merge real-token re-measurement is performed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARAGRAPH SEMANTIC CHUNKING STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Paragraph Semantic Chunking Strategy targets documents with a clear sectional structure such as DOCX and PDF, aiming to align chunk boundaries with the document's native semantic boundaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
