  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy does not decide split points purely by token-length counting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRAILING COMMENTARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `last` role starts a fresh accumulation block, so the trailing commentary is appended after the last slice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `last` role's table slice starts a fresh accumulation block, with the trailing commentary automatically appended after the last slice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE FORMAT=&quot;HTML&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This checks if the table is identified as `&lt;table format="html"&gt;` in `.blocks.jsonl`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE CONTEXT FRACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROBLEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy addresses Table context fracture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy aims to address the problem of table context fracture after a large table is split, ensuring the head/tail slices remain connected to their explanation or commentary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDINARY TEXT CHUNK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A non-table slice or an unsplit whole table is handled as an ordinary text chunk."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `none` role is handled as an ordinary text chunk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOKEN COUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The token count of the table is checked against `table_max`."&lt;SEP&gt;"Token counts may be underestimated due to newline joiner.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
