  <data key="d4">"The P strategy addresses Underused hierarchy information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LARGE TABLE A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"There is a large table A that is part of the pattern "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE TEXT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Bridge text between tables may overlap bidirectionally.&lt;SEP&gt;"The bridge text is encoded into tokens."&lt;SEP&gt;"This checks if the bridge text between consecutive large tables is within the same content line."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;P STRATEGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"P strategy has multi-layer fallback protection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy aligns chunk boundaries with the document's native semantic boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy does not accept split_by_character / split_by_character_only "&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy draws a precise boundary on text duplication (overlap)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy only processes type == "content" lines "&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy processes `.blocks.jsonl` convention "&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy targets documents with a clear sectional structure, aligning chunk boundaries with the document's native semantic boundaries as much as possible."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMBALANCED FINE-GRAINED SECTION SIZES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROBLEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy addresses Imbalanced fine-grained section sizes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy deals with imbalanced fine-grained section sizes by merging short clauses together to avoid creating semantically thin chunks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHORT BRIDGE TEXT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"There is short bridge text that is part of the pattern "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-BLOCK RE-SPLITTING BREAKS STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROBLEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy addresses Long-block re-splitting breaks structure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDDLE TABLE SLICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This checks for the presence of a `middle` table slice to block batched tail absorption."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
