  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every slice becomes a complete header-bearing table after TableRowSplit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME-LEVEL MERGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Merging of clauses at the same level requires them to have the same `level` value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Same-level merging happens between blocks of equal `level`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG BODY TEXT WITHIN ONE CONTENT LINE FALLING BACK TO R&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Long body text may overlap.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NO OVERLAP AT SECTION BOUNDARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"INVARIANT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy has four overlap invariants: No overlap at section boundaries, Long body text overlaps by `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`, Bridge text between consecutive large tables overlaps bidirectionally, and Heading metadata is inherited or promoted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG BODY TEXT OVERLAPS BY `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"INVARIANT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy has four overlap invariants: No overlap at section boundaries, Long body text overlaps by `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`, Bridge text between consecutive large tables overlaps bidirectionally, and Heading metadata is inherited or promoted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEADING EXPLANATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `first` role's table slice is appended to the tail of the current accumulation block, including the table's leading explanation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FALLBACK TO RECURSIVE_CHARACTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"LOG"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This is a log keyword indicating wholesale or single-paragraph degradation, used in troubleshooting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KEEPS SEMANTIC CONTINUITY AT A MID-BODY CUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"EFFECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Overlap keeps semantic continuity at a mid-body cut.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE TEXT BETWEEN CONSECUTIVE LARGE TABLES OVERLAPS BIDIRECTIONALLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"INVARIANT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy has four overlap invariants: No overlap at section boundaries, Long body text overlaps by `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`, Bridge text between consecutive large tables overlaps bidirectionally, and Heading metadata is inherited or promoted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE_CHUNK_ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Each table slice has an internal field `table_chunk_role` that determines how it glues to surrounding paragraphs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The internal field `table_chunk_role` determines how each table slice glues to surrounding paragraphs."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a log keyword related to table-role handling, used in troubleshooting."&lt;SEP&gt;"`table_chunk_role` is an internal field that does not survive into the final output but serves as a merging constraint in LevelMerge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE TEXT BETWEEN CONSECUTIVE LARGE TABLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Bridge text may overlap between tables.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEADING METADATA IS INHERITED OR PROMOTED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"INVARIANT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy has four overlap invariants: No overlap at section boundaries, Long body text overlaps by `CHUNK_P_OVERLAP_SIZE`, Bridge text between consecutive large tables overlaps bidirectionally, and Heading metadata is inherited or promoted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEADING LINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Boundary ambiguity involves a body line that is misjudged as a heading line.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIDIRECTIONAL OVERLAP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Overlap is bidirectional.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRIDGE EXPLANATION SERVES AS CONTEXT FOR BOTH THE LEFT AND RIGHT TABLES&quot;">
