</node>
<node id="&quot;CHUNK SIZES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy considers `target_max` as a hard cap for chunk sizes and `target_ideal` as a soft target, ensuring chunks do not exceed a certain token limit while still being semantically meaningful."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHASE A PEER MERGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Phase A peer merging is a process that can separate a heading from its child content in LevelMerge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTIONAL CONSTRAINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Proportional constraints are applied to the thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOKEN LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy considers `target_max` as a hard cap for chunk sizes and `target_ideal` as a soft target, ensuring chunks do not exceed a certain token limit while still being semantically meaningful."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;_GLUE_HEADING_ONLY_BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PRE-PASS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `_glue_heading_only_blocks` pre-pass is used to prevent headings from being separated from their child content in LevelMerge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ITEM.LEVEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"XML ATTRIBUTE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"- **docling**: `label="title"` → level 1, `label="section_header"` → `item.level + 1` (default level 2), likewise maintaining the parent chain."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEATING HEADER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The reason for the role constraint is the injection of a repeating header at TableRowSplit time.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE_MAX &lt; TARGET_IDEAL &lt; TARGET_MAX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Thresholds are scaled proportionally by `chunk_token_size`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROW BOUNDARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"When dealing with tables, the P strategy ensures that tables under a certain size (`table_max`) remain whole, and large tables are sliced along row boundaries and re-wrapped as `&lt;table&gt;` elements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRIGGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Table with missing JSON / HTML structure uses R-strategy character splitting."&lt;SEP&gt;"The trigger for the `_glue_heading_only_blocks` pre-pass is when the next block is strictly deeper in level and has a `table_chunk_role` of `none` or `first`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRBLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DATA STRUCTURE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"All three ultimately produce a unified `IRBlock` (carrying `heading` / `level` / `parent_headings`), persisted by `write_sidecar()` into an identically-structured `.blocks.jsonl`; tables, equations, and drawings are extracted as single-line tags (`&lt;table id="..." format="json"&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;` etc.) written to the corresponding sidecar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INPUT AND OUTPUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Input and output details are provided.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE ELEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"When dealing with tables, the P strategy ensures that tables under a certain size (`table_max`) remain whole, and large tables are sliced along row boundaries and re-wrapped as `&lt;table&gt;` elements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST SLICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A `first` slice is the first piece of a split large table in LevelMerge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERLAP BETWEEN CHUNKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy allows for overlap between chunks when a section is too long, ensuring that the text within one section can be split in a way that maintains readability and context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITE_SIDECAR()&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FUNCTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"All three ultimately produce a unified `IRBlock` (carrying `heading` / `level` / `parent_headings`), persisted by `write_sidecar()` into an identically-structured `.blocks.jsonl`; tables, equations, and drawings are extracted as single-line tags (`&lt;table id="..." format="json"&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;` etc.) written to the corresponding sidecar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIERARCHY-AWARE MERGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Fine-grained clauses are gathered toward the ideal size without cross-topic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchy-aware merging is a process that gathers fine-grained clauses to the ideal size without cross-topic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy uses heading outline level and `parent_headings` + table-row boundaries + anchors + hierarchy-aware merging for chunking."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENT-HEADING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `_glue_heading_only_blocks` pre-pass preserves the parent-heading identity in the merged block, ensuring the heading-path levels are not lost."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLOCKS.JSONL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FILE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"All three ultimately produce a unified `IRBlock` (carrying `heading` / `level` / `parent_headings`), persisted by `write_sidecar()` into an identically-structured `.blocks.jsonl`; tables, equations, and drawings are extracted as single-line tags (`&lt;table id="..." format="json"&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;` etc.) written to the corresponding sidecar."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy is valid for the structured output of any parser that can produce a `.blocks.jsonl` sidecar."&lt;SEP&gt;"This checks if the `.blocks.jsonl` file pointed to by `lightrag_document_path` exists and is non-empty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEURISTIC AMBIGUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Boundary ambiguity is the same heuristic ambiguity documented in `lightrag/parser/_markdown.py`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Knowledge fragments were missed in the last extraction.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION IS TOO LONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P strategy allows for overlap between chunks when a section is too long, ensuring that the text within one section can be split in a way that maintains readability and context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BODY LINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Boundary ambiguity involves a body line that begins with `#␠`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TARGET HARD CAP N&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The target hard cap N is set to default `2000` "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER SUPPORTED FORMATS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Other supported formats use docling for parsing with P."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"RULE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Each rule of §3 is mapped to its effect and implementing stage.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy has rules that align chunk boundaries with the document's native semantic boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;"The rule specifies the process from deeper levels to shallower levels, including the merging phases and constraints.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNSUPPORTED FORMATS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FORMAT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Unsupported formats fall back to legacy-R."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEEPER LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"LEVEL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rule starts from deeper levels.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOUNDARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunk boundaries align with the document's native semantic boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;P CHUNKER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOOL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P chunker reads `.blocks.jsonl` directly, treating each content line as an independent processing unit for the subsequent TableRowSplit/AnchorSplit — which also means `[part n]` numbering is **reset independently** per original content line (see §3.4 and §4.4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHALLOW LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"LEVEL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rule ends at shallower levels.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"An input document into the system. These either represent individual rows in a CSV or individual .txt files."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chunk boundaries align with the document's native semantic boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;"The ID is generated using a hash of the text content.&lt;SEP&gt;"The documents list includes a document field which specifies the document content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-813bfd09c5663aba506972a834914fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79b90a7af3598028d581d94c6d76678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAP ON LONG-BODY FALLBACK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The cap on long-body fallback within one content line is set "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPTION FLAGS I/T/E&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Option flags `i`, `t`, `e` stand for image, table, and formula analysis respectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Option flags `i`, `t`, `e` stand for image, table, formula analysis respectively."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLEROWSPLIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A table of unrecognized format cannot start TableRowSplit's role mechanism, which is checked here."&lt;SEP&gt;"During TableRowSplit, the header row is re-injected into the non-first slices' own `&lt;table&gt;`."&lt;SEP&gt;"TableRowSplit is the process where the header row is re-injected into the non-first slices' own `&lt;table&gt;`."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P chunker reads `.blocks.jsonl` directly, treating each content line as an independent processing unit for the subsequent TableRowSplit/AnchorSplit — which also means `[part n]` numbering is **reset independently** per original content line (see §3.4 and §4.4)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The role constraint is due to the repeating header injected at TableRowSplit time.&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a stage name used as a cross-reference identifier, corresponding to Stage B for table integrity and row-boundary slicing, in code comments, docstrings, logs, and tests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME-LEVEL SMALL BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"BLOCK"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rule first merges same-level small blocks (Phase A)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The run consists of same-level small blocks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEMANTIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunk boundaries align with the document's native semantic boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE BRIDGE BUDGET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The cap is also on the table bridge budget "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANCHORSPLIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"AnchorSplit is a process that splits the block at `target_max`, which can lead to a sub-block being over the cap when prepending the parent heading line(s)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The P chunker reads `.blocks.jsonl` directly, treating each content line as an independent processing unit for the subsequent TableRowSplit/AnchorSplit — which also means `[part n]` numbering is **reset independently** per original content line (see §3.4 and §4.4)."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a stage name used as a cross-reference identifier, corresponding to Stage C for anchor-driven long-block re-splitting, in code comments, docstrings, logs, and tests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BATCH-ABSORB THE TAIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rule then batch-absorbs the tail.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;100&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"NUMBER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The default value of the cap is `100` "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERRIDE PER FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"You can override settings per file."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOKENIZER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The tokenizer is already resolved by LightRAG "&lt;SEP&gt;"The tokenizer is an object used to tokenize the text, which is a critical step in many natural language processing tasks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c748ee608ace11e7d348ea0448f352</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;[PART N] NUMBERING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The P chunker reads `.blocks.jsonl` directly, treating each content line as an independent processing unit for the subsequent TableRowSplit/AnchorSplit — which also means `[part n]` numbering is **reset independently** per original content line (see §3.4 and §4.4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHALLOW BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"BLOCK"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The rule finally allows shallow blocks to absorb deep blocks (Phase B)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCRETE RULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The goal is decomposed into concrete rules for different scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MY-PROPOSAL.DOCX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Document `my-proposal.docx` with native-P settings for docx format."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE_MAX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"**Rule**: a table whose token count does not exceed `table_max` **stays whole**; only a table exceeding `table_max` is sliced, and it is **sliced along row boundaries first** — the whole table degrades to character-level splitting only when a slice has collapsed to a single row that still cannot be expressed within the limit.&lt;SEP&gt;"Table slicing trigger threshold is 1250 tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;"This checks if the table's token count exceeds `table_max`."&lt;SEP&gt;"When dealing with tables, the P strategy ensures that tables under a certain size (`table_max`) remain whole, and large tables are sliced along row boundaries and re-wrapped as `&lt;table&gt;` elements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every merge must satisfy four constraints: size, table role, level, and parent-heading path.&lt;SEP&gt;"Split-table slices cannot absorb forward, be absorbed backward, nor join batched tail absorption.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOKEN COUNTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Token counting is based on the tokenizer "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PEER MERGING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Peer merging is a process that occurs when `2.3` is still less than `target_ideal`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOUNDARY AMBIGUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Boundary ambiguity is a concept where a body line begins with `#␠` and is misjudged as a heading line.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Rules are provided for long blocks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEXT-OVERLAP EXTRACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Text-overlap extraction is based on the tokenizer "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAPER.PDF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Document `paper.pdf` with mineru-P settings for pdf format."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2.3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"VERSION NUMBER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"`2.3` is a version number related to the peer merging process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIZE CONSTRAINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONSTRAINT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every merge must satisfy a size constraint.&lt;SEP&gt;"The size constraint requires the merged real text token count not to exceed `target_max`.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE-GRAINED SECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Rules are provided for fine-grained sections.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINERU-P&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CHUNKING STRATEGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Chunking strategy mineru-P is used for the document paper.pdf."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TARGET_IDEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"THRESHOLD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Text-chunk ideal target is 1500 tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy considers `target_max` as a hard cap for chunk sizes and `target_ideal` as a soft target, ensuring chunks do not exceed a certain token limit while still being semantically meaningful."&lt;SEP&gt;"The effect merges clauses toward near `target_ideal`.&lt;SEP&gt;"`target_ideal` is a threshold for the peer merging process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE ROLE CONSTRAINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONSTRAINT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every merge must satisfy a table role constraint.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERLAP INVARIANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Overlap invariants delimit where text duplication is allowed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FALLBACK PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Fallback protection ensures the document is not silently dropped due to missing sidecar."|</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEADING AND PARAGRAPH STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The normal path is driven by heading and paragraph structure "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAIL ABSORPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Tail absorption is a process that occurs when the whole is below `small_tail_threshold`."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tail absorption is initiated either.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEVEL CONSTRAINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONSTRAINT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every merge must satisfy a level constraint.&lt;SEP&gt;"The level constraint requires same-level merging between blocks of equal `level` and allows shallow-absorbs-deep absorption.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION BOUNDARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Section boundaries never overlap, avoiding mis-attribution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARACTER-LEVEL SPLITTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Retreats to character-level splitting when structural capability fails."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL_TAIL_THRESHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"THRESHOLD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Tail-fragment absorption threshold is 250 tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;"`small_tail_threshold` is a threshold related to the tail absorption process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENT-HEADING-PATH CONSISTENCY CONSTRAINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONSTRAINT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Every merge must satisfy a parent-heading-path consistency constraint.&lt;SEP&gt;"The parent-heading-path consistency constraint is a key to avoiding cross-topic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;"This constraint ensures that the path of parent headings is consistent, preventing cross-topic merging of adjacent clauses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEGRADATION BEHAVIOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Degrades to R-strategy character splitting if header does not fit."|</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL TOKEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOKEN"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The real token is a measure within the tail absorption process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG BODY TEXT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Long body text within a section may overlap.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLOCKS_PATH MISSING UNREADABLE NO VALID CONTENT LINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TRIGGER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Missing, unreadable, or no valid content lines in `blocks_path` leads to degrading to `chunking_by_recursive_character()`."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TARGET_MAX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"THRESHOLD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Text-chunk hard cap is 2000 tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;"The P strategy considers `target_max` as a hard cap for chunk sizes and `target_ideal` as a soft target, ensuring chunks do not exceed a certain token limit while still being semantically meaningful."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `target_max` limit for a single-row table is checked in this scenario."&lt;SEP&gt;"The `target_max` threshold is used in AnchorSplit to define the maximum allowed size of a block. It can be exceeded when prepending parent heading line(s)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The maximum token limit for a single-row table that can be split without exceeding the limit."&lt;SEP&gt;"The size constraint refers to the threshold `target_max`.&lt;SEP&gt;"Token count must not exceed `target_max`.&lt;SEP&gt;"`target_max` is a threshold that bounds the re-measured real token.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84c6dc4e56f32ef79bfc21440cf2ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b99487e9daf270364082281b0c65f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE-GRAINED CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The effect involves many 100–300 token fine-grained clauses.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAGMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Fragments split from one content line may maintain R-style overlap.&lt;SEP&gt;"Multiple fragments split from one content line may keep R-style overlap.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dfdc14720aca7f1c8740b02182c2b4d8</data>
</node>
