<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once that is done, the engine automatically gets: a dedicated (or shared) parsing concurrency pool, three engine-selection methods (filename hints / `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` routing rules / API `parse_engine` parameter), suffix capability validation, and single-file debug support through `python -m lightrag.parser.cli --engine &lt;name&gt;`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When using `queue_group=&quot;native&quot;` to share the built-in pool, `concurrency` does not take effect (pool size is determined by `max_parallel_parse_native`; ignored spec-level `concurrency` values are recorded as warning logs at batch startup).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The registry is a module-level singleton: after calling `register_parser` in a test, clean up with `finally: registry._REGISTRY.pop(&quot;myengine&quot;, None)` (see `tests/parser/test_registry.py`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. **`LIGHTRAG_PARSER` rules**: for example, `LIGHTRAG_PARSER=&quot;foo:myengine,pdf:mineru&quot;` (matched by suffix glob; the first match wins);&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Entry-point loading logic: see `tests/parser/test_plugins.py` (monkeypatch `lightrag.parser.plugins.entry_points` to inject a fake entry point; the `plugins._loaded` flag must be reset).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Debug CLI**: `python -m lightrag.parser.cli sample.foo --engine myengine` works directly (`main()` loads plugins before building `--engine` choices). For engines without sidecars (`blocks_path=&quot;&quot;`), the CLI prints a plain-text summary instead of a block summary; engines inheriting `ExternalParserBase` automatically get raw cache display and `--force-reparse` support;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For architecture background, see RFC #3197; for the sidecar file format, see `docs/LightRAGSidecarFormat.md`; for CLI usage, see `docs/ParserDebugCLI.md`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Lightweight local engines (such as `legacy`) fit this mode, while external-service engines should usually use a dedicated group so slow requests do not block local parsing.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;See `tests/parser/test_plugins.py` for more information.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. **Default**: `legacy`;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Embedded library usage** (using the `LightRAG` class directly without going through the server or CLI): call this once before building the pipeline:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once a `BaseParser` subclass is implemented, the engine needs to be registered to be recognized and used by the LightRAG system. This registration is done through a `ParserSpec` object, which contains metadata about the engine such as its name, version, and supported file types. The entry point for automatic discovery of these `ParserSpec` objects is the `lightrag.parsers` directory, where third-party engines can provide their own modules that are discovered at runtime by LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`fake_rag` only needs to provide `_persist_parsed_full_docs` / `_resolve_source_file_for_parser` / `full_docs` / `doc_status` (see `build_debug_rag()` in `lightrag/parser/debug.py`, or the minimal `_FakeRag` in `tests/parser/test_legacy_parser.py`).&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG automatically discovers third-party engines through the `lightrag.parsers` entry-point group (`lightrag/parser/plugins.py`). A third-party package only needs to:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;u` / `docling`) are determined by LightRAG instance fields `max_parallel_parse_*` (constructor overrides are supported); a third-party dedicated group uses the `concurrency` value from the group's sole owner spec; **only one** spec in a group may declare `concurrency`, otherwise batch startup fails;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When API upload explicitly passes `parse_engine=&quot;myengine&quot;`, that engine is fixed directly (stored in the `PENDING_PARSE` row and honored verbatim by the worker; unsupported suffixes are FAILED instead of silently falling back). Engines that register `endpoint_configured` are skipped by routing when the endpoint is not configured (hint/rule validation also shows the `endpoint_requirement` prompt);&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Loading semantics: idempotent per process (repeated calls are no-ops); **if a single plugin raises an exception, it is only logged and skipped**. It does not affect other plugins or built-in engines, and it does not block server startup. However, that engine will be unavailable, so watch for `[parser-plugins]` lines in startup logs.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `BaseParser` subclass must implement the `parse` method, which is the entry point for the parsing logic. This method takes a `ParseContext` object as an argument, which contains all the necessary information about the document to be parsed, such as the document identifier, file path, and content data. The implementation of the `parse` method should handle the parsing logic and return a `ParseResult` object, which contains the parsing results and any necessary metadata.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**1. Declare the entry point in its own `pyproject.toml`:**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG's parsing layer dispatches all parsing engines through a unified `BaseParser` contract plus the central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`). Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) and third-party engines use the exact same dispatch path: both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;&gt; If you do not want to publish a package, you can skip entry points and directly call `register_parser(...)` in your own startup script before starting/calling LightRAG. The registry is an in-process module singleton, so the effect is the same, just without &quot;install and it works&quot; behavior.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `plugins._loaded` flag must be reset.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**2. Provide a zero-argument registration function:**&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;a third-party dedicated group uses the `concurrency` value from the group's sole owner spec;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Unit-test the engine itself: bypass the CLI and directly call `get_parser(&quot;myengine&quot;).parse(ParseContext(fake_rag, doc_id, file_path, content_data))`.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-429475b51505ea7515c25bea7c5c4a00</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Engine selection priority (`lightrag/parser/routing.py`):&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After `pip install my-pkg`, it works immediately without changing LightRAG code:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**only one** spec in a group may declare `concurrency`, otherwise batch startup fails;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **Filename hint**: `report.[myengine].foo` (processing options are allowed, such as `report.[myengine-iet].foo`);&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **API Server**: `create_app()` calls `load_third_party_parsers()` **before** validating `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` routing rules, so routing rules can directly reference third-party engine names (for example, `LIGHTRAG_PARSER=&quot;foo:myengine&quot;`). File-type guarding for uploads and scans is **derived entirely from the registry plus routing at runtime**. The criterion is &quot;can this file route to an engine that supports it&quot;: a bare suffix (no hint) requires a `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` rule that routes it to your engine (otherwise the default `legacy` engine cannot handle it, so the file is rejected instead of being accepted and later FAILED during parsing); uploads with a filename hint (for example, `report.[myengine].foo`) pass without a rule; unique suffixes of engines whose endpoints are not configured do not participate (the same rule used by built-in mineru/docling image formats). **Practical recommendation: when publishing a third-party engine, tell users to configure the matching `LIGHTRAG_PARSER=&quot;foo:myengine&quot;` rule in deployment docs**, so bare-filename uploads and directory scans work automatically;&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSE METHOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `parse` method is the entry point for the parsing logic in the `BaseParser` subclass. It processes the document and returns a `ParseResult` object.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSERESULT OBJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `ParseResult` object contains the parsing results and any necessary metadata, which is returned by the `parse` method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TESTING RECOMMENDATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Testing recommendations are provided("hyper-relation"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75f938ff935899b319e2b8e1890da167</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEDICATED PARSING CONCURRENCY POOL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The engine automatically gets a dedicated parsing concurrency pool for efficient parsing operations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAGSIDECARFORMAT.MD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LightRAGSidecarFormat.md provides information about the sidecar file format used by LightRAG.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSECONTEXT OBJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `ParseContext` object contains all the necessary information about the document to be parsed, such as the document identifier, file path, and content data. It's used by the `parse` method.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHARED PARSING CONCURRENCY POOL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The engine automatically gets a shared parsing concurrency pool for efficient parsing operations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT IDENTIFIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The document identifier is a unique identifier for the document being parsed, used for tracking and referencing the document.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILT-IN ENGINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) are parsing engines that come pre-installed with LightRAG. They use the same dispatch path as third-party engines, without any special cases for built-in engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEBUG CLI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The debug CLI is a command-line interface that drives parsing through the `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))` process, without any special cases for built-in engines. It's used for debugging and testing purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THREE ENGINE-SELECTION METHODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The engine automatically gets three methods for engine selection: filename hints, `LIGHTRAG_PARSER` routing rules, and the `parse_engine` API parameter.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSERDEBUGCLI.MD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"ParserDebugCLI.md provides information about the CLI usage for debugging and testing the parsing engine.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CENTRAL ENGINE REGISTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`) manages and dispatches parsing engines through the `BaseParser` contract. It handles both built-in and third-party engines without special cases for built-in engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASEPARSER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `BaseParser` contract is a unified interface for all parsing engines to be dispatched by LightRAG's parsing layer. It's used for both built-in and third-party engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A third-party package must implement a `BaseParser` subclass for the new parsing engine.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFIX CAPABILITY VALIDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The engine automatically gets suffix capability validation to ensure compatibility with different file types.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BASEPARSER SUBCLASS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A `BaseParser` subclass is a custom implementation of the parsing engine that conforms to the `BaseParser` contract provided by LightRAG. It's the core of a third-party engine implementation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPORTED FILE TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `ParserSpec` object lists the file types supported by the parsing engine, which is important for the LightRAG system to know which files to use it on.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ENGINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Third-party engines are additional parsing engines that can be registered and used with LightRAG, using the same dispatch path as built-in engines without special cases for built-in engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTENT DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The content data is the actual text or data of the document, used by the `parse` method to perform parsing operations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIPELINE WORKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Pipeline workers are components of the system that drive parsing through the `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))` process. They handle parsing without special cases for built-in engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SINGLE-FILE DEBUG SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The engine automatically gets single-file debug support through `python -m lightrag.parser.cli --engine &lt;name&gt;` for easier debugging and testing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSERSPEC OBJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A `ParserSpec` object is a metadata container for a parsing engine, including its name, version, and supported file types. It's used for registration and recognition by the LightRAG system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAG.PARSERS DIRECTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE_COMPONENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The `lightrag.parsers` directory is the entry point for automatic discovery of third-party engines' `ParserSpec` objects. It allows LightRAG to dynamically load and use these engines.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTRAG'S PARSING LAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"LightRAG's parsing layer is a unified system for dispatching parsing engines through a `BaseParser` contract and a central registry. It handles built-in and third-party engines without special cases for built-in engines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARSING LOGIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The parsing logic is the set of rules and operations that the `parse` method uses to process the document and produce the parsing results.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A third-party package must register a `ParserSpec` for the new parsing engine, which can be done automatically through the `lightrag.parsers` entry point.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</node>
