<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Factories enable the registration of custom implementations.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This allows deep customization to support your own implementations of models, storage, and so on that we haven't built into the core library.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Individual workflows are described in the dataflow page.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This model is designed to be an abstraction over the underlying data storage technology, and to provide a common interface for the GraphRAG system to interact with.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cache layer is added to handle errors from LLM interactions.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following subsystems use a factory pattern that allows you to register your own implementations:">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Because of these potential error cases, we've added a cache layer around LLM interactions.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Errors in LLM APIs can be caused by network issues.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Cached results are returned for repeated input sets.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The GraphRAG library was designed with LLM interactions in mind, and a common setback when working with LLM APIs is various errors due to network latency, throttling, etc..">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;All of these factories allow you to register an impl using any string name you would like, even overriding built-in ones directly.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When completion requests are made using the same input set (prompt and tuning parameters), we return a cached result if one exists.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cache layer is part of the GraphRAG library.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Custom implementations can be registered using factories.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The outputs of the indexing engine are aligned to a knowledge model called the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cache layer handles errors from LLM interactions.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Custom implementations can override built-in ones.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Below is the core GraphRAG indexing pipeline. Individual workflows are described in detail in the [dataflow](./default_dataflow.md) page.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The indexing engine operates in the Default Configuration Mode.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This allows our indexer to be more resilient to network issues, to act idempotently, and to provide a more efficient end-user experience.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In order to support the GraphRAG system, the outputs of the indexing engine (in the Default Configuration Mode) are aligned to a knowledge model we call the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Cached results are used for repeated inputs.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ abstracts the data storage technology.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The indexing pipeline consists of core workflows described in the dataflow page.&quot;">
