</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA STORAGE TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The model is an abstraction over the underlying data storage technology."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Let's take a look at how the default-configuration workflow transforms text documents into the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_. This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ is a knowledge model designed to be an abstraction over the underlying data storage technology and to provide a common interface for the GraphRAG system to interact with."&lt;SEP&gt;"The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ is a knowledge model that aligns the outputs of the indexing engine."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INPUT READER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SUBSYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The input reader subsystem allows for the implementation of custom input document readers.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Factories allow the registration of implementations using any string name, even overriding built-in ones directly.&lt;SEP&gt;"Factories are used to register custom implementations in the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Custom implementations can be used to override built-in ones in the system.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ERRORS FROM LLM INTERACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROBLEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The cache layer manages errors that occur during LLM interactions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CACHE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SUBSYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The cache subsystem allows for the creation of custom cache storage locations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;_GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"KNOWLEDGE_MODEL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ is an abstraction layer for the underlying data storage technology.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEATED INPUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Cached results are employed when the same inputs are repeated.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CACHE LAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"A cache layer has been added around LLM interactions to handle potential error cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cache layer is implemented to manage errors from LLM interactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORY PATTERN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PATTERN"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Several subsystems within GraphRAG use a factory pattern for registering and retrieving provider implementations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOGGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SUBSYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The logger subsystem allows for the creation of custom log writing locations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT CONFIGURATION MODE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"MODE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The indexing engine operates in the Default Configuration Mode."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPHRAG SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ provides a common interface for the GraphRAG system to interact with.&lt;SEP&gt;"The default prompts are designed to work with the GraphRAG system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ac2e652be419ab7d9491e584ea178d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LLM APIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"API"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The GraphRAG library works with LLM APIs that can have errors due to network latency, throttling, etc."&lt;SEP&gt;"The library is designed to interact with LLM APIs that can encounter errors due to network issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOM PROVIDER IMPLEMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Custom provider implementations can be registered through the factories.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The ':module: graphrag.cli.main' indicates a specific module within the graphrag library.&lt;SEP&gt;"The GraphRAG library was designed with LLM interactions in mind."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cache layer is included in the GraphRAG library.&lt;SEP&gt;"The page documents the command-line interface of the graphrag library.&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'CLI Reference' suggests the text is a reference guide for the graphrag library's command-line interface.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CUSTOMIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The factory pattern allows for deep customization to support user implementations of models and storage that are not built into the core library."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STORAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SUBSYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The storage subsystem allows for the creation of custom storage providers.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TOOL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"After running the indexing pipeline, an output folder is created."&lt;SEP&gt;"The indexing pipeline includes core workflows that are detailed in the dataflow page."&lt;SEP&gt;"We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph for our memory model."&lt;SEP&gt;"The indexing pipeline processes the data and produces an output folder.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-753b54f11987ea184b7a7af0bb9e15ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATAFLOW PAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The individual workflows are detailed in a separate dataflow page.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLETION REQUESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Completion requests with the same input set result in a cached result if available."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRATION OF CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ACTION"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Factories facilitate the registration of custom implementations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEXER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PACKAGE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The cached result allows the indexer to be more resilient to network issues and to provide a more efficient end-user experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"The docpages for the Indexer package provide detailed information about the GraphRAG Indexer sub-system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CACHED RESULTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Cached results are provided for repeated input sets to improve efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NETWORK ISSUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROBLEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Errors in LLM APIs can arise from network issues.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPHRAG INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PIPELINE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The core of the GraphRAG indexing pipeline is described in detail in the dataflow page."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LANGUAGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The language model subsystem allows for the registration of custom model providers.&lt;SEP&gt;"The reasoning tasks, including entity and relationship extraction, entity summarization, relationship summarization, claim extraction, and community report generation, are performed by a language model in Standard GraphRAG."&lt;SEP&gt;"The standard indexing pipeline uses a language model to extract the graph for the memory model, which is the basis for the memory model."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIPELINE + WORKFLOWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SUBSYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The pipeline + workflows subsystem allows for the implementation of custom workflow steps or entire pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</node>
