  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPTH LEVEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The depth level of 0 suggests the documentation's level of detail for the 'app' command.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The ':prog_name: graphrag' indicates the program or command is named 'graphrag'.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMAND-LINE INTERFACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The command-line interface of the graphrag library is used for operations indicated by the commands in the documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;"The page documents the command-line interface of the graphrag library.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLI REFERENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The term 'CLI Reference' suggests the text is a reference guide for the graphrag library's command-line interface.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPHRAG PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The ':command: app' indicates a specific command within the 'graphrag' program.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"SOFTWARE FEATURE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The ':module: graphrag.cli.main' indicates a specific module within the graphrag library.&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions the module 'graphrag.cli.main' which is part of the graphrag library's internal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;:module: graphrag.cli.main is mentioned in the documentation of the graphrag library.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;0&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"VALUE"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The ':depth: 0' indicates the documentation is at the highest level of abstraction for the 'app' command.&lt;SEP&gt;"The depth level of 0 suggests the documentation's level of detail for the 'app' command.&lt;SEP&gt;"The documentation indicates a 'depth' of 0, which may mean it does not provide specifics of the commands.&lt;SEP&gt;:depth: 0 is mentioned in the documentation of the graphrag library.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFERENCE GUIDE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The term 'CLI Reference' suggests the text is a reference guide for the graphrag library's command-line interface.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following entity types are provided. The fields here represent the fields that are text-embedded by default.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Now that we have a usable graph of entities and relationships, we want to understand their community structure. These give us explicit ways of understanding the organization of our graph.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm is a recursive community-clustering algorithm that is used to generate a hierarchy of communities.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Note: if you are using the [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option, entity and relationship extraction will be performed using NLP to conserve LLM resources, and claim extraction will always be skipped.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Community Report` - The contents of each community are summarized into a generated report, useful for human reading and downstream search.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At this point, some bookkeeping work is performed and we export the **Community Reports** tables.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Document` - An input document into the system. These either represent individual rows in a CSV or individual .txt files.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, we generate a hierarchy of entity communities using the Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm. This method will apply a recursive community-clustering to our graph until we reach a community-size threshold. This will allow us to understand the community structure of our graph and provide a way to navigate and summarize the graph at different levels of granularity.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The final step in the process is the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables, which contain the results of the graph augmentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Let's take a look at how the default-configuration workflow transforms text documents into the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_. This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `TextUnit` - A chunk of text to analyze. The size of these chunks, their overlap, and whether they adhere to any data boundaries may be configured below.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once our graph augmentation steps are complete, the final **Entities**, **Relationships**, and **Communities** tables are exported.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Community reports provide a high-level understanding of the graph at different levels of granularity, allowing for a scoped view of the graph's content.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option is a tool that allows for entity and relationship extraction, as well as claim extraction, to conserve LLM resources. This option is particularly useful when working with large datasets where efficient processing is required.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Entity` - An entity extracted from a TextUnit. These represent people, places, events, or some other entity-model that you provide.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At this point, we have a functional graph of entities and relationships and a hierarchy of communities for the entities.">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text embedding step generates embeddings for entities, text units, and community reports, which are then stored in a vector store for downstream vector search.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The output of the graph extraction step includes a subgraph for each text unit, which contains a list of entities and relationships extracted from the raw text.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Relationship` - A relationship between two entities.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this first step of graph extraction, we process each text-unit to extract entities and relationships out of the raw text using the LLM. The output of this step is a subgraph-per-TextUnit containing a list of **entities** with a _title_, _type_, and _description_, and a list of **relationships** with a _source_, _target_, and _description_.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Now we want to build on the communities data and generate reports for each community. This gives us a high-level understanding of the graph at several points of graph granularity. For example, if community A is the top-level community, we'll get a report about the entire graph. If the community is lower-level, we'll get a report about a local cluster.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;tu --&gt; ce[Claim Extraction] &quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The knowledge model is a specification for data outputs that conform to our data-model definition.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;```mermaid">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">6.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The merging of subgraphs involves combining entities with the same title and type into a single entry, and similarly, relationships with the same source and target into a single entry.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Covariate` - Extracted claim information, which contains statements about entities which may be time-bound.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, we generate a summary of each community using the LLM. This will allow us to understand the distinct information contained within each community and provide a scoped understanding of the graph, from either a high-level or a low-level perspective. These reports contain an executive overview and reference the key entities, relationships, and claims within the community sub-structure.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;These subgraphs are merged together - any entities with the same _title_ and _type_ are merged by creating an array of their descriptions. Similarly, any relationships with the same _source_ and _target_ are merged by creating an array of their descriptions.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You can find these definitions in the python/graphrag/graphrag/model folder within the GraphRAG repository.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Community detection is a crucial step in understanding the organization of the graph, as it identifies communities of entities that are closely related.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Community` - Once the graph of entities and relationships is built, we perform hierarchical community detection on them to create a clustering structure.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">16.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, each _community report_ is then summarized via the LLM for shorthand use.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME-BOUND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The extracted claim information contains statements about entities which may be time-bound."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIS PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEXT EMBEDDINGS &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT "</data>
  <data key="d4">"Text embeddings are generated for artifacts that require downstream vector search.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHASE3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"```mermaid title: Dataflow Overview flowchart TB subgraph phase1[Phase 1: Compose TextUnits] documents[Documents] --&gt; chunk[Chunk] chunk --&gt; textUnits[Text Units] end subgraph phase2[Phase 2: Document Processing] documents --&gt; link_to_text_units[Link to TextUnits] textUnits --&gt; link_to_text_units link_to_text_units --&gt; document_outputs[Documents Table] end subgraph phase3[Phase 3 Graph Extraction] textUnits --&gt; graph_extract[Entity &amp; Relationship Extraction] graph_extract --&gt; graph_summarize[Entity &amp; Relationship Summarization] graph_summarize --&gt; claim_extraction[Claim Extraction] claim_extraction --&gt; graph_outputs[Graph Tables] end subgraph phase4[Phase 4: Graph Augmentation] graph_outputs --&gt; community_detect[Community Detection] community_detect --&gt; community_outputs[Communities Table] end subgraph phase5[Phase 5: Community Summarization] community_outputs --&gt; summarized_communities[Community Summarization] summarized_communities --&gt; community_report_outputs[Community Reports Table] end subgraph phase6[Phase 6: Text Embeddings] textUnits --&gt; text_embed[Text Embedding] graph_outputs --&gt; description_embed[Description Embedding] community_report_outputs --&gt; content_embed[Content Embedding] end</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TU &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"TEXT-UNIT "</data>
  <data key="d4">"tu is a text unit that is being processed for claim extraction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL FOLDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"FOLDER"</data>
  <data key="d4">"These definitions are in the python/graphrag/graphrag/model folder within the GraphRAG repository."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBGRAPHS &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT "</data>
  <data key="d4">"Subgraphs are merged to combine entities and relationships with identical attributes.&lt;SEP&gt;"Subgraphs are merged together during the graph extraction process.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM EXTRACTION &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Claim Extraction is a type of indexing prompt.&lt;SEP&gt;"Claim extraction is a process that is conserved by using FastGraphRAG.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15ee7c6b211b6ac87701bf817a50f7cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRAPH AUGMENTATION &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS "</data>
  <data key="d4">"Graph augmentation is the process of generating the final Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables.&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of graph augmentation results in the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"ENTITY_MODEL"</data>
  <data key="d4">"These entities represent people, places, events, or some other entity-model that you provide."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY DATA &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT "</data>
  <data key="d4">"Community data is used to generate reports for each community.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Communities are generated by Leiden and are hierarchical.&lt;SEP&gt;"Once the graph of entities and relationships is built, we perform hierarchical community detection on them to create a clustering structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contents of each community are summarized into a generated report, useful for human reading and downstream search."&lt;SEP&gt;"The communities list includes a community field which is a Leiden-generated cluster ID for the community.&lt;SEP&gt;"The community_reports list includes a community field which is the short ID of the community the report applies to.&lt;SEP&gt;"The summarized reports are for each community.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f79b90a7af3598028d581d94c6d76678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY REPORT TEXT &quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT "</data>
  <data key="d4">"Community report text is embedded by default.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
