<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `settings.yaml` contains the settings for the pipeline. You can modify this file to change the settings for the pipeline.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;⚠️ GraphRAG can consume a lot of LLM resources! We strongly recommend starting with the tutorial dataset here until you understand how the system works, and consider experimenting with fast/inexpensive models first before committing to a big indexing job.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">5.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If running in OpenAI mode, you only need to update the value of `GRAPHRAG_API_KEY` in the `.env` file with your OpenAI API key.&quot;">
