<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each of these prompts may be overridden by writing a custom prompt file in plaintext. We use token-replacements in the form of `{token_name}`, and the descriptions for the available tokens can be found below.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15ee7c6b211b6ac87701bf817a50f7cb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;However, it is quite common to want to tune the prompts to better suit your specific use case.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">8.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15ee7c6b211b6ac87701bf817a50f7cb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We provide a means for you to do this by allowing you to specify a custom prompt file, which will each use a series of token-replacements internally.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15ee7c6b211b6ac87701bf817a50f7cb</data>
</node>
<node id="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The GraphRAG indexer, by default, will run with a handful of prompts that are designed to work well in the broad context of knowledge discovery.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">hyperedge</data>
  <data key="d1">7.0</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15ee7c6b211b6ac87701bf817a50f7cb</data>
</node>
