<node id="&quot;HYBRID TECHNIQUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"FastGraphRAG is a hybrid technique that incorporates both language model reasoning and NLP methods for faster and cheaper indexing alternatives to Standard GraphRAG."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONING TASKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Standard GraphRAG uses a language model for all reasoning tasks such as entity extraction, relationship extraction, entity summarization, relationship summarization, claim extraction, and community report generation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTEXT WINDOW CONTENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"GraphRAG is a platform for our research into RAG indexing methods that produce optimal context window content for language models."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEMORY MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The standard indexing pipeline extracts a graph based on which the memory model is built, and this page documents those options."&lt;SEP&gt;"We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph for our memory model."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NAMED ENTITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"In Standard GraphRAG, named entities are extracted from each text unit, and a description is provided by the LLM.&lt;SEP&gt;"Named entities are extracted from each text unit in Standard GraphRAG."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The standard indexing pipeline uses a language model to extract the graph for the memory model."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAIR OF ENTITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The LLM describes the relationship between each pair of entities in each text unit.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RAG INDEXING METHODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"GraphRAG is a platform for research into RAG indexing methods that produce optimal context window content for language models."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD GRAPHRAG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"This is the method described in the original blog post, which uses a language model for all reasoning tasks, including entity and relationship extraction, entity summarization, relationship summarization, claim extraction, and community report generation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LANGUAGE MODELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"GraphRAG is a platform for our research into RAG indexing methods that produce optimal context window content for language models."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEXT UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"OBJECT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"Claims are extracted and described from each text unit by the LLM, as an optional task.&lt;SEP&gt;"Named entities are extracted from each text unit in Standard GraphRAG, which are then provided with descriptions by the LLM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Named entities are extracted from each text unit, and the LLM provides a description for these entities.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM creates a single summary by combining descriptions of entities found across all text units.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM describes relationships between pairs of entities within each text unit.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM generates a single summary for relationships by combining descriptions from all text units.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SINGLE SUMMARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d4">"The LLM combines descriptions for each entity found across the text units into a single summary.&lt;SEP&gt;"The LLM creates a single summary by combining descriptions of relationships found across all text units.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FASTGRAPHRAG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">entity</data>
  <data key="d3">"METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d4">"FastGraphRAG is a method that uses traditional natural language processing (NLP) methods in addition to some language model reasoning to develop a faster and cheaper indexing alternative to Standard GraphRAG."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</node>
