<edge source="&quot;ENV&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`.env` is **not** chowned, so the host keeps ownership and you can edit it freely. It only needs to be *readable* by uid 1000, which the default `0644` permission satisfies.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12c55028ed60ac15f2cc10cf11febe66</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENV&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Please copy this file to the startup directory and rename it to `.env`. After that, you can modify the parameters related to the LLM and Embedding models in the `.env` file.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After building a custom tag, update the `postgres.image` value in the generated `docker-compose.final.yml` to point at that tag. On later setup wizard reruns, existing wizard-managed service images are preserved.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8fbdf17e3767d2cc6b62e0485bfedf7c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The official images run the server as a non-root user (lightrag, uid/gid 1000) to satisfy CIS Docker Benchmark 4.1. The behavior is designed so existing deployments keep working on upgrade:&quot;&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ea9b2e06bd3e26acee17a3b67d9a834</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text gives an example of how the resolution chain works, using `CHUNK_R_OVERLAP_SIZE=42` and `LightRAG(chunk_overlap_token_size=2)`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">75.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8270352cccb49b2bcd5b1d3ab329e22b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The process of resolving the stored document parser engine and the role of environment variables in tuning system parameters are highlighted. Environment variables control system behavior, with their values affecting the system's performance and functionality. These values are read at the construction of `LightRAG` and can be adjusted through `.env` or environment variables. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG caches the parsing results of the `mineru` and `docling` engines locally. Re-uploading the same file usually does not trigger the engine to re-parse the document. To delete the parse cache, you must click the &quot;also delete file&quot; option in the delete-file dialog of the document management interface. Modifying the endpoint addresses and effective extraction parameters of the `mineru` / `docling` engines will also invalidate the cache, causing the engine to re-parse the file content on the next upload of the same file.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;```python\nfrom lightrag import LightRAG\nrag = LightRAG(working_dir=&quot;./rag_storage&quot;, ...)\nawait rag.initialize_storages()\nawait rag.ainsert(&quot;text&quot;, file_paths=&quot;doc.pdf&quot;)```&quot;">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`LightRAG(chunk_token_size=…, chunk_overlap_token_size=…)` is **tier 3** in §3.3's priority chain: &quot;legacy constructor field&quot;. Strategy-agnostic and coarse-grained default, fills only slots still empty:&quot;">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88cc39237fb1678f1803346e3c8046b6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;U path — LightRAG mandates `canonical_basename` uniqueness within the same workspace (HTTP 409 on upload / enqueue), and combined with the pipeline's serialization per document, `*.docling_raw/` has no concurrent write conflicts and needs no extra locks.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-59fa2d582eb20bc136094483fb09d31c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then add the following configuration to LightRAG's `.env` file: &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After deployment completes, write `DOCLING_DO_FORMULA_ENRICHMENT=true` into LightRAG's `.env` to enable LaTeX equation recognition.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`native` is LightRAG's built-in structured content extractor that runs **fully locally**: it does not depend on external services such as MinerU / Docling, the extraction stage never calls a VLM, and it works out of the box with no deployment. Its runtime dependencies are only `python-docx` + `defusedxml` (required); the markdown path additionally relies on the **optional** `cairosvg` for SVG rasterization (when missing, the SVG is skipped with a warning and the rest of the content is unaffected).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3823ede94fd87dec38980f3c5e83b533</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios. It outlines key principles and installation scenarios for end users, contributors, and for testing package builds. It also describes how to create distribution packages and the automated release process through GitHub Actions. The guide provides a quick reference for different scenarios and instructions for Bun installation. The file structure of the project is outlined, and troubleshooting steps are provided for common issues with the installation and building process. The document ends with a summary indicating the completion of the guide.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Use the interactive setup wizard when you want LightRAG to guide you through the configuration instead of editing `.env` by hand.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3-large is a document that includes several configuration options for a service called LightRAG. The configuration is detailed in various steps that pertain to different aspects of the service, including embedding dimensions, data storage, reranking, and deployment settings. This text seems to be a reference document for setting up and operating LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The configuration options for LightRAG include setting up the environment for the service to function properly. This involves initializing the necessary parameters and configurations before starting the service. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</edge>
