</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG necessitates the integration of both an LLM (Large Language Model) and an Embedding Model to effectively execute document indexing and querying operations.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When LightRAG uses multimodal-capable content parsing engines such as native/mineru/docling to extract file content, it splits &quot;body text + multimodal objects + parsing metadata&quot; into a `*.parsed/` directory.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The analysis result dict `llm_analyze_result` is written by LightRAG and may be appended or overwritten; parsers should not pre-populate it.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The surrounding content is automatically injected by LightRAG during the analysis stage; it does not need to be actively written into the sidecar by the document parsing engine.">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIGHTRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG requires that filenames (`document_name`) be unique within the same workspace (knowledge base). &quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
