<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The image starts as root and drops privileges at runtime (the pattern used by the official PostgreSQL/Redis images), so the *running process* is non-root while the image's configured `USER` is still root. Scanners that judge CIS 4.1 purely from the `USER` directive may still flag the image even though no server process runs as root.&quot;" target="&quot;ROOT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">60.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12c55028ed60ac15f2cc10cf11febe66</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The image starts as root and drops privileges at runtime (the pattern used by the official PostgreSQL/Redis images), so the *running process* is non-root while the image's configured `USER` is still root. Scanners that judge CIS 4.1 purely from the `USER` directive may still flag the image even though no server process runs as root.&quot;" target="&quot;POSTGRESQL/REDIS IMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12c55028ed60ac15f2cc10cf11febe66</data>
