<edge source="&quot;MAKE ENV-BASE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Run commands from the repository root. The `make env-*` targets automatically choose a compatible Bash 4+ interpreter. Use the documented `make env-*` targets rather than invoking the setup script yourself. `make env-base` is the normal starting point because it creates the initial `.env`. `make env-storage` and `make env-server` require an existing `.env`. If you choose any wizard-managed Docker service, the wizard also prepares LightRAG for the Docker startup path.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d78cb23a1beadc3e7c5c84bc0595ed1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAKE ENV-BASE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For Docker deployment details beyond the interactive wizard, see [DockerDeployment.md](./DockerDeployment.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">340.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAKE ENV-BASE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- For Docker deployment details beyond the interactive wizard, see [DockerDeployment.md](./DockerDeployment.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7a530e3034e426f2ca111c6843c2a28</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER COMPOSE UP&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The server is started with `docker compose up`, and can be run in the background with `-d`.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER COMPOSE UP&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Running `docker compose up` starts the server.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMERS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Software packages requiring `transformers`, `torch`, or `cuda` will not be included in the offline dependency group. Consequently, document extraction tools such as Docling, as well as local LLM models like Hugging Face and LMDeploy, are outside the scope of offline installation support. These high-compute-resource-demanding services should not be integrated into LightRAG. Docling will be decoupled and deployed as a standalone service.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMERS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG uses dynamic package installation (`pipmaster`) for optional features based on file types and configurations. In offline environments, these dynamic installations will fail. This guide shows you how to pre-install all necessary dependencies and cache files.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER COMPOSE UP -D&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then execute `docker compose up -d` in that directory to start the service.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following uses a Docker-based docling-serve deployment as an example, giving the complete steps from image download to model mounting.">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text provides instructions on how to start the service and verify its health. This is done by running a command to start the Docker containers and another to check the service's status. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If you deploy LightRAG using Docker, there is no need to refer to this document, as the LightRAG Docker image is pre-configured for offline operation.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Install with Docker (without plugins):&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;docker run -d -p 9200:9200 -e \&quot;discovery.type=single-node\&quot; \n  -e \&quot;OPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=&lt;custom-admin-password&gt;\&quot; \n  opensearchproject/opensearch:latest&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">185.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Docker image for PostgreSQL can be used for ease of installation.">
