<edge source="&quot;PGGRAPHSTORAGE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here is how workspaces are implemented for different types of storage: for local file-based databases, data isolation is achieved through workspace subdirectories; for databases that store data in collections, it's done by adding a workspace prefix to the collection name; for Qdrant vector database, data isolation is achieved through payload-based partitioning (Qdrant's recommended multitenancy approach); for relational databases, data isolation is achieved by adding a `workspace` field to the tables for logical data separation; for graph databases, logical data isolation is achieved through labels; for OpenSearch, data isolation is achieved through index name prefixes.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
