<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The process of resolving the stored document parser engine and the role of environment variables in tuning system parameters are highlighted. Environment variables control system behavior, with their values affecting the system's performance and functionality. These values are read at the construction of `LightRAG` and can be adjusted through `.env` or environment variables. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text document discusses various aspects of the LightRAG parser and its chunking strategies, including the responsibilities of process_options and chunk_options, as well as the environment variables involved in configuring the chunker parameter settings.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f245702d4300114f106e260ea1773771</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**How changes take effect**: all parameters are passed in via `.env` (or environment variables), read once at `LightRAG` construction; restart the service after changing them.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f95d6aa1ada1a445751726c13f57d913</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;A local reranker that exposes a Cohere-compatible API can be used by setting the appropriate environment variables. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server. There is an example environment variable file named `env.example` in the root directory of the project. Please copy this file to the startup directory and rename it to `.env`. After that, you can modify the parameters related to the LLM and Embedding models in the `.env` file. It is important to note that the LightRAG Server will load the environment variables from `.env`&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is important to note that the LightRAG Server will load the environment variables from `.env` into the system environment variables each time it starts. **LightRAG Server will prioritize the settings in the system environment variables to .env file**.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;It is recommended to use environment variables to configure the LightRAG Server, which allows for flexible and dynamic settings that can be adjusted without restarting the server.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Set the max_tokens to **prevent excessively long or endless output loop** during the entity relationship extraction phase for Large Language Model (LLM) responses.  The purpose of setting max_tokens parameter is to truncate LLM output before timeouts occur, thereby preventing document extraction failures. This addresses issues where certain text blocks (e.g., tables or citations) containing numerous entities and relationships can lead to overly long or even endless loop outputs from LLMs. This setting is particularly crucial for locally deployed, smaller-parameter models.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You can select the storage implementation by configuring environment variables. For instance, prior to the initial launch of the API server, you can set the following environment variable to specify your desired storage implementation:&quot;&quot;">
