</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **`local_parse_method` is local-only.** It only affects the local MinerU request, so it is **rejected** under `MINERU_API_MODE=official` (the official API neither sends it nor folds it into the cache key — accepting it would silently do nothing).&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL_PARSE_METHOD&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Title-level correction (`title_aided`)**: MinerU uses an external LLM to correct the title hierarchy of the parsed output, improving the quality of the structured artifacts. This is especially helpful for the [P (paragraph semantic) chunking strategy](#25-file-processing-options), which depends on the title structure; the `P` chunking strategy splits by titles first, so the more accurate the title hierarchy, the better the chunking semantics. &quot;" target="&quot;TITLE-LEVEL CORRECTION FEATURE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</edge>
