<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG caches the parsing results of the `mineru` and `docling` engines locally. Re-uploading the same file usually does not trigger the engine to re-parse the document. To delete the parse cache, you must click the &quot;also delete file&quot; option in the delete-file dialog of the document management interface. Modifying the endpoint addresses and effective extraction parameters of the `mineru` / `docling` engines will also invalidate the cache, causing the engine to re-parse the file content on the next upload of the same file.&quot;" target="&quot;NATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04c25eb38b88488839f25538326154e2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Then modify `llm-aided-config.title_aided` in `mineru-lightrag.json`: fill in `api_key` and change `enable` to `true` &quot;" target="&quot;MINERU-LIGHTRAG.JSON&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-329eac639a865519f1557ce9dc303a63</data>
</edge>
