<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The legacy `apipeline_enqueue_documents` behavior of `reprocess_existing_non_processed=True` would directly delete non-PROCESSED old records and rebuild them during scan, which conflicts with the rules in §5 / §6; it has been entirely removed. This means that the system will no longer delete non-PROCESSED records by default when enqueueing new documents.&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT_DELETION_BEHAVIOR&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</edge>
