</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Automatic resume: scan handles same-named files per the classification rules in §6.4 (archive / resume / delete stub then re-enqueue), uniformly picked up by the resume rules in §7 inside the processing loop. This ensures that the system can resume processing without losing any data or reprocessing the same documents multiple times.&quot;" target="&quot;UNIFORM_PROCESSING&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- Automatic resume: scan handles same-named files per the classification rules in §6.4 (archive / resume / delete stub then re-enqueue), uniformly picked up by the resume rules in §7 inside the processing loop. This ensures that the system can resume processing without losing any data or reprocessing the same documents multiple times.&quot;" target="&quot;DATA_PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9cacff08851a81dd67802953d0d966e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **INPUT directory scan**: canonicalize the basename to be saved via `canonicalize_parser_hinted_basename`, traverse the INPUT directory for any existing same-canonical variant (with hint / without hint); 409 on hit." target="&quot;INPUT DIRECTORY SCAN&quot;">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</edge>
