<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Inside `apipeline_enqueue_documents`, &quot;read doc_status to dedupe → write `full_docs` / `doc_status`&quot; runs serially under the workspace-level `enqueue_serialize` lock. Reason: now that concurrent enqueue is allowed during the busy/scan-processing phases, two enqueues with identical content but different filenames (typical scenario: a scan-processing-phase enqueue and an upload arriving together) would, without the lock, race as follows —" target="&quot;ENQUEUE_SERIALIZE LOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b23b4175c6c0f4dc09cf75abdbc8b03</data>
</edge>
