<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- File moves only act on the current input file and do not overwrite or move existing document source files. If a file with the same name already exists at the destination, the system automatically appends `_001`, `_002`, etc., e.g., `report.pdf` is archived as `report_001.pdf`, `report_002.pdf`.&quot;" target="&quot;MINERU RAW ARTIFACTS DIRECTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- File moves only act on the current input file and do not overwrite or move existing document source files. If a file with the same name already exists at the destination, the system automatically appends `_001`, `_002`, etc., e.g., `report.pdf` is archived as `report_001.pdf`, `report_002.pdf`.&quot;" target="&quot;MINERU_RAW&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Several key points:**&quot;" target="&quot;KEY POINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- External URL images (`![](http://...)`) are **downloaded and embedded by default** (`NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_DOWNLOAD_ENABLED` defaults to `true`); a drawing is always emitted (the fetched asset on success, or an external-link fallback on failure). Downloading allows only globally-routable public IPs (both DNS-resolved IPs and every redirect target are checked, and the socket dials the validated IP directly to defeat DNS rebinding; any ambient `HTTP(S)_PROXY` is ignored); private / loopback / link-local / reserved / CGNAT (`100.64.0.0/10`) ranges are all rejected. To allow specific internal ranges, configure a CIDR allowlist via `NATIVE_MD_IMAGE_ALLOWED_NON_PUBLIC_CIDRS`. Set the flag to `false` to instead drop external images entirely (no drawing emitted, so a document whose only images are external links produces no `drawings.json`). &quot;" target="&quot;NATIVE_* &quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-45b2ffc333b4ce2b5c8d066e6c3114fc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. Parsing stage is isolated per engine**, so when mixing native/mineru/docling, you don't have to worry about a slow engine dragging another down.&quot;" target="&quot;ENGINE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. Parsing stage is isolated per engine**, so when mixing native/mineru/docling, you don't have to worry about a slow engine dragging another down.&quot;" target="&quot;PARSING STAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After the container is ready, set the following in LightRAG's `.env`:&quot;" target="&quot;LIGHTRAG'S `.ENV` SETTINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Design goals:&quot;" target="&quot;DESIGN GOALS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">140.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6cea8687c979b2611fc1fbab8d9e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a332187a994e8a8bda343951839585b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. mineru / docling default to 2**: both have high resource usage, so the default keeps parallelism modest. Lower to 1 when resources are tight (OOM / VRAM contention / failure retry); with multi-GPU or a dedicated parser server, you can raise them manually.&quot;" target="&quot;MINERU / DOCLING&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This enables LightRAG to recognize equations in documents via the local docling-serve and output them in LaTeX form.&quot;" target="&quot;LIGHTRAG RECOGNIZING EQUATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This enables LightRAG to recognize equations in documents via the local docling-serve and output them in LaTeX form.&quot;" target="&quot;FILE PROCESSING OPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. `MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` doubles as worker pool size and semaphore cap**: the pipeline creates a `Semaphore(max_parallel_insert)`, and each process worker also takes the semaphore before extraction and ingest. So even if you manually raise the worker count, the actual concurrency cap is still bounded by this value — just tune it directly.&quot;" target="&quot;MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7fd65aa6723acd55b13afedde44866</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Processing options control the behavior of a single file with respect to multimodal analysis, knowledge graph construction, and text chunking." target="&quot;TEXT CHUNKING&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Processing options control the behavior of a single file with respect to multimodal analysis, knowledge graph construction, and text chunking." target="&quot;KNOWLEDGE GRAPH CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b9c9df7784c6448099a1a7853640291</data>
</edge>
