<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text emphasizes that `CHUNK_F_SIZE` / `CHUNK_R_SIZE` / `CHUNK_V_SIZE` work differently from `CHUNK_P_SIZE` because when unset, they fall back to the top-level `chunk_token_size` (F is the default global window, R prefers a smaller target to better split sentences, while V typically wants to be enlarged to reduce over-splitting).&quot;" target="&quot;CHUNK_TOKEN_SIZE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">150.0</data>
