</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARAMETERS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The configuration options for LightRAG include setting up the environment for the service to function properly. This involves initializing the necessary parameters and configurations before starting the service. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c19f3acc7d1050e16d5cc8de39fec3a4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARAMETERS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Please copy this file to the startup directory and rename it to `.env`. After that, you can modify the parameters related to the LLM and Embedding models in the `.env` file.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARAMETERS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Parameters are passed to `MilvusIndexConfig` which applies defaults and validates them&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9de68fb6438d36191c59a2bd51dc2410</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VLM CONFIGURATION&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;| `docling` | External docling-serve parser for PDFs, Office files, Markdown/HTML, and images. Requires `DOCLING_ENDPOINT`. |&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this first step of graph extraction, we process each text-unit to extract entities and relationships out of the raw text using the LLM. The output of this step is a subgraph-per-TextUnit containing a list of **entities** with a _title_, _type_, and _description_, and a list of **relationships** with a _source_, _target_, and _description_.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;These subgraphs are merged together - any entities with the same _title_ and _type_ are merged by creating an array of their descriptions. Similarly, any relationships with the same _source_ and _target_ are merged by creating an array of their descriptions.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once our graph augmentation steps are complete, the final **Entities**, **Relationships**, and **Communities** tables are exported.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The output of the graph extraction step includes a subgraph for each text unit, which contains a list of entities and relationships extracted from the raw text.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The merging of subgraphs involves combining entities with the same title and type into a single entry, and similarly, relationships with the same source and target into a single entry.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Community detection is a crucial step in understanding the organization of the graph, as it identifies communities of entities that are closely related.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The final step in the process is the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables, which contain the results of the graph augmentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTITIES &quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text embedding step generates embeddings for entities, text units, and community reports, which are then stored in a vector store for downstream vector search.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FILENAME HINTS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Changing parser routing (LIGHTRAG_PARSER) or filename hints affects newly uploaded files. To switch an existing document to another parser engine, delete that document and upload it again.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPTIONS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Two options, picked by where the prefix-aware upstream lives. The Vite-side configuration is identical; only this one variable changes.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f50a1a569536dcf7b4109c246e92d1a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;P&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At most one of `F`, `R`, `V`, and `P` should be selected for a file.&quot;">
