</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHUNKING STRATEGIES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks produced by chunking strategies record the blockid for tracing the chunk back to its location in the sidecar. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">310.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHUNKING STRATEGIES&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- The chunking strategies `F` / `R` &quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` controls how many files are processed in parallel. `MAX_ASYNC_LLM` (deprecated alias: `MAX_ASYNC`) controls concurrent LLM calls, including extraction, merging, query keyword generation, and final answer generation. Optional staged-pipeline variables such as `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_DOCLING`, and `MAX_PARALLEL_ANALYZE` can be used for parser-heavy deployments.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Optional staged-pipeline variables such as `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_DOCLING`, and `MAX_PARALLEL_ANALYZE` can be used for parser-heavy deployments.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHUNK_OPTIONS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;These values are read at server startup and stored as a per-document `chunk_options` snapshot when a document is enqueued.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">150.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOC_ID&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;">
  <data key="d5">120.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOC_ID&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`doc_id` | `&quot;doc-&lt;md5&gt;&quot;` | Global document ID. Sidecar item IDs (`im-/tb-/eq-`) use the hash portion of `doc_id` with the `doc-` prefix removed, in order to shorten the placeholder tags embedded in body text. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANIFEST&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The CLI does not check the manifest; as long as the raw directory is non-empty, the docling-serve call is skipped&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f0e2827f0656f23647a5ad5b252099d6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPLIT_BY_CHARACTER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy **does not accept** `split_by_character` / `split_by_character_only`, because the normal path is driven by heading and paragraph structure.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPLIT_BY_CHARACTER_ONLY&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy **does not accept** `split_by_character` / `split_by_character_only`, because the normal path is driven by heading and paragraph structure.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VLM&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Max tokens value can be calculated by this formula: `LLM_TIMEOUT * llm_output_tokens/second` (i.e. `240s * 50 tokens/s = 12000`, max_tokens should smaller than 12000)&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-280dedf626baee86fc0d61cdd836e6ac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VLM&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Drawing objects are sent to a VLM for analysis; analysis results are written back.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VLM&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG supports configuring different LLMs or VLMs for different processing stages. This mechanism is useful when using a lower-cost model for extraction, a stronger model for final answers, or a dedicated vision-language model for multimodal analysis.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-082eb07a755d44999510e8f240806102</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VLM&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Four roles are currently supported: EXTRACT, KEYWORD, QUERY, and VLM. Each has a specific purpose for different stages of processing.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-082eb07a755d44999510e8f240806102</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NATIVE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy is valid for the structured output of any parser that can produce a `.blocks.jsonl` sidecar, such as `native` / `mineru` / `docling`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NATIVE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The parser guarantees &quot;the body under one heading as one basic block&quot; (native via heading-driven structural splitting, mineru / docling via their respective IR builders), with no token-threshold splitting at parse time. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NATIVE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`# docx uses native, pdf uses mineru, other supported formats use docling, all with P; unsupported formats fall back to legacy-R`&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PYTHON-DOCX&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Note**: Document processing dependencies (`pypdf`, `python-docx`, `python-pptx`, `openpyxl`) are now pre-installed with the `api` extras group and no longer require dynamic installation.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARAGRAPH_SEMANTIC&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;P-strategy-related log keywords (for `grep` troubleshooting):&quot;\">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINERU&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`mineru`: detects headings by an item's `text_level &gt; 0` or `label` being `title` / `section_header`, using a heading_stack to maintain the parent chain.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">75.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-631139d87a5854bded80f7eef24fed9c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINERU&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy is valid for the structured output of any parser that can produce a `.blocks.jsonl` sidecar, such as `native` / `mineru` / `docling`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINERU&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The parser guarantees &quot;the body under one heading as one basic block&quot; (native via heading-driven structural splitting, mineru / docling via their respective IR builders), with no token-threshold splitting at parse time. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINERU&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`# docx uses native, pdf uses mineru, other supported formats use docling, all with P; unsupported formats fall back to legacy-R`&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a157ba8bb77c0492f14d1d2322564184</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROCESSING LOOP&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Uploads and text inserts can be accepted while the processing loop is busy; the running loop is nudged to pick up the new pending work. Destructive jobs such as document clear/delete and the classification phase of `/documents/scan` still reject concurrent enqueues to protect storage consistency.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HEADING LEVELS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy utilizes heading levels and `parent_headings` to maintain hierarchy information, which is often underused by other methods.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HEADING LEVELS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy prevents long-block re-splitting by considering table-row boundaries and heading levels, maintaining the structure of the document.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARAGRAPHS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Internally the implementation also uses temporary fields like `paragraphs`, `content`, `table_chunk_role`, `blockids` to aid splitting and merging, but they do **not** enter the final output under those names (`blockids` is materialized as `sidecar` after conversion). &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FILE_PATH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The code snippet with `insert_text` demonstrates the use of a `file_path` parameter, suggesting that the system is designed to work with files or file paths.">
  <data key="d5">75.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6c748ee608ace11e7d348ea0448f352</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOURCE FILE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **The source file is not archived**: the source file stays at its original location (the production path moves the source file to `&lt;INPUT_DIR&gt;/__parsed__/&gt;`);&quot;">
