<edge source="&quot;MULTIMODAL ANALYSIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;v1.5 introduces a staged document pipeline. Files first go through a content extraction engine, optional multimodal analysis, text chunking, and then entity/relation extraction unless the file disables knowledge graph construction.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MULTIMODAL ANALYSIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The v1.5.0rc2 release adds the new file-processing pipeline, parser routing, multimodal analysis, role-specific LLM/VLM configuration, JSON entity extraction, and several provider/storage changes.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8286dc1e92acbe46895a3e4b4adbe05d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MULTIMODAL ANALYSIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;VLM_PROCESS_ENABLE=true&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-724331b1e2f5105ca6162abeddd355d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLASSIFICATION PHASE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Uploads and text inserts can be accepted while the processing loop is busy; the running loop is nudged to pick up the new pending work. Destructive jobs such as document clear/delete and the classification phase of `/documents/scan` still reject concurrent enqueues to protect storage consistency.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84523726bee4688a44b0a4ac3253a74c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;JSONDOCSTATUSSTORAGE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here is how workspaces are implemented for different types of storage: for local file-based databases, data isolation is achieved through workspace subdirectories; for databases that store data in collections, it's done by adding a workspace prefix to the collection name; for Qdrant vector database, data isolation is achieved through payload-based partitioning (Qdrant's recommended multitenancy approach); for relational databases, data isolation is achieved by adding a `workspace` field to the tables for logical data separation; for graph databases, logical data isolation is achieved through labels; for OpenSearch, data isolation is achieved through index name prefixes.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINERU_LOCAL_ENDPOINT&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# raw directory is cleared → docling-serve is called again to download → sidecar regenerated&quot;">
