</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGN GOALS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy has design goals: Align chunk boundaries with the document's native semantic boundaries, Make each chunk understandable on its own at recall time, and Decompose this goal into concrete rules for three scenarios (tables, long blocks, fine-grained sections).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EFFECT&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Effect**: many 100–300 token fine-grained clauses are merged toward near `target_ideal` (chunks are no longer too short and semantically thin), while **never lumping together adjacent small blocks that belong to different topics / different parent sections** — curing both &quot;chunks too small&quot; and &quot;cross-topic pollution&quot;.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</edge>
