<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The LightRAG project includes a React-based WebUI frontend. This guide explains how frontend building works in different scenarios. It outlines key principles and installation scenarios for end users, contributors, and for testing package builds. It also describes how to create distribution packages and the automated release process through GitHub Actions. The guide provides a quick reference for different scenarios and instructions for Bun installation. The file structure of the project is outlined, and troubleshooting steps are provided for common issues with the installation and building process. The document ends with a summary indicating the completion of the guide. The guide emphasizes the importance of the frontend build process and its role in the project's functionality and distribution. It also highlights the use of Git and PyPI for version control and distribution, respectively. Additionally, it mentions the role of contributors in the development process and the need for a clean and efficient build process to ensure the project's quality and maintainability.&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRIBUTION PACKAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d00e4ce6ff0f87215af7eacdd73129</data>
