<edge source="&quot;RERANKER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;# SURROUNDING_TRAILING_MAX_TOKENS=2000&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0ff5c99c56fa54fe27e56cb06863931</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONGOVECTORDBSTORAGE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here is how workspaces are implemented for different types of storage: for local file-based databases, data isolation is achieved through workspace subdirectories; for databases that store data in collections, it's done by adding a workspace prefix to the collection name; for Qdrant vector database, data isolation is achieved through payload-based partitioning (Qdrant's recommended multitenancy approach); for relational databases, data isolation is achieved by adding a `workspace` field to the tables for logical data separation; for graph databases, logical data isolation is achieved through labels; for OpenSearch, data isolation is achieved through index name prefixes.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONGOVECTORDBSTORAGE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;MongoVectorDBStorage is used for vector storage in MongoDB.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STORAGE BACKENDS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG uses dynamic package installation (`pipmaster`) for optional features based on file types and configurations. In offline environments, these dynamic installations will fail. This guide shows you how to pre-install all necessary dependencies and cache files.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERACTIVE SETUP WIZARD&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Instead of editing `env.example` by hand, you can use the interactive setup wizard to generate a configured `.env` and, when needed, `docker-compose.final.yml`:">
  <data key="d5">155.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-021f97620f79cb0c99aad301145dfec1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKERDEPLOYMENT.MD&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You can get the official docker compose file from here: [docker-compose.yml](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/refs/heads/main/docker-compose.yml). For historical versions of LightRAG docker images, visit this link: [LightRAG Docker Images](https://github.com/HKUDS/LightRAG/pkgs/container/lightrag). For more details about docker deployment, please refer to [DockerDeployment.md](./DockerDeployment.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7149569405d52b329c2d9c690f051dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKERDEPLOYMENT.MD&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Looking for the basic single-instance Docker setup? See [DockerDeployment.md](./DockerDeployment.md). For frontend build mechanics in general, see [FrontendBuildGuide.md](./FrontendBuildGuide.md).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCKERDEPLOYMENT.MD&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The document provides additional resources for the reader, including [DockerDeployment.md](./DockerDeployment.md) for the basic single-instance Docker setup and [FrontendBuildGuide.md](./FrontendBuildGuide.md) for frontend build mechanics in general.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-900da8eeab3b8744fbf99eb48a223646</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENV-SECURITY-CHECK&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The setup wizards update configuration only; run `make env-security-check` separately to audit the current `.env` for security risks before deployment.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
