<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`MAX_PARALLEL_INSERT` controls how many files are processed in parallel. `MAX_ASYNC_LLM` (deprecated alias: `MAX_ASYNC`) controls concurrent LLM calls, including extraction, merging, query keyword generation, and final answer generation. Optional staged-pipeline variables such as `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_NATIVE`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_MINERU`, `MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_DOCLING`, and `MAX_PARALLEL_ANALYZE` can be used for parser-heavy deployments.&quot;" target="&quot;MAX_PARALLEL_PARSE_DOCLING&quot;">
