  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J_WORKSPACE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Storage-specific workspace environment variables override the common `WORKSPACE` variable: `REDIS_WORKSPACE`, `MILVUS_WORKSPACE`, `QDRANT_WORKSPACE`, `MONGODB_WORKSPACE`, `POSTGRES_WORKSPACE`, `NEO4J_WORKSPACE`, `OPENSEARCH_WORKSPACE`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-99142de25f745182f551fb22af5fa5ea</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To maintain compatibility with legacy data, the default workspace for PostgreSQL is 'default' and for Neo4j is 'base' when no workspace is configured.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG uses dynamic package installation (`pipmaster`) for optional features based on file types and configurations. In offline environments, these dynamic installations will fail. This guide shows you how to pre-install all necessary dependencies and cache files.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This text describes the use of Neo4j as a storage solution for the LightRAG project.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For high-performance graph database requirements, Neo4j is recommended over Apache AGE.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEO4J&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;non-graph storage is `default`; for PostgreSQL AGE graph storage is null; for Neo4j graph storage is `base`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-99142de25f745182f551fb22af5fa5ea</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEMGRAPH_WORKSPACE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all external storages, the system provides dedicated workspace environment variables to override the common 'WORKSPACE' environment variable configuration.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEMGRAPH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Memgraph is a high-performance, in-memory graph database compatible with the Neo4j Bolt protocol.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH_WORKSPACE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all external storages, the system provides dedicated workspace environment variables to override the common 'WORKSPACE' environment variable configuration.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH_WORKSPACE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Storage-specific workspace environment variables override the common `WORKSPACE` variable: `REDIS_WORKSPACE`, `MILVUS_WORKSPACE`, `QDRANT_WORKSPACE`, `MONGODB_WORKSPACE`, `POSTGRES_WORKSPACE`, `NEO4J_WORKSPACE`, `OPENSEARCH_WORKSPACE`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-99142de25f745182f551fb22af5fa5ea</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AZ LOGIN&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;az login:">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AZ LOGIN&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;You will also need to login with [az login](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/authenticate-azure-cli) and select the subscription with your endpoint.">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG uses dynamic package installation (`pipmaster`) for optional features based on file types and configurations. In offline environments, these dynamic installations will fail. This guide shows you how to pre-install all necessary dependencies and cache files.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-282ce1c61fc13efc3e86b9d5f4e51547</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Recommended Redis configuration:&lt;br&gt;```&lt;br&gt;save 900 1&lt;br&gt;save 300 10&lt;br&gt;save 60 1000&lt;br&gt;stop-writes-on-bgsave-error yes&lt;br&gt;maxmemory 4gb&lt;br&gt;maxmemory-policy noeviction&lt;br&gt;maxclients 500&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When the interactive setup manages a local Redis container, it stages a user-editable config at `./data/config/redis.conf` and mounts it into the container. Setup preserves that file on reruns so local Redis tuning can be adjusted without losing manual edits.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDIS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Redis is supported as a KV storage for LightRAG.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a95e21c3d4aa9dd77f673c11a10f2f2a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Here is how workspaces are implemented for different types of storage: local file-based databases, databases storing data in collections, Qdrant vector database, relational databases, graph databases, and OpenSearch.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1417f2fecf74afcbf4d69be846fd679a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When the interactive setup manages a local Redis container, it stages a user-editable config at `./data/config/redis.conf` and mounts it into the container. Setup preserves that file on reruns so local Redis tuning can be adjusted without losing manual edits.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Requirements**: OpenSearch 3.x or higher with k-NN plugin enabled.">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Install with Docker (without plugins):&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;docker run -d -p 9200:9200 -e \&quot;discovery.type=single-node\&quot; \n  -e \&quot;OPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=&lt;custom-admin-password&gt;\&quot; \n  opensearchproject/opensearch:latest&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Install with Docker Compose (Recommended, with plugins):&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opensearch-project/opensearch-build/main/docker/release/dockercomposefiles/docker-compose-3.x.yml\nOPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=&lt;custom-admin-password&gt; docker-compose -f docker-compose-3.x.yml up -d&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Configuration** (see `env.example` for full list):&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;export OPENSEARCH_HOSTS=localhost:9200\nexport OPENSEARCH_USER=admin\nexport OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD=&lt;custom-admin-password&gt;\nexport OPENSEARCH_USE_SSL=true\nexport OPENSEARCH_VERIFY_CERTS=false&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Graph Traversal**: When the OpenSearch SQL plugin with PPL support is available, graph queries use server-side BFS via the `graphlookup` command for optimal performance. Otherwise, it falls back to client-side batched BFS. Auto-detected at startup, or force via `OPENSEARCH_USE_PPL_GRAPHLOOKUP=true|false`. &quot;">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**Integration Testing**:&lt;br&gt;1. Start OpenSearch using Docker Compose:&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;OPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=&lt;custom-admin-password&gt; docker-compose -f docker-compose-3.x.yml up -d&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;2. Verify the cluster is running:&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;curl -sk -u admin:&lt;custom-admin-password&gt; https://localhost:9200&lt;br&gt;curl -sk -u admin:&lt;custom-admin-password&gt; https://localhost:9200/_cat/plugins?v&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01ff0c3484b2ce9e7b7c81987558e93</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPENSEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;3. Run unit tests (no OpenSearch required — uses mocks):&lt;br&gt;```bash&lt;br&gt;python -m pytest tests/kg/opensearch_impl/test_opensearch_storage.py -v&lt;br&gt;```">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
