</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NGINX&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The text describes the configuration and deployment of a web application using Nginx and Kubernetes Ingress. It also discusses local development with a Vite server and the handling of API prefixes and environment variables.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8695c3b8cfc1cc28382a176ac4d0e7ba</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NGINX&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**A. Local backend with `LIGHTRAG_API_PREFIX=/site01`** (no nginx anywhere) — the simplest setup, two processes on your laptop. Vite's proxy itself plays the role of the reverse proxy.">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f50a1a569536dcf7b4109c246e92d1a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NGINX&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;**B. Real (remote) backend reached through its production nginx** — useful when the actual backend has data / configs that are painful to reproduce locally. nginx already strips `/site01/` before forwarding to the backend; the dev frontend benefits without changing anything in production.">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f50a1a569536dcf7b4109c246e92d1a</data>
</edge>
