</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OVERLY LONG OR ENDLESS LOOP OUTPUTS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Set the max_tokens to **prevent excessively long or endless output loop** during the entity relationship extraction phase for Large Language Model (LLM) responses. The purpose of setting max_tokens parameter is to truncate LLM output before timeouts occur, thereby preventing document extraction failures. This addresses issues where certain text blocks (e.g., tables or citations) containing numerous entities and relationships can lead to overly long or even endless loop outputs from LLMs. This setting is particularly crucial for locally deployed, smaller-parameter models:">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a5f058377b951c53da07f784f3944ef</data>
</edge>
