</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`table_file` / `equation_file` / `drawing_file` | `bool` | Whether the corresponding sidecar files exist (when true, the corresponding file must exist) &quot;" target="&quot;TABLE_FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`table_file` / `equation_file` / `drawing_file` | `bool` | Whether the corresponding sidecar files exist (when true, the corresponding file must exist) &quot;" target="&quot;EQUATION_FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`table_file` / `equation_file` / `drawing_file` | `bool` | Whether the corresponding sidecar files exist (when true, the corresponding file must exist) &quot;" target="&quot;DRAWING_FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Therefore, concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks must form the complete document content — no content missing, no content overlapping. &quot;" target="&quot;COMPLETE DOCUMENT CONTENT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">140.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each JSON / JSONL file in that directory is collectively called a **sidecar** file.&quot;" target="&quot;SIDECAR FILE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Every recognized heading starts its own block: if a heading is immediately followed by body text, that body is merged into the same block (content = markdown-rendered heading line + body); if a heading has no following body (e.g., it is immediately followed by a heading at the next level), it still becomes a standalone block whose content is just the markdown-rendered heading line. This ensures that concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks still reconstructs the complete original text without overlap. &quot;" target="&quot;RECOGNIZED HEADING&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Every recognized heading starts its own block: if a heading is immediately followed by body text, that body is merged into the same block (content = markdown-rendered heading line + body); if a heading has no following body (e.g., it is immediately followed by a heading at the next level), it still becomes a standalone block whose content is just the markdown-rendered heading line. This ensures that concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks still reconstructs the complete original text without overlap. &quot;" target="&quot;BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Every recognized heading starts its own block: if a heading is immediately followed by body text, that body is merged into the same block (content = markdown-rendered heading line + body); if a heading has no following body (e.g., it is immediately followed by a heading at the next level), it still becomes a standalone block whose content is just the markdown-rendered heading line. This ensures that concatenating the `content` fields of all blocks still reconstructs the complete original text without overlap. &quot;" target="&quot;MARKDOWN-RENDERED HEADING LINE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `self_ref` field is optional; object reference from the original parsing engine output (e.g., Docling JSON Pointer `#/texts/15`, or MinerU `content_list.json#/45`), used to look up the original artifact when tracing back &quot;" target="&quot;SELF_REF FIELD&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`asset_dir` | `bool` | Whether the `blocks.assets` asset directory exists &quot;" target="&quot;ASSET_DIR&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;" target="&quot;HEADING&quot;">
  <data key="d5">120.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;" target="&quot;BLOCKID&quot;">
  <data key="d5">140.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;blockid computation: `md5(doc_id + &quot;:&quot; + block_index + &quot;:&quot; + heading + &quot;:&quot; + content)` &quot;" target="&quot;BLOCK_INDEX&quot;">
  <data key="d5">120.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Sidecars are the only reliable source of truth for the subsequent pipeline (multimodal analysis → multimodal chunk construction → entity extraction → cache cleanup on document deletion).&quot;" target="&quot;SIDECAR&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;8. positions&quot;" target="&quot;BLOCKID&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0457e4c69abfc4709a265a8f9f349adb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The `llm_analyze_result` field is the canonicalized LaTeX equation output by the LLM (outer `$ / \[ \] / equation` environment, Unicode converted to LaTeX, no leading/trailing `$` delimiters); this is the string actually used by the downstream multimodal chunk &quot;" target="&quot;LLM_ANALYZE_RESULT FIELD&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The directory stores original image assets.&quot;" target="&quot;ORIGINAL IMAGE ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;`split_option` | `object` | Optional. Free-form metadata the parsing engine records about itself (e.g. `engine_version`, engine-specific extras). Omitted entirely when the engine recorded nothing (the common native/markdown case). Chunking is NOT performed at the parse stage — it is the downstream chunker's responsibility — so this field never carries chunking parameters. &quot;" target="&quot;SPLIT_OPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks produced by chunking strategies record the blockid for tracing the chunk back to its location in the sidecar. &quot;" target="&quot;CHUNK&quot;">
  <data key="d5">310.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks produced by chunking strategies record the blockid for tracing the chunk back to its location in the sidecar. &quot;" target="&quot;SIDECAR&quot;">
  <data key="d5">300.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a79bee86d871fa85d9e457899f3ff418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Chunks produced by chunking strategies record the blockid for tracing the chunk back to its location in the sidecar. &quot;" target="&quot;BLOCKID&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1394c48f6affe43ef3462e870a7090e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The sidecar format is LightRAG's built-in universal file interchange format; new multimodal content extraction engines must follow this format.&quot;" target="&quot;MULTIMODAL CONTENT EXTRACTION ENGINES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The sidecar format is LightRAG's built-in universal file interchange format; new multimodal content extraction engines must follow this format.&quot;" target="&quot;SIDECAR FORMAT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">180.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33d111aa7def535c2ef43b93f5b747d7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The goal is to avoid injecting too much noise into the extraction results.&quot;" target="&quot;GOAL&quot;">
  <data key="d5">140.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-473420f06d48aa17cce8e74c7be782ac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Original image files are extracted from the document.&quot;" target="&quot;ORIGINAL IMAGE FILES&quot;">
