</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VERSION&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once a `BaseParser` subclass is implemented, the engine needs to be registered to be recognized and used by the LightRAG system. This registration is done through a `ParserSpec` object, which contains metadata about the engine such as its name, version, and supported file types. The entry point for automatic discovery of these `ParserSpec` objects is the `lightrag.parsers` directory, where third-party engines can provide their own modules that are discovered at runtime by LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SIDECAR&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Note: this is the equivalent replacement for the &quot;rebuild sidecar from an existing raw directory&quot; scenario that used to live in the legacy `python -m lightrag.parser.external.docling` debug entry point — just place the raw directory at the agreed location (`&lt;sidecar_parent&gt;/&lt;source&gt;.docling_raw/`) to trigger the cache-hit branch.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f0e2827f0656f23647a5ad5b252099d6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TABLE_HEADER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **Header source**: at parse time each table's &quot;cross-page repeating header&quot; is written into the sibling `.tables.json` (entry field `table_header`; **only tables that genuinely carry a repeating header have this field**). **The field is stored in the table's own format so merged-cell semantics survive end-to-end**: a `format=&quot;json&quot;` table stores it as a JSON 2-D array string (e.g. `[[&quot;H1&quot;,&quot;H2&quot;]]`), a `format=&quot;html&quot;` table stores it as the raw `&lt;thead&gt;…&lt;/thead&gt;` fragment (preserving `rowspan` / `colspan`). P traces back to the matching table entry via the `id` preserved on the to-be-split `&lt;table&gt;` tag and takes its `table_header`.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">7.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIELDS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following entity types are provided. The fields here represent the fields that are text-embedded by default.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- **Same-level merging (Phase A / tail absorption)**: the two blocks' `parent_headings` must be **exactly equal** (true siblings). Blocks with the same `level` but different parent chains (e.g. `2.4.1` and `2.5.1`) may not merge.">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Check whether adjacent clauses have consistent `parent_headings`: the parent-heading-path consistency constraint blocks cross-topic merging.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">70.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1f6e0884f12ea67e008e26e0216f0a4e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy uses heading outline level and `parent_headings` + table-row boundaries + anchors + hierarchy-aware merging for chunking.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy utilizes heading levels and `parent_headings` to maintain hierarchy information, which is often underused by other methods.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The P strategy uses `parent_headings` to preserve the hierarchical structure of the document, ensuring that the relationships between headings and subheadings are maintained during chunking.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c83519f50b4e9e94ec0fa78d3401a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT_HEADINGS&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Each content line typically contains: &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f62767a155c127d2e19bb2a763d570c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;for exact path)">
