<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;1. **Header source**: at parse time each table's &quot;cross-page repeating header&quot; is written into the sibling `.tables.json` (entry field `table_header`; **only tables that genuinely carry a repeating header have this field**). **The field is stored in the table's own format so merged-cell semantics survive end-to-end**: a `format=&quot;json&quot;` table stores it as a JSON 2-D array string (e.g. `[[&quot;H1&quot;,&quot;H2&quot;]]`), a `format=&quot;html&quot;` table stores it as the raw `&lt;thead&gt;…&lt;/thead&gt;` fragment (preserving `rowspan` / `colspan`). P traces back to the matching table entry via the `id` preserved on the to-be-split `&lt;table&gt;` tag and takes its `table_header`.&quot;" target="&quot;TABLE_CHUNK_ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a78f97cbe007105c80acba2db42453d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;A table of unrecognized format can only go through character splitting and cannot start TableRowSplit's role mechanism.&quot;" target="&quot;UNRECOGNIZED FORMAT&quot;">
