<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If an **ordinary (`none`)** block that has reached `target_ideal` is immediately followed by a run of same-level small blocks whose total token count is below `small_tail_threshold` and whose merged real token count does not exceed `target_max`, then **absorb that run in one shot**. Stop on encountering **any split-table slice** (`first` / `middle` / `last`), or when the parent-heading path diverges; a split-table slice never initiates tail absorption either." target="&quot;ORDINARY (`NONE`) BLOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If an **ordinary (`none`)** block that has reached `target_ideal` is immediately followed by a run of same-level small blocks whose total token count is below `small_tail_threshold` and whose merged real token count does not exceed `target_max`, then **absorb that run in one shot**. Stop on encountering **any split-table slice** (`first` / `middle` / `last`), or when the parent-heading path diverges; a split-table slice never initiates tail absorption either." target="&quot;TOTAL TOKEN COUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If an **ordinary (`none`)** block that has reached `target_ideal` is immediately followed by a run of same-level small blocks whose total token count is below `small_tail_threshold` and whose merged real token count does not exceed `target_max`, then **absorb that run in one shot**. Stop on encountering **any split-table slice** (`first` / `middle` / `last`), or when the parent-heading path diverges; a split-table slice never initiates tail absorption either." target="&quot;SAME-LEVEL SMALL BLOCKS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d5becb2ed078b428ad8287c1f5c91acf</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;If an **ordinary (`none`)** block that has reached `target_ideal` is immediately followed by a run of same-level small blocks whose total token count is below `small_tail_threshold` and whose merged real token count does not exceed `target_max`, then **absorb that run in one shot**. Stop on encountering **any split-table slice** (`first` / `middle` / `last`), or when the parent-heading path diverges; a split-table slice never initiates tail absorption either." target="&quot;MERGED REAL TOKEN COUNT&quot;">
