</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NAME&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Once a `BaseParser` subclass is implemented, the engine needs to be registered to be recognized and used by the LightRAG system. This registration is done through a `ParserSpec` object, which contains metadata about the engine such as its name, version, and supported file types. The entry point for automatic discovery of these `ParserSpec` objects is the `lightrag.parsers` directory, where third-party engines can provide their own modules that are discovered at runtime by LightRAG.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
