</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG's parsing layer dispatches all parsing engines through a unified `BaseParser` contract plus the central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`). Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) and third-party engines use the exact same dispatch path: both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;" target="&quot;BUILT-IN ENGINES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">80.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG's parsing layer dispatches all parsing engines through a unified `BaseParser` contract plus the central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`). Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) and third-party engines use the exact same dispatch path: both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;" target="&quot;LIGHTRAG'S PARSING LAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG's parsing layer dispatches all parsing engines through a unified `BaseParser` contract plus the central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`). Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) and third-party engines use the exact same dispatch path: both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;" target="&quot;BASEPARSER&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;LightRAG's parsing layer dispatches all parsing engines through a unified `BaseParser` contract plus the central engine registry (`lightrag/parser/registry.py`). Built-in engines (`native` / `legacy` / `mineru` / `docling`) and third-party engines use the exact same dispatch path: both pipeline workers and the debug CLI drive parsing through `get_parser(engine).parse(ParseContext(...))`, with **no special cases for built-in engines**. Therefore, a third-party package only needs to do two things:&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD-PARTY ENGINES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-befc9ee33b58f79fec1dbee2eaeae5f2</data>
</edge>
