</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The GraphRAG library was designed with LLM interactions in mind, and a common setback when working with LLM APIs is various errors due to network latency, throttling, etc.." target="&quot;LLM APIS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The GraphRAG library was designed with LLM interactions in mind, and a common setback when working with LLM APIs is various errors due to network latency, throttling, etc.." target="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;All of these factories allow you to register an impl using any string name you would like, even overriding built-in ones directly." target="&quot;FACTORIES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;When completion requests are made using the same input set (prompt and tuning parameters), we return a cached result if one exists." target="&quot;COMPLETION REQUESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cache layer is part of the GraphRAG library." target="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Custom implementations can be registered using factories." target="&quot;FACTORIES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The outputs of the indexing engine are aligned to a knowledge model called the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_.&quot;" target="&quot;GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The cache layer handles errors from LLM interactions." target="&quot;ERRORS FROM LLM INTERACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Custom implementations can override built-in ones." target="&quot;CUSTOM IMPLEMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Below is the core GraphRAG indexing pipeline. Individual workflows are described in detail in the [dataflow](./default_dataflow.md) page.&quot;" target="&quot;GRAPHRAG INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The indexing engine operates in the Default Configuration Mode.&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT CONFIGURATION MODE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This allows our indexer to be more resilient to network issues, to act idempotently, and to provide a more efficient end-user experience." target="&quot;INDEXER&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In order to support the GraphRAG system, the outputs of the indexing engine (in the Default Configuration Mode) are aligned to a knowledge model we call the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_.&quot;" target="&quot;GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Cached results are used for repeated inputs." target="&quot;REPEATED INPUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_ abstracts the data storage technology." target="&quot;_GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The indexing pipeline consists of core workflows described in the dataflow page.&quot;" target="&quot;INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Several subsystems within GraphRAG use a factory pattern to register and retrieve provider implementations." target="&quot;FACTORY PATTERN&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Custom provider implementations can be registered in the factories." target="&quot;CUSTOM PROVIDER IMPLEMENTATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The model provides a common interface for the GraphRAG system." target="&quot;GRAPHRAG SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The library is designed for interactions with LLM APIs, which can face errors due to network issues." target="&quot;LLM APIS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a691fd7a7b44653de8f16248cba628</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG KNOWLEDGE MODEL&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Let's take a look at how the default-configuration workflow transforms text documents into the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_. This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG SYSTEM&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The default prompts are the simplest way to get started with the GraphRAG system. It is designed to work out-of-the-box with minimal configuration.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37ac2e652be419ab7d9491e584ea178d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This page documents the command-line interface of the graphrag library.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The term 'CLI Reference' suggests that the text is a reference guide for the command-line interface of the graphrag library.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG LIBRARY&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The ':module: graphrag.cli.main' indicates that there is a specific module within the graphrag library that is being referenced.">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bbc9cbe94e549538ada5a47127f63ede</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;GraphRAG is a platform for our research into RAG indexing methods that produce optimal context window content for language models. We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph that our memory model is based upon. We may introduce additional indexing methods from time to time. This page documents those options.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEXING PIPELINE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;After running the indexing pipeline over your data, there will be an output folder (defined by the `storage.base_dir` setting).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-753b54f11987ea184b7a7af0bb9e15ee</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEXER&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For a deeper dive into the main sub-systems, please visit the docpages for the [Indexer](index/overview.md) and [Query](query/overview.md) packages.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LANGUAGE MODEL&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This page documents those options.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LANGUAGE MODEL&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph that our memory model is based upon. We may introduce additional indexing methods from time to time. This page documents those options.&quot;">
