  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;⚠️ GraphRAG can consume a lot of LLM resources! We strongly recommend starting with the tutorial dataset here until you understand how the system works, and consider experimenting with fast/inexpensive models first before committing to a big indexing job.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following is a simple end-to-end example for using GraphRAG on the command line after installing from [pypi](https://pypi.org/project/graphrag/).&quot;">
  <data key="d5">175.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-640e5c41fd121c0003f70f439e8b3b48</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Welcome to GraphRAG&quot;">
  <data key="d5">95.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Using _GraphRAG_ with your data out of the box may not yield the best possible results. We strongly recommend to fine-tune your prompts following the [Prompt Tuning Guide](prompt_tuning/overview.md) in our documentation.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;GraphRAG supports several input formats to simplify ingesting your data. The mechanics and features available for input files and text chunking are discussed here.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-813bfd09c5663aba506972a834914fb8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;GraphRAG is a platform for our research into RAG indexing methods that produce optimal context window content for language models. We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph that our memory model is based upon. We may introduce additional indexing methods from time to time. This page documents those options.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRAPHRAG&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following step-by-step guide walks through the process to visualize a knowledge graph after it's been constructed by graphrag. Note that some of the settings recommended below are based on our own experience of what works well. Feel free to change and explore other settings for a better visualization experience!&quot;">
  <data key="d5">160.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-753b54f11987ea184b7a7af0bb9e15ee</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRIFT SEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The approach described here will be to run a custom GraphRAG workflow pipeline that assumes the text chunking, entity extraction, and relationship extraction has already occurred.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04e9a4e23946a2a3618f112c8e332247</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRIFT SEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- [_DRIFT Search_](query/drift_search.md) for reasoning about specific entities by fanning-out to their neighbors and associated concepts, but with the added context of community information.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESEARCH&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;GraphRAG builds upon our prior [research](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/worklab/patterns-hidden-inside-the-org-chart) and [tooling](https://github.com/graspologic-org/graspologic) using graph machine learning. The basic steps of the GraphRAG process are as follows:&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71f126a1f713fce89f72bd739d4c81eb</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BLOG POST&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This page documents those options.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;See the full entities [table schema](./outputs.md#entities). For graph summarization purposes, you only need id, title, description, and the list of text_unit_ids." target="&quot;ENTITIES TABLE SCHEMA&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04e9a4e23946a2a3618f112c8e332247</data>
</edge>
