</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;To cover the basic use cases for GraphRAG query, you should have two or three tables derived from your data: - entities.parquet - this is the list of entities found in the dataset, which are the nodes of the graph. - relationships.parquet - this is the list of relationships found in the dataset, which are the edges of the graph. - text_units.parquet - this is the source text chunks the graph was extracted from. This is optional depending on the query method you intend to use (described later).&quot;" target="&quot;TEXT_UNITS.PARQUET&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04e9a4e23946a2a3618f112c8e332247</data>
</edge>
