<edge source="&quot;PAGE&quot;" target="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;We have a standard indexing pipeline that uses a language model to extract the graph that our memory model is based upon. We may introduce additional indexing methods from time to time. This page documents those options.&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b98dce4eef8d1a08af62b430c1fe835e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following entity types are provided. The fields here represent the fields that are text-embedded by default.&quot;" target="&quot;ENTITY TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The following entity types are provided. The fields here represent the fields that are text-embedded by default.&quot;" target="&quot;TEXT-EMBEDDED&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Now that we have a usable graph of entities and relationships, we want to understand their community structure. These give us explicit ways of understanding the organization of our graph.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY STRUCTURE &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Now that we have a usable graph of entities and relationships, we want to understand their community structure. These give us explicit ways of understanding the organization of our graph.&quot;" target="&quot;ORGANIZATION &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm is a recursive community-clustering algorithm that is used to generate a hierarchy of communities.&quot;" target="&quot;HIERARCHICAL LEIDEN ALGORITHM &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm is a recursive community-clustering algorithm that is used to generate a hierarchy of communities.&quot;" target="&quot;HIERARCHY &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm is a recursive community-clustering algorithm that is used to generate a hierarchy of communities.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY-CLUSTERING &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Note: if you are using the [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option, entity and relationship extraction will be performed using NLP to conserve LLM resources, and claim extraction will always be skipped.&quot;" target="&quot;LLM &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Note: if you are using the [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option, entity and relationship extraction will be performed using NLP to conserve LLM resources, and claim extraction will always be skipped.&quot;" target="&quot;FASTGRAPHRAG &quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Note: if you are using the [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option, entity and relationship extraction will be performed using NLP to conserve LLM resources, and claim extraction will always be skipped.&quot;" target="&quot;NLP &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Community Report` - The contents of each community are summarized into a generated report, useful for human reading and downstream search.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Community Report` - The contents of each community are summarized into a generated report, useful for human reading and downstream search.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At this point, some bookkeeping work is performed and we export the **Community Reports** tables.&quot;" target="&quot;BOOKKEEPING &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;At this point, some bookkeeping work is performed and we export the **Community Reports** tables.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY REPORTS &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Document` - An input document into the system. These either represent individual rows in a CSV or individual .txt files.&quot;" target="&quot;TXT FILES&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;- `Document` - An input document into the system. These either represent individual rows in a CSV or individual .txt files.&quot;" target="&quot;CSV&quot;">
  <data key="d5">170.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, we generate a hierarchy of entity communities using the Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm. This method will apply a recursive community-clustering to our graph until we reach a community-size threshold. This will allow us to understand the community structure of our graph and provide a way to navigate and summarize the graph at different levels of granularity.&quot;" target="&quot;HIERARCHICAL LEIDEN ALGORITHM &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, we generate a hierarchy of entity communities using the Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm. This method will apply a recursive community-clustering to our graph until we reach a community-size threshold. This will allow us to understand the community structure of our graph and provide a way to navigate and summarize the graph at different levels of granularity.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY-CLUSTERING &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;In this step, we generate a hierarchy of entity communities using the Hierarchical Leiden Algorithm. This method will apply a recursive community-clustering to our graph until we reach a community-size threshold. This will allow us to understand the community structure of our graph and provide a way to navigate and summarize the graph at different levels of granularity.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY-SIZE THRESHOLD &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The final step in the process is the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables, which contain the results of the graph augmentation.&quot;" target="&quot;GRAPH AUGMENTATION &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The final step in the process is the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables, which contain the results of the graph augmentation.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITIES &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The final step in the process is the export of the Entities, Relationships, and Communities tables, which contain the results of the graph augmentation.&quot;" target="&quot;RELATIONSHIPS &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;Let's take a look at how the default-configuration workflow transforms text documents into the _GraphRAG Knowledge Model_. This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation.&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT-CONFIGURATION WORKFLOW&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;" target="&quot;ENTITY DESCRIPTIONS &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;" target="&quot;TEXT UNIT TEXT &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY REPORT TEXT &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;" target="&quot;TEXT EMBEDDINGS &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;For all artifacts that require downstream vector search, we generate text embeddings as a final step. These embeddings are written directly to a configured vector store. By default we embed entity descriptions, text unit text, and community report text.&quot;" target="&quot;VECTOR STORE &quot;">
