<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;This page gives a general overview of the major steps in this process. To fully configure this workflow, check out the [configuration](../config/overview.md) documentation.&quot;" target="&quot;THIS PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e8c003efcd580037bb1cdeb5a33b78f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option is a tool that allows for entity and relationship extraction, as well as claim extraction, to conserve LLM resources. This option is particularly useful when working with large datasets where efficient processing is required.&quot;" target="&quot;LLM &quot;">
  <data key="d5">90.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&lt;hyperedge&gt;&quot;The [FastGraphRAG](https://microsoft.github.io/graphrag/index/methods/#fastgraphrag) option is a tool that allows for entity and relationship extraction, as well as claim extraction, to conserve LLM resources. This option is particularly useful when working with large datasets where efficient processing is required.&quot;" target="&quot;FASTGRAPHRAG &quot;">
  <data key="d5">85.0</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1510fdc0a4611e7ac84d55abc79e6e54</data>
</edge>
